20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Best At: </b>7 (Grappling, Infection, Sneaking)<br /> <b>Worst At: </b>1 (understanding human emotions and logic)<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Grow strong and infect new hosts<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 3<br /> <b>Initiative: </b>7<br /> <b>Defense: </b>3<br /> <b>Speed: </b>8 [Glide 16]<br /> <b>Bane: </b>Fire<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Contagious*, Drain Life*, Jump Scare, Madness and Terror, Skin Taker<br /> <br /> <b><i>Contagious:</i> </b>The horror carries a virulent disease that turns the infected into a creature of the same (or similar) type as the Contagious Horror. To infect a target, the horror must typically injure the victim (a bite or claw is most common, but other methods can be defined depending on the horror) and inflict one level of lethal damage. The victim must make a reflexive Stamina +Resolve roll (with a penalty equal to the Horrors Potency (maximum 5))<br /> Success means that the victim doesn't contract the contagion.an exceptional success renders them immune to further uses of this Dread Power from that particular creature. If the roll fails, then the victim gains the Sick (grave) tilt and becomes a Horror themselves after (9-Potency) hours. At the Storytellers discretion, certain supernatural creatures may be immune to this Dread Power.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Drain Life:</i> </b>With a touch, the Horror can extract the life essence from a living creature. Whenever the Horror inflicts damage in a grapple, it regains 1 point of Willpower per point of damage inflicted and heals one point of Lethal or two points of Bashing Damage. Every 5 points of damage inflicted can heal a level of Aggravated Damage. If the Horror is using this ability against a supernatural creature, it loses points from its fuel trait (Essence, Mana, Vitae, etc.) instead.</div></div> </div> </div></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Can you make a greater Horror like this based on The Thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T06:49:25-07:00","id":1120777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1120742#post1120742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you make a greater Horror like this based on The Thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. Give it the Skin-Thief merit from Dark Eras: Beneath the Skin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T10:36:44-07:00","id":1120890,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Hag</b></span><br /> A poor defenseless little old lady, lives like a shut-in. The children of the neighborhood are frightened of her, saying she's a witch and that she eats children. No children are missing of course, and she's had to call the police several times because of the harassment she's received.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Best At: </b>10 (Cooking and baking; Seeming frail, old and helpless; Intimidating and manhandling children)<br /> <b>Worst At:</b> 2 (Escaping from within appliances, Outsmarting children)<br /> <b>All Other Pools:</b> 5<br /> <b>Aspiration: </b>Avoid paying the price for her child-devouring appetite, Maintain friendships with those that understand the plight of being a monster<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene: </b>6<br /> <b>Health: </b>12<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 15<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Being baked/roasted in an oven, Going more than a month without eating baked goods magically made from children<br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b><i>Immortal </i>(Resurrection Clause: A child being baked in an oven by someone chanting the hag's name), <i>Miracle</i> (Always involves baking, and requires being next to an oven to use), <i>Homeground </i>(Kitchens but not within Appliances), <i>Hunter's Senses </i>(Children), <i>Know Soul</i>, <i>Maze</i> (Works by making every passage in the building lead to the Kitchen), <i>Numen-Omen Trance</i><br /> <br /> Hags prefer a diet of baked goods made from abandoned bad children whom no one will miss. This is especially true in the modern age of Amber Alerts and ubiquitous fear of harm coming to children. One thing a hag knows though is that all children are not made equal, and there are some children people expect (and secretly hope) to go missing, and those are the types of children that feed hags in the modern day.<br /> <br /> How do the hags eat the children? The begging screams of those children in the oven pleading for the pain to stop results in the hag killing the child by using their wish to miraculously transforming the child into dough. Going a month without each such food to eat causes the hag to shrivel away to a dried husk which then crumble into a pile of dust in mere moments and is something all hags fear. Much of a hag's power come from being within close proximity of their other weakness, the oven. These ironies are not lost on hags which frequently have survived for centuries, and have a collection of lore and secrets most occult scholars would give an eye for. Hags, while terrible, have found allies among the more monstrous denizens lurking through the world, and hags which are resurrected are known to be very grateful in granting a baked miracle for the one that resurrected them.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-26-2017, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T21:19:39-07:00","id":1122207,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Thing, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/87831-the-thing-from-another-world\"><b>this thread</b></a> has traits for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T16:36:20-07:00","id":1124076,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: The Thing </b><br /> <br /> the Thing is one of my favorite movie monsters, and the interpretation set up by @ClaireRedfield is hard to beat!<br /> <br /> My own version of a similar concept was the Horror called &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=856916#post856916\">Proteus</a>&quot;, which I have written up a few pages up thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 08-02-2017, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T18:35:58-07:00","id":1124114,"title":"","content":"Have you ever created any mad science Horrors besides the Hideous Mind and Proteus? I was thinking of creating a malfunctioning but hopeful super soldier who struggles with the conflict between his programming to be an efficient killing machine and his natural compassion. But I need a Dread Power that works like the Biomechanical Nightmare from Hunter Mortal Remains, but more 2ed style. Can you please help me with that, Reighnhell?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Could you also help me create an Electricity Elemental Dread Power?<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: Also, I suggest adding a way to undo the permanent effect of Baleful Metamorphosis, kinda like how your Fabricate usually comes with a flaw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-02-2017, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T17:26:06-07:00","id":1127840,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Biomechanical Nightmare</b><br /> <br /> I read over this power - each dot grants a discrete effect. When you think about it, thats the way the current Horror rules operate, with each Dread Power selection considered a &quot;Dot&quot;. For this we wouldn't really need to convert, just select the powers you want him to have as per the Horror Rules, and flavor appropriately. Alternatively, you could create him using the &quot;Lost Boy&quot; template from Hurt Locker.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Electricity Elemental</b><br /> <br /> I went over the various Elemental Form Dread Powers, and came up with something inline with how those power were written.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Lightning Elemental</b><br /> The creature\u2019s body is comprised of living lightning, or perhaps it's body cascading arcs of electric power. Anyone that makes physical contact with the creature suffers 6 bashing damage per turn of contact.The creature is immune to damage from electricity.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Re: Baleful Metamorphosis </b><br /> <br /> Good call - I have updated the Dread Power up thread with an &quot;Resolution Clause.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T18:05:08-07:00","id":1127863,"title":"","content":"Nice work! I would add that Lightning Elemental lets you travel through circuitry and such at increased Speed.<br /> <br /> Also, what do you think of this Dread Power I wrote?<br /> <br /> <b>Mad Science:</b> The Horror must have a medium or tools upon which to work in order to use this Dread Power (represented by Resources, Staff, Retainer or a similar Merit). It then rolls an appropriate dice pool to create a piece of Equipment containing a Dread Power as an extended action requiring [the total dot rating of Dread Powers invested into the Equipment x 5] in Successes, with each roll taking 30 minutes. This requires 1 Willpower point, but spending 3 Willpower points makes each roll take one turn. Spending 2 extra Willpower points makes the Equipment permanent (it lasts for one scene otherwise). The Horror need not possess the Dread Powers built into the Equipment: it is considered to have a pool of additional floating Dread Power dots equal to its highest Mental Attribute + Potency, which it can only use via Mad Science. Once per chapter, the Horror may spend 1 Willpower point to redistribute the Dread Power dots it can build via Mad Science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T18:36:19-07:00","id":1127875,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Lightning Elemental</b><br /> <br /> I modeled this power after the Air, Earth, Fire, and Water Elemental Dread Powers from Werewolf:the Forsaken 2nd Edition. these powers are either defensive (Earth, Fire), Offensive (Fire), or Movement (Air and Water). Currently I have it so that Lightning elemental is about on par with Fire Elemental power-wise. Adding a movement mode with be a bit too powerful (lets not forget, by Horror rules, you can make the creature as swift as you see fit with no power needed). I would set up the ability to travel through a medium as a separate power.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Transmit</b><br /> The Horror is capable of transmitting itself though space via a specific medium (such as mirrors, doorways, electrical wiring, etc) which is chosen when this Dread Power is selected. By stepping into their chosen medium (or changing into a form that can travel through the medium), the creature will exit 1 minute later from another location where the medium is present, within a range of (Potecy x 5) miles.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Re: Mad Science</b><br /> <br /> There is a lot going on here. The first thing I notice it would be very easy for a creature with this ability to effectively have access to a vast number of dread powers. I would curb this potential, remember that these are ease- of - use abilities to make running the game easier. Stacking powers onto a Horror is often more trouble (and more work for the Storyteller) with little appreciable gain. What I might suggest is using something similar to <i><b>Price of Power </b></i>the extra Ban can represent the powers gained are tied to a relatively vulnerable item. And opening the flavor so it can apply equally well to Mad Scientists as well as Relic Makers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 08-11-2017, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T19:35:40-07:00","id":1127886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1127875#post1127875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: Lightning Elemental</b><br /> I would set up the ability to travel through a medium as a separate power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like?<br /> <br /> <b>Medium Surf</b> [Rename?]<br /> The Horror can travel through one specific medium (such as stone, sand, water, conductive material, etc.) arbitrarily fast. Determine the medium and the Speed at which the Horror can move through it - by spending a point of Willpower, the Horror can subsume itself into the medium and travel at speed. It can only move through contiguous portions of the medium (no teleporting between separate sources), though the Horror may be able to squeeze its entire form through even the smallest spaces the medium allows.<br /> <br /> I figure, you can recast the other teleporty Dread Powers to use a medium too, if you want Blood-Walking or something. This one requires an unbroken connection, so it <i>can</i> be hedged in with adequate planning and environment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1127875#post1127875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: Mad Science</b><br /> <br /> There is a lot going on here. The first thing I notice it would be very easy for a creature with this ability to effectively have access to a vast number of dread powers. I would curb this potential, remember that these are ease- of - use abilities to make running the game easier. Stacking powers onto a Horror is often more trouble (and more work for the Storyteller) with little appreciable gain. What I might suggest is using something similar to <i><b>Price of Power </b></i>the extra Ban can represent the powers gained are tied to a relatively vulnerable item. And opening the flavor so it can apply equally well to Mad Scientists as well as Relic Makers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. An elegant solution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1127875#post1127875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: Lightning Elemental</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Transmit</b><br /> The Horror is capable of transmitting itself though space via a specific medium (such as mirrors, doorways, electrical wiring, etc) which is chosen when this Dread Power is selected. By stepping into their chosen medium (or changing into a form that can travel through the medium), the creature will exit 1 minute later from another location where the medium is present, within a range of (Potecy x 5) miles.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Ack, ninja'd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-11-2017, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T22:48:20-07:00","id":1127929,"title":"","content":"<b>Mad Science </b>- Why does it not simply use rules for <b>Building Equipment</b> from <b>CoD Rulebook</b>? If rules from corebook can be used for doing magical talismans, they clearly could be used for Mad Science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-12-2017, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T06:28:38-07:00","id":1129203,"title":"","content":"Here's something: a Thing That Should Not Be in 2E rules (also something from the Champions Universe)<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Vulshoth, the Eye of the Void</span></b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">One of the infamous entities known collectively as the Kings of Edom, Vulshoth is a native of the &quot;Qliphotic World&quot;, a realm of &quot;dying&quot; universes that may or may not be the same thing as (or a subsection of, or something else) as the Abyss mages so fear. As with all his kind, he is a profoundly alien, amoral being with little care for any entity but himself-and like all the Kings of Edom, he was successfully imprisoned by ancient beings of extraterrestrial nature. In Vulshoth's case, he was imprisoned in something fitting his own influence, an extradimensional labyrinth within a metallic shell made of unknown matter. Normally Vulshoth could easily crack said shell, but the entity seems vulnerable to radiation-while the shell is not dangerous to humans, it prevents the Eye of the Void from regaining his strength. Unfortunately, the Kings do not need their power to find cracks in the prison small enough to send dreams through to those who might free them to feast on the life force of the universe again.<br /> <br /> <b>Power: </b>4. While Vulshoth is a potent creature, his imprisonment and inability to communicate directly with mortals (he must use prophetic dream and metaphor to translate his desires into something comprehensible) limits his influence on Earth. Hence the scheme of most of his cultists to construct &quot;amplifiers&quot; to focus and enhance his powers over space and enslavement.<br /> <br /> <b>Virulence: </b>8. This is why Edomites are so feared; they observed the current universe as it formed, and so they have adapted their powers to be almost part of reality. Vulshoth is no exception-once the Shining Darkness of the Qliphothic World enters the healthy universe, it stays until great sacrifice is needed to purge it. <br /> <br /> <b>Vulnerability: </b>As with most of his kin, Vulshoth has been forced to accept two universal vulnerabilities that show the Kings of Edom to be of the same class of being. First is the Spider Sign, a crystal lens that has been electrified after a precise relief of an eight-legged sigil has been carved on it forces the Kings and their creations to relive ancestral memories of its initial creators, who imprisoned them in the first place-the only things they fear. Second is the Mordant Flame, the result of mixing five sacred herbs that are found in most ingredient stores (just because, say, aluminum is common doesn't mean it isn't valuable) with the pulped brain of a member of an alien race called an Elder Worm, mixed with accelerant. The result is a purplish-blue conflagration that, while simply stinky to most beings, might as well be the Sun's own plasma to Edomite creatures with actual flesh (even Vulshoth, who is a physical entity). In addition, Vulshoth and his direct creations have a noted vulnerability to any harmful source of ionizing radiation-doubtless Vulshoth could be more resistant at full power, but the architects of the Black Maze smartly did not risk that.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T07:24:54-07:00","id":1129215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1127929#post1127929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mad Science </b>- Why does it not simply use rules for <b>Building Equipment</b> from <b>CoD Rulebook</b>? If rules from corebook can be used for doing magical talismans, they clearly could be used for Mad Science.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader?p=801821#post801821\">I have some homebrew rules where I use Paradigms as a type of switchable bane which is not necessarily unique to Mages</a>, and I am currently reworking it a bit to smooth it out, but includes new base Ephemeral Conditions Ascendant for Supernal Angels, which are the equivalent to Resonant for spirits and Anchors for ghost. Ascendant Condition is always tagged with one or more Paradigms to define what belief system(s) it supports. Those belief systems range from mystical traditions, religious practices, and even mad science.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader?p=859927#post859927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">---Mana Based Ephemeral Entities---</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Angel</span></b><br /> Angels are Ephemeral beings that require the Ascendant Condition of a corresponding specific Paradigm to use their Manifestations and use Mana as their supernatural fuel source. Angels are entities of pure Supernal magic and each is tied to a particular Paradigm. Angels gain Mana through others sacrificing to them, in a way similar to how a mage can sacrifice items to harvest Mana, but is mystically empowered by their presence so even devout non-template can fulfill the Yantra needed, in addition to the universal methods to for ephemeral beings to regain supernatural fuel.<br /> Each angel has a Purpose, the reason for its existence and the mechanism by which it regains willpower. When attempting but failing to further its purpose it gains back one Willpower, and when successful they regain all Willpower. This makes an angel in pursuit of their purpose extremely determined foes (as reflected in a willingness to spend willpower to achieve their purpose) as success replenishes any Willpower invested, and reserved spending of willpower would only happen when it began to seem unlikely that success was possible even with extensive willpower spent.<br /> <br /> <b>Sample Purposes:</b><ul><li>Ferry the souls of the dead deeper into the underworld</li> <li>Inspire art and creative brilliance in mortals</li> <li>Disprove the existence of the supernatural to the public</li> <li>Punished the dead souls of the damned.</li> <li>Guard the gates to Eden</li> </ul>Angels Influence is always their Purpose. Angels within Twilight are visible to those with the Paradigm Bane (including Angels of the same Paradigm) which matches their Paradigm. Angels are governed by the Prime Arcanum<br /> <b>Natural Plane:</b> Aether<br /> <b>Universal Tags:</b> Supernal, Angel, Ephemeral<br /> <b>Variable Tags </b><b>(IE Specific Paradigms)</b><b>:</b> Emergent Entheogenic Ritualism, Enochian Invocation , Onmy\u014dd\u014d, Hermeticism Goetia, Hermeticism Alchemy, Qigong, Aetheric Electromagnetism, Paranormal Psi Testing, Harmonic Mesmerism, Hellenic Vitalism, Phrenological Surgery, Christian Theurgy, Sufi Mysticism, Hermeticism Theurgy, Kabbalism, Mesoamerican Blood-Letting, African Tribal Shamanism, Theosophic Meditation, Vodoun Invocation, Shaolinquan, Neo-celtic derivative, New Age practices, Shinto Animistic Practices<br /> <br /> Ascendant is a condition that applies to locations that may be used as Yantra for specific Paradigm due to their suitable nature, beings in the process of using action Yantra to use powers or cast spells, and objects that are dedicated as tool Yantra. During casting of a spell or use of a power that has the condition is Open.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which allows me to use my homebrew Minor Template procedure, which is essentially adding potency 1 Horror stats with a couple modifications, to create Mad Scientists as a Minor Template<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader?p=859927#post859927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Minor Template</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Minor Templates are templates which are acquired by choice and dedication. In many cases even a Non-Template without assistance can gain the template if they do what is necessary and have the proper mastery. Minor templates always have prerequisites that must be met to gain them, and may be easier for certain types of character than others to fulfill (which is how they are categorized below). Associations with a Major Template (or Human) is either Prominent or Marginal. Minor Templates with a Prominent association with a Major Template may interchangeably use that Splat's Power Source for Willpower in activating the Dread Powers granted by the Minor Template and Willpower to activate things which normally take the Splat's Power Source, and requiring only a single dot in the Skill associate with the Minor Template plus the specific Specialty listed, and members of the Major Template may universally act as Mentors to lower the skill requirements to enter the Minor Template. Minor Template which are only Marginal associated with a Major Template only benefit from the ability to interchangeably use that Splat's Power Source for Willpower in activating the Dread Powers granted by the Minor Template and Willpower to activate things which normally take the Splat's Power Source. For clarification, Humans have Willpower is their Splat Power Source.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Each Minor Template which isn't exclusive to a particular Major Template gains a special type of Aspiration called a Feeding Aspiration. If being with a Minor Template doesn't fulfill their Feeding Aspiration each Month, then they cumulatively lose access to a Willpower Dot for each month they abstain. If the starving being with the Minor Template fulfills their Feeding Aspiration then they immediately regain access to the Willpower Dots they've been denied access due to abstaining from their Feeding Aspiration. Feeding Aspirations also replenish Willpower points spent instead of providing beats, exactly as they do with Horrors.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Minor Templates may or may not have a Bane and/or Ban, which are in place along with the severity of their Feeding Aspiration to balance them against other Minor Templates in terms of unequal Dread Powers.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Each Minor Template is keyed to a Skill and a specific Specialization. The Specialization is non-negotiable, but the levels of skill needed vary depending if it is Prominently Associated with a Major Template, members of the Associated Template (or Human) only require 1 dot in the skill, those apprentice under a Mentor of the Major Template with a Prominent association require 2 dots, apprenticing under an existing Member of the Minor Template which doesn't qualify for the Prominent discount is 3 dots, and those without any guidance or innate Template association require 4 dots.</span> <div align=\"center\"><i>-snip-</i></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mage</b><ul><li>Science (Any Mad Science Paradigm \u2013See Paradigm Bane) - Mad Scientist (Prominent)<ul><li>Influence 3 \u2013 Choose a Mad Science Paradigm (Ascendant)<ul><li>Feeding Aspiration: Harness something which is Ascendant with the Mad Scientist Paradigm for radical affect.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul><div align=\"center\"><i>-snip-</i></div> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Paradigms</span></b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Paradigm is one's conception of how supernatural abilities should be. All supernatural effects are a product of will, but the psyche isn't well equipped to channel reality twisting effects without ascribing it some rationale. Paradigm is an intellectually consistent framework of why supernatural abilities works that serves as 'insulation' between the supernatural being and the power they wield.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">In practice, a paradigm has two parts. First, it's a philosophy or methodology, an understanding of why and how supernatural powers work. This can be any known framework, so long as it's internally consistent and follows after mortal metaphysical tradition at least a hundred years old (though pseudo-sciences that old also work). Pseudo-science less than a hundred years old lack some quality that makes them suitable for use as a paradigm, while accurate and 'real' scientific theory fails entirely regardless of age. Increased supernatural powers may be understood as the ability to frame more and more abilities in the context of one's paradigm.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Secondly, and more concretely, it's a set of physical actions (formally called methods), locations prepared for the purpose, (called sanctums or laboratories) and/or physical objects (called implement or instrument) that the supernatural being uses to use its powers.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Paradigm always reflects a core aspect of the supernatural using it, tied to either its mortal upbringing, traumatic events that introduced it to the supernatural while still mortal, or the deep connection to the being that mentored them changing their Bane, and as such those that successfully identity a supernatural's paradigm gain the Informed Condition in relation to the contesting or identifying the supernatural creature's powers once per chapter. Additionally abilities of a supernatural to rise from the dead do not work if rest-in-peace practices appropriate to their paradigm are performed for them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Each supernatural being with the Paradigm Bane defines what broad belief system they are tapping into to perform their spells or powers. Feel free to use one of the following sample Paradigms that is appropriate to your character or how your character gained the Paradigm bane, or use them as a measuring stick to judge what is appropriate in breadth of a belief system.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Some </b></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>sample paradigms:</b></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Emergent Entheogenic Ritualism (Spontaneously arising spiritualism from psychotropic journeys)</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ceremonial Magic: Enochian Invocation (calling angels)</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ceremonial Magic: Onmy\u014dd\u014d</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ceremonial Magic: Hermeticism Goetia</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ceremonial Magic: Hermeticism Alchemy</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ceremonial Magic: Qigong</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mad Science: Aetheric Electromagnetism</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mad Science: Paranormal Psi Testing</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mad Science: Harmonic Mesmerism</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mad Science: Hellenic Vitalism</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mad Science: Phrenological Surgery</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Prayer &amp; Religious Practices: Christian Theurgy</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Prayer &amp; Religious Practices: Sufi Mysticism</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Prayer &amp; Religious Practices: Hermeticism Theurgy</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Prayer &amp; Religious Practices: Kabbalism</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Prayer &amp; Religious Practices: Mesoamerican Blood-Letting</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Prayer &amp; Religious Practices: African Tribal Shamanism</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Prayer &amp; Religious Practices: Theosophic Meditation</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Prayer &amp; Religious Practices: Vodoun Invocation</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Prayer &amp; Religious Practices: Shaolinquan</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Prayer &amp; Religious Practices: Neo-celtic derivative</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Prayer &amp; Religious Practices: New Age practices</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Prayer &amp; Religious Practices: Shinto Animistic Practices</span></span></span></li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And in my setting it is possible to switch one of the three banes each Major Template endures, and characters can have Minor and Major Template slots which can be filled (Bloodline legacies and such count towards this, but so do my skill based Minor Templates, like Mad Scientist) This allows flexibility to have a daylight immune Ordo Dracul Ventrue that must use his Disciplines and Devotions through Phrenological Surgery and also a Mad Scientist in Phrenological Surgery (I picture something like an undead version of <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0279688/\" target=\"_blank\">Beyond the Walls of Sleep</a>.) and that's something I think is pretty nifty to have that much flexibility in concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 08-18-2017, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T19:44:12-07:00","id":1130655,"title":"","content":"Enjoying the mechanics and ideas that are appearing here !<br /> <br /> I have a fresh horror that has been lurking in my mind for a few days - enjoy! <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Requ'ilu, the Looming Distance</b></span><br /> The \u201cRequ\u2019ilu\u201d is a Horror that has rarely been seen by anyone that was left sane and whole enough to recount the experience. The profoundly ancient creature dwells in the depths of the Shadow, but seems to be a creature of flesh as much as it is ephemera. The Creature is massive, rivaling the size of the greatest pre-historic beasts. Its body is a headless conglomeration of tree-like limbs, vine-like tendrils that cover its back, and leathery flesh shot with incandescent violet veins. It presence warps perspective and breaks down minds. Denizens of the deep Hisil flee at its approach. The Looming Distance seems to devour space itself, leaving behind terrible vacuums of collapsed space and shredded essence. While it seems to have some degree of intelligence, it never communicates and its motives are enigmatic.<br /> Thankfully, the creature seems to be bound only to the deeper reaches of the Hisil, places-that-aren\u2019t that seemingly encompass leagues. When compelled to wander into more densely populated sections of the Shadow, it can cause devastation that can take decades if not centuries to repair.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 4, Resolve 9, Strength 14, Dexterity 4, Stamina 10, Presence 8, Manipulation 2, Composure 10<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 4, Brawl 6, Intimidate 8, Occult 6(Hisil), Survival 5<br /> <b>Merits: </b>Danger Sense, Hardy 3, Indomitable, Iron Stamina 3, Trained Observer 3<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 9<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 19<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 14<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 10<br /> <b>Defense: </b>8<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 26 (Species 8)<br /> <b>Size:</b> 35<br /> <b>Health:</b> 45<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Cannot leave the <i>Hisil</i><br /> <b>Banes: </b>Claws and Fangs of Half Ephemeral creatures (such as Shartha or Uratha)<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Body Slam &amp;Trample [+2L melee; 20 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers**: <i>Colossus</i></b>, <b><i>Hideous Strength,</i></b> Immortal, Influence 3 (Space), Madness and Terror, <b><i>Mass Slam</i></b>, Numina (Awe), Reality Stutter, Regenerate<br /> <br /> <b><i>Colossus:</i></b> The Horror is a creature immense size and power. The Horror gains Armor equal to its Stamina. Against creatures and objects of smaller Size than the Horror, its attacks benefit from the 8-Again rule.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Hideous Strength:</i></b> The creature\u2019s might is truly formidable; by spending a point of Willpower, the Horror can increase its Strength by its Potency until the end of the scene. Furthermore, it adds its Potency as automatic successes on Strength + Stamina rolls made to perform a feat of strength, such as lifting a massive object or breaking free of restraints.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Mass Slam:</i></b> The horror is adept at using its monstrous bulk to crash into groups of smaller adversaries. The creature may inflict Body Slam or Trample attacks upon multiple adjacent targets with a combined Size 13. Roll its dice pool separately for each target, but count it as only one attack.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">*The Looming Distance\u2019s immense size grants it an additional 4 points of Strength<br /> ** The Looming Dread has exchanged 20available Skill Points for 4 Additional Dread Powers </span></div></div> </div> </div></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T07:27:21-07:00","id":1130813,"title":"","content":"Saw this in another thread, it is really good and decided to quote it here for people's future reference:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130662-new-horror-baphometalos#post1130662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>[New Horror] Baphometalos</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://pre01.deviantart.net/3e58/th/pre/f/2016/111/2/c/metal_god_by_glooh-d9zpb9r.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>Many monsters are afraid to show themselves. They think that mankind will fear and hate them, and therefore wish for their death. What they don't realize is that there is an alternate path: being adored. Little discretion is needed when everyone wants you to be in the spotlight, and so Baphometalos gives the people exactly what they want (and often a great deal more). Fear turns to awe and hatred turns to frustration in his wake, just as peace and order are made a laughingstock throughout the night. Should you be drawn by his legend and decide to meet him, rest assured that conformism, weakness and safety will be gone from your life for a long time!<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Awesome<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Brutal<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Rock The Fuck Out, Face Greater And Greater Challenges, Inspire People To Be Badass<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 8, Resolve 10<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 9, Dexterity 7, Stamina 9<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 10, Manipulation 4, Composure 6<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2, Crafts 1, Investigation 2, Occult 3, Athletics 4, Brawl 3, Drive (Motorcycle) 3, Weaponry (Battle Axe) 4, Empathy 2, Expression (Heavy Metal, Inspiring) 8, Intimidation (Larger Than Life, Massive Property Damage) 6, Persuasion 2, Socialize (Parties) 5, Streetwise 3, Subterfuge 3<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise 1 (Heavy Metal), Interdisciplinary Specialty 1 (Heavy Metal), Professional Training 5 (Heavy Metal God: Expression, Socialize, Intimidation), Contacts (Celebrities, Fans), Fame 2, Inspiring 3, Iron Will 2, Resources 4, Striking Looks 2 (Blacker Than The Blackest Black), Table Turner 1<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 26<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 11<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 13<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 30 In Human Form, 50 In God Form<br /> <b>Health:</b> 15 In Human Form, 25 In God Form<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6 In Human Form, 16 In God Form<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> <br /> Metal Fists [+0L, Melee, 13 Dice]<br /> Blast (Electric Guitar) [+0L to +5L, Maximum 100 Yards, Presence + Expression + Heavy Metal, 20 Dice]<br /> Flaming Battle Axe [+4L, Melee, 14 Dice]<br /> Psychokinesis [+5L, 13 Dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Ban 1:</b> Can only use Blast with Electric Guitar<br /> <br /> <b>Ban 2:</b> Must answer any challenges to his badassery<br /> <br /> <b>Ban 3:</b> Must help for one scene whoever impresses him in a musical duel<br /> <br /> <b>Ban 4:</b> Must stick it to The Man at the end of every scene he is in<br /> <br /> <b>Bane 1:</b> Being laughed off the stage<br /> <br /> <b>Bane 2:</b> Calm music<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Elemental Fury*, Elusive*, Fire Elemental, Hideous Strength*, Immortal, Influence (Badassery 1), Madness And Terror, Monstrous Resilience, Numen (Aggressive Meme, Blast [Electric Guitar], Hallucination [Special Effects], Rapture), Psychic Talent* x 1 (Psychokinesis 5, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/842864-advanced-supernatural-merits-and-styled-supernatural-merits\"><b>Advanced 3, Epic 2 [Fire]</b></a>), Regenerate 1, Unbreakable, Price Of Power* x 6<br /> <br /> <b>*Elemental Fury: </b>Baphometalos has Influence (Storms) 5. When using this Influence, he can affect an area as large as his Potency in diameter in miles.<br /> <br /> <b>*Elusive: </b>Creatures with this Dread Power only ever appear on camera as a blurred silhouette of their actual shape. Humanoid monsters can easily be mistaken for humans or upright bears, while unusually large creatures blend into the scenery. Humans have a hard time remembering exact detail about creatures they encounter. Rolls to accurately describe or recall such events are made at a \u20133 modifier.<br /> <br /> <b>*Hideous Strength:</b> The creature\u2019s might is truly formidable; by spending a point of Willpower, the Horror can increase its Strength by its Potency until the end of the scene. Furthermore, it adds its Potency as automatic successes on Strength + Stamina rolls made to perform a feat of strength, such as lifting a massive object or breaking free of restraints.<br /> <br /> <b>*Psychic Talent:</b> Creatures with this dread power are endowed with great powers of the mind. Each dot in this Dread Power grants a creature a number of Merit dots equal to its Potency. These Merit dots may be used to purchase Supernatural Merits.<br /> <br /> <b>*Price Of Power:</b> By taking on an additional Ban or Bane, an entity can increase its repertoire of abilities. Each additional Ban or Bane can give it one of the following.<br /> <br /> * Two Numina, Influence dots, or Manifestations.<br /> * An increase of its maximum Essence pool by 5.<br /> * A Dread Power.<br /> <br /> An entity may take this Numina a number of times equal to its Rank.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I changed which parts have Spoilers to fit the standard format for this thread. Also when I picture the use of Heavy Metal Blast I am picturing something to the affect of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FfQWz4gVcP8\" target=\"_blank\">opening the Ark of the Covenant in Raiders of the Lost Ark, faces melting</a> because of the <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/SugarWiki/MomentOfAwesome\" target=\"_blank\">sheer awesome display.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 08-18-2017, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T12:10:36-07:00","id":1132342,"title":"","content":"What do you think of the following new effects for Dread Powers, Reighnhell? Would you use them in a game?<br /> <br /> <b>Chameleon Horror +1:</b> The Horror receives Rote Quality on Stealth rolls, may make Stealth rolls even when moving at full Speed, and any supernatural attempts to find them provoke a Clash Of Wills against their Dexterity + Stealth + Potency. By spending 1 Willpower, it can also add its Potency to Stealth rolls for the scene. Spending 3 Willpower points adds its Potency as bonus Successes on a Stealth roll for one turn, or divides its Potency as bonus Successes across multiple turns. However: it automatically acquires a Ban that dictates a situation which removes Chameleon Horror (both versions), prevents Willpower expenditure on Stealth rolls and applies the opposite of Advanced Action to said Skill (roll twice and keep worst result).<br /> <br /> <b>Natural Weapons +1:</b> All attacks count as supernatural damage and may pierce even supernatural armor and barriers with a Clash Of Wills consisting of Strength + Brawl or Weaponry + Potency, Replace Strength with Dexterity if the Horror has Fighting Finesse. This may take the Dread Power up to a rating of 4 dots. By spending 3 Willpower points, the damage becomes aggravated for one turn. However, the Horror automatically acquires a Ban that prevents them harming others physically in certain situations.<br /> <br /> <b>Beastmaster +1:</b> The Horror not only can command animals, it can enhance them as well. By touching an animal and spending 1 Willpower, it may give a number of Dread Power dots to it equal to Success on an appropriate roll (e.g. Presence + Animal Ken, Intelligence + Medicine). By spending 3 Willpower points, it gains Rote Quality on this roll and may enhance animals via direct line of sight. The animal gains one Dread Power dot even if the roll fails. The Horror must know the Dread Powers it wishes to give, which remain with the animal for the scene. Spending 2 additional Willpower points makes this last for 24 hours. However, the enhanced animals suffer from the same Bans and Banes as the Horror while this effect lasts.<br /> <br /> <b>Beastmaster +1: </b>The Horror may conjure animals from nothing. Spending 1 Willpower point conjures a group of smaller animals, or one larger animal. The animals last for one scene, after which they disappear. Spending 2 additional Willpower points makes the animals last for 24 hours. The Horror may have instances of this effect active up to its Potency at any given time, and most Horrors have restrictions on which types of animals they can conjure.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunter's Senses +1: </b>The Horror gains a +6 bonus and 8 Again on Perception rolls against its favored prey. By spending 3 Willpower, it may add its Potency as bonus Successes on an active Perception roll for one turn, or divide its Potency as bonus Success across multiple turns. This stacks with the Occult Sight Numen. However, the Horror automatically acquires a Ban that dictates a situation which removes Hunter's Senses (both versions), applies its Potency as a penalty to all Perception rolls, prevents Willpower expenditure on said rolls and downgrades its Failures into Dramatic Failures.<br /> <br /> <b>Maze +1:</b> Attempting to leave the Maze through supernatural means provokes a Clash Of Wills against the Horror's Resolve + An Appropriate Skill + Potency. The Horror gains Rote Quality on Chase rolls while inside the Maze. However, the Horror automatically acquires a Ban that forces it to release its captives in a certain situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-21-2017, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T12:55:59-07:00","id":1132365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1130813#post1130813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saw this in another thread, it is really good and decided to quote it here for people's future reference: I changed which parts have Spoilers to fit the standard format for this thread. Also when I picture the use of Heavy Metal Blast I am picturing something to the affect of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FfQWz4gVcP8\" target=\"_blank\">opening the Ark of the Covenant in Raiders of the Lost Ark, faces melting</a> because of the <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/SugarWiki/MomentOfAwesome\" target=\"_blank\">sheer awesome display.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I'm flattered. And that is exactly what his Blast looks like! You get +1 Internet Cookie.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T20:11:46-07:00","id":1132481,"title":"","content":"Here's what I was leading up to with Vulshoth...though very poorly formatted due to a phone.<br /> <b>Tappan Arkwright III</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Quote:<i> &quot;Soon I will be I, and sooner, you will be nothing at all.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> This lead-in is a lie. Arkwright, the person actually named as such, is not a Horror. In fact, he's not even a bad person by any reasonable stretch of the imagination. It's really not his fault he is host to the High Priest of Vulshoth, and while he can't quite overcome his unwanted passenger's survival instinct, he has been quietly responsible for thwarting his wicked brother's schemes more often than not.<br /> <br /> His<i> brother</i>, on the other hand, has no name. In fact, for much of Arkwright's life, nobody was aware that there was a brother-just a freakish birth defect. Quite simply, the Twin is a parasitic one, the result of an incomplete reabsorbtion that, due to Abyssal energies in the graveyard Arkwright was conceived, has a functioning brain despite it being the size of a walnut and sharing his brother's brain stem. Driven insane by isolation and the fear people have of a literal second face at the back of his brother's skull, the Twin came to despise the species he was nearly a part of, and his hate and despair called to Vulshoth's dreaming intellect. In symbolic dreams, the Eye made a deal with the Twin-in return for service, the King would give the Twin the ability to take control of his and Arkwright's shared body. In return for freedom, a place as a fully independent god-king at the Eye's side.<br /> <br /> As might be obvious from his title, the High Priest has made good on his promise.<br /> <br /> <b>Description</b>: Tappan Arkwright and the Twin share a body, so they share a description. Arkwright is an unassuming white Bostonian in bis 40s, one who is only notable for wearing silk scarves rather than ties in his conservative business suits. He wears his hair long to conceal the Twin's face in the back of his head, a lined two-inch diameter mug that has gained the ability to express since the deal with Vulshoth (it goes back to its original blankness when the Twin is in control, so the Twin doesn't let his sibling go to a barber-however, that does mean the local shops remember, and dread, Arkwright, as the Twin is a horrible and mean-spirited customer). One can tell who is currently driving by their stance and expression-Tappan is withdrawn, slumped, and shy, while the Twin is manic, vicious, and wilful.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints</b>: Arkwright himself is a victim. He doesn't share memories with the Twin, but is all too aware of what, and who, his brother is. The Twin can't help but gloat, really, giving his &quot;lucky&quot; sibling a taste of the helplessness the Twin felt for decades. He tries to help when he can, but the Twin is wise to his brother's shenanigans and he can only manage manipulating his brother's considerable ego and inferiority complex. As for the Twin, his story may make him pitiable, but the idea of some disgusting human feeling for him is, if anything, even more offensive than the constant jeers he (actually Arkwright, but since when has a crazed worshiper of alien gods ever been known for perspective?) endured. Even beyond the deaths required to supply power for Edomite mysticism, the Twin regularly kills humans at relative random, deliberately chosing a wide palate to confuse the authorities-the police have no idea that the sudden increase in violent deaths is the work of one killer, let alone he's the same person as the Mind Flayer (the recharge ritual requires pulping the sacrifice's brain matter and extracting their cerebral fluid to drink later to revitalize the High Priest's powers).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> (Character sheet later)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 08-22-2017, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T22:33:19-07:00","id":1132509,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Advanced Dread Powers</b><br /> <br /> I like this idea. I normally balance an Horror as if I was writing blue-book material (ie. with the idea that anyone going against the horror will be mostly mortal). That being said, Horror that go up against Template characters may need a bit more oomph to keep things challenging. However, Generally speaking, I try to avoid just adding more dice - dice bloat just slows down the action at the table. Strive for simplicity of effect. Here are a few of my notes and suggestions below.<br /> <hr /><b>Chameleon Horror +1:</b> I like the overall idea of Advanced Dread Powers and I like giving the rote quality to a specific task. However, adding Potency extra dice to a roll the Horror is getting rote quality on, in addition to the penalties observers take from regular Chameleon Horror (not even considering the possibility of auto -successes) becomes really excessive. At a point, its easier to say &quot;the creature is invisible&quot; than giving it a massive dice pool. Try this version -<br /> <br /> <i><b>Invisible Horror (prerequisite -Chameleon Horror):</b> The Horror becomes wholly invisible. The penalty the Horror imposes upon attempts to perceive it granted by Chameleon Horror becomes -6 in all circumstances. Supernatural perceptions can pierce this Invisibility, invoking a Clash of Wills against the Horrors Composure+Potency to negate the penalty imposed by this Dread Power until the end of the scene.In addition, the Horror receives Rote Quality on Stealth rolls, and may make Stealth rolls even when moving at full Speed. In most cases Invisibility is a permanent aspect of the creature, but some can control when they are visible. In the latter case, altering its visibility for a scene costs the Horror one point of Willpower. The creature\u2019s Invisibility imposes a Ban - which is always condition where it does not apply (such as infrared light or when observed by children).</i> <hr /><b>Natural Weapons +1:</b> Offensive Powers are best kept simple - invoking a Clash of Will on each attack is probably too much.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Rending Attack (prerequisite - Natural Weapons \u2022\u2022): </b>The Horror's Natural Attacks are imbued with power enough to rend even the most resilient flesh. The Horrors natural attacks gain the 9-Again quality and are considered supernatural damage. When the Horror inflicts damage with its Natural Weapons, it may spend a point of Willpower to convert a point of the Lethal Damage it inflicted to Aggravated Damage. </i> <hr /><b>Beastmaster +1:</b> With the first Beastmaster power, the effect can be streamlined a bit. The second Beastmaster power is not really necessary, as where the animals come from is more of a flavor consideration and not a explicit concern of the Beastmaster Dread Power.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Dark Menagerie (prerequisite - </b></i><b>Beastmaster</b><i><b>): </b>The Horror not only can command animals, it can enhance them as well. By spending 1 Willpower, and making an appropriate roll, it may share one of its Dread Powers with any animal it commands that is within its line of sight. The animal gains use of the Dread Power until the end of the scene. On an exceptional Success, the Horror may share 1 additional Dread power with the animal. Any animal enhanced in this fashion suffers from the same Bans and Banes as the Horror while this effect lasts.</i> <hr /><b>Hunter's Senses +1: </b>8 again is good, but a +6 dice bonus may be a bit much, and Potency auto-success (even with numerous drawbacks) may also be a bit much. This would be a good place for a special effect.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Relentless Pursuit (prerequisite - Hunter's Senses): </b>The Horror gains 8 Again on Perception rolls against its favored prey. By spending 3 Willpower, and making an appropriate roll resisted by the targets Wits+Supernatural Tolerance, it may &quot;mark&quot; a chosen target. The target gains the Marked Condition. The Horror will know the distance and direction of a target it imposed this condition upon. Targets with the Marked Condition suffer a -3 penalty to rolls to avoid, flee or hide from the Horror, and any failures become dramatic failures. Attempts to use Supernatural methods of escape or Stealth invoke a Clash of Wills against the Horrors Resolve+Potency. The condition ends when the target either fulfills a &quot;escape clause&quot; or after a number of days equal to the Horrors Potency. This escape clause is typically a distance from the Horror (Potency x 20 miles is common) or location (such as hallowed ground or across a particular body of water). </i> <hr /><b>Maze +1:</b> I like Advanced version of Maze mostly as is. the only real adjust is its Clash of Will roll. Clash of Will rolls are typically &quot;Power +Potency&quot;. To keep that parity, I suggest Attribute + Potency to keep it in line with how Clash of Wills are set up in most of the other game lines.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Escher Knot </b><b>(prerequisite - Maze):</b> Attempting to leave the Maze through supernatural means provokes a Clash Of Wills against the Horror's Resolve + Potency. The Horror gains Rote Quality on Chase rolls while inside the Maze. However, the Horror automatically acquires a Ban that forces it to release its captives in a certain situation.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T08:46:09-07:00","id":1133026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1132509#post1132509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: Advanced Dread Powers</b><br /> [/I] <hr /><b>Maze +1:</b> I like Advanced version of Maze mostly as is. the only real adjust is its Clash of Will roll. Clash of Will rolls are typically &quot;Power +Potency&quot;. To keep that parity, I suggest Attribute + Potency to keep it in line with how Clash of Wills are set up in most of the other game lines.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Escher Knot </b><b>(prerequisite - Maze):</b> Attempting to leave the Maze through supernatural means provokes a Clash Of Wills against the Horror's Resolve + Potency. The Horror gains Rote Quality on Chase rolls while inside the Maze. However, the Horror automatically acquires a Ban that forces it to release its captives in a certain situation.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue Maze would already provoke Clash of Wills when using supernatural powers to escape since it is a supernatural power designed to contain beings and prevent escape. Additionally while I see that a Chase might be possible since the victims could just flee from the Horror in an unspecific path away, but I think we can make it more frightening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CofD p. 146</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>MAZE</b></span><br /> The creature can turn a structure into something out of an M. C. Escher painting, creating an insane maze. By spending 3 Willpower and touching the building, it turns the interior chambers into a tangled mess of corridors and rooms that lead back on themselves; this effect lasts for an hour. Anyone other than the creature who attempts to move through the building must succeed at a Wits + Composure check minus the creature\u2019s Resolve each time they attempt to leave the area or progress through it to somewhere specific; if they fail they are unable to progress and simply get more lost.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>H. H. Holmes Horror Hotel</b><b>(prerequisite - Maze):</b><br /> The structure changes to degrees greater than merely warping space . Rooms reset to hide evidence of slaughter, mayhem, and carnage. Additionally the floors can open under its victims, walls drop down to prevent their escape, and swinging blades or spike spill crimson blood. The Horror is aware of the location of every being within the Maze may spend a Willpower while the Maze is active to inflict a Trap upon a victim as per Safe Place equal to their Potency. Additionally attempts escape in a Chase from the Horror or gain Clues about things done in the Maze are considered a Recondite action. Additionally Horror gains a Ban which states the how someone may exit the structure and barring a successful Clash of Wills of a supernatural power that'd allow egress that's the only exit method. Travel within the structure is still governed by the rules of Maze.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u200bNew Permutation</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Recondite</b><br /> The task takes extreme training and preparation to have a reasonable chance for success, and you\u2019ve got a significant reduced chance of success if you don't. When you make a roll, you must reroll any dice that shows an 8, 9, or 10. Do not count the first roll of those dice as successes. If you\u2019re reduced to a chance die on a Recondite action, reroll if you don't get a dramatic failure and disregard 10-Again. You may only reroll each die once unless it comes a 10 the second time, if 10-Again applies. Rote and Recondite negate each other instead of applying the mechanics of either.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Inspired by<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt3424690/\" target=\"_blank\">Havenhurst</a> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 08-25-2017, 01:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T21:50:35-07:00","id":1133666,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Maze +1 </b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3279_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3279\" data-vbnamecard=\"3279\">Pale_Crusader</a>, You raise a very good point! I will agree that Maze would provoke a Clash without need a special add on - which sort of makes my version redundant. That is OK, since I like your &quot;H.H Holmes&quot; version much better and I'm adding it to my Dread Powers file.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T12:00:58-07:00","id":1133900,"title":"","content":"Finally finishing Tappan's character sheet:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> Note that this character sheet only applies to Tappan when the Twin is in control; the real Arkwright is a normal human who is more likely to pass out in a physical conflict (which, unfortunately, also gives Twin an opening to overtake their body).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Intelligence 6, Wits 5, Resolve 7, <br /> <br /> Strength 2, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3, <br /> <br /> Presence 6, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b><br /> <br /> Academics 3, Crafts (Edomite Rune Magic) 2, Investigation 3, Occult (Edom Lore) 5, Science 2<br /> <br /> Athletics 2, Brawl 2, Stealth 1, Weaponry (Ritual Knife) 2<br /> <br /> Empathy 2, Intimidation (Misanthropy Incarnate) 4, Streetwise 3, Subterfuge 3<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b>:<br /> <br /> Encyclopedic Knowledge (Lore of the Kings) **, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Edom Lore) *, Relentless **, Mentor (Vulshoth) ***, Resources ***, <br /> <br /> (while he is the High Priest of Vulshoth, the Twin does not have a proper organization to have Status in, as the worshipers of the Kings are too disorganized, at the moment. What powers he would have gained from Mystery Cult Initiation are covered by his Dread Powers.)<br /> <br /> <b>Potency: </b>5<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Ban of Power (refreshment ritual, grants 2 Dread Powers), Beastmaster (Least Edomites*), Blast (Dissolution of Matter), Drain, Influence (Qliphotic Energies ***), Implant Mission, Madness and Terror, Maze<br /> <br /> * Actually, the Twin can summon much bigger things that last longer in our universe, but these require specialized rituals that, in fact, much of the Twin's waking hours are dedicated to preparing and carrying out. The creatures summoned by Beastmaster are the few species he can manage without all of that mucking about with rituals and alien chanting, a chaotic arrangement of animal-like monsters that resemble mutated versions of vermin with redundant organs, tentacles, and the like. They vanish after about a day.<br /> <br /> <b>Ban: </b>The Twin must drink a specially prepared serum of pulped brain matter every month (counting the time Tappan is in control) or lose his access to Dread Powers until he does drink the serum. The preparation, naturally, being a ritualized murder in which he slices the donor in seven sacred spots with his ritual knife, but Vulshoth isn't picky about the choice of victim, and the ritual only takes about ten minutes if the victim is fighting back.<br /> <br /> <b>Ban: </b>Tappan is somewhat aware of what his sibling does (not the least because the Twin bullies him into living a normal-esque life to hide his activities, or occasionally helping when the Twin needs to work in a constructive social manner to get a particular resource), and fights back. Whenever the Twin is knocked unconscious, tired, or frightened (the last of which is not easy to do, seeing as how the High Priest has generally seen the worst any universe has to offer), Tappan roles his own Resolve + Composure pool of 6 versus the Twin's own. This means that the Twin can be active for days given how his pool is nearly twice that, but even Tappan losing to the Twin (assuming that the Twin does not roll an exceptional success) inflicts a -2 dice penalty for the rest of the scene to the Twin's actions as he fends off his brother's control. The Twin's loss (which he is known to do on purpose when laying low), means Tappan rests control and the Twin sleeps...at least until Vulshoth calls his servant once more...</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T14:22:13-07:00","id":1133947,"title":"","content":"What does his Influence: Qliphotic Energies allow him to do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T15:29:26-07:00","id":1133964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1133947#post1133947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does his Influence: Qliphotic Energies allow him to do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Control, strengthen, and influence anything corrupted by or born from the Qliphothic World. The Qliphoth turns everything it touches a bit Lovecraftian (for example, making a painter who tried to paint and image-less picture instead paint one of a corrupt soul and causing her to start extruding tentacles made of her lower soul). It tends everything towards madness and dissolution, as it is literally the realm of the Solipist, the Anti-Creator.<br /> <br /> More importantly, it's what allows him to wrangle servants of the Kings of Edom, as they are by definition Qliphothic in nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T08:05:55-07:00","id":1134470,"title":"","content":"I want to create a new Horror called (tentatively) Wormflesh. What's the best source for up-to-date ruleswise dread powers? Is Mortal Remains up-to-date?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T10:24:29-07:00","id":1134513,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7920_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7920\" data-vbnamecard=\"7920\">Master Aquatosic</a> Yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T10:33:29-07:00","id":1134516,"title":"","content":"Here's his first write-up <div align=\"center\"><b>Wormflesh</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><i>The worms crawl in and the worms crawl out<br /> They'll eat your guts and spit it out<br /> Put the blood of your enemy in the worms' den<br /> and we shall see what happens then</i></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Most musical historians place the Hearse Song as we know it as originating from at least WWI. Some more fragmented reports of the story attribute the song to British soldiers in the Crimean War. There's even another song they won't admit is the same emerging from the 1810s. .<br /> <br /> But the song is even older than that.<br /> <br /> The true song is known to few people (and we can thank many brave hunters for that), but its original form is a description of the ritual to summon the great beast, Wormflesh. The details can get tricky, but the gist is that you must find at least a mass of earthworms equal to at least your own weight. Then, you must give them the richest compost you can find and mix in the concoction of sacred, or perhaps infernal, &quot;herbs&quot;, before adding the final, and most important ingredient: the blood of your worst enemy.<br /> <br /> And as you sing the song and the worms make their gruesome feast, the worms will learn to taste your hatred, bathe in it and form the monster. That monster's first victim will be you. But that's not where it ends.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Hateful; <b>Vice: </b>Trustworthy<br /> <b>Aspiration: </b>Destroy everything their target loves, eventually kill target<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 8, Resolve 6<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 7, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 10, Manipulation 8, Composure 3<br /> <b>Ban 1</b>: must flee sunlight<br /> <b>Ban 2: </b>Can only use Contagious on rotting corpses<br /> <b>Bane 1</b>: soil untouched by any life for 10 years<br /> <b><b>Bane 2:</b></b> The blood of someone whose trust he has betrayed<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Occult 3, Crafts 3 (trapped passages), Athletics 3, Brawl 2, Larceny 3, Survival 2, Weaponry 1, Animal Ken 3 (scavengers), Empathy 3 (Vices), Intimidation 5, Persuasion 4, Subterfuge 3(spreading rumors)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Striking Looks (Revolting, 00); Safe Place (00); Staff (00; Wormlings Spies [stealth] and Trap Builders [Crafts]); Grappling (000); Pusher; Spin Doctor; Fast-Talking (0000); Double-Jointed<br /> <b>]Potency: </b>8<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 17<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 10<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 0/0<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 10<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 15 burrowing / 13 above ground<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Grapple 0B Melee<br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Numen(Price of Power(Hallucination, Implant Mission)), Discorporate, Swarm, Hunter's Senses (target and immediate sympathetic connections), Numen(Price of Power(Mortal Mask, Aggressive Meme)), Contagious (transmits through forcing worms into orifices for at least 1 sustained minute)*, Dead Flesh (00)<br /> <br /> *This version of Contagious creates the brief nightmares known as wormlings, vaguely humanoid mounds of worms slavishly loyal to Wormflesh. Here's a single entity<br /> <b>Best At (5 dice): </b>spying unseen, suffocating victims, creating underground lairs<br /> <b>Worst at (Chance die)</b>: fine manipulation, bravery against their bane, communicating with anyone other than Wormflesh<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> please their master, frolic in fresh corpses<br /> <b>Willpower/scene</b>: 2<br /> <b>Bane</b>: worm-killing pesticides<br /> <b>Dread Powers</b>: Swarm, Unbreakable, Innocuous<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 10-23-2021, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T10:44:09-07:00","id":1134521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1134513#post1134513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7920_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7920\" data-vbnamecard=\"7920\">Master Aquatosic</a> Yes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you. What do you think of the write-up. i know it sounds like a brief nightmare, but it doesn't just want to kill the person the ritual makes it hate, it wants to ruin their life first and I'm trying to give it the ability to do just that and still put up a fight. And I realized halfway through that it could be used as a Huntsman in C:tL with a few changes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T11:40:52-07:00","id":1134535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1134521#post1134521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thank you. What do you think of the write-up. i know it sounds like a brief nightmare, but it doesn't just want to kill the person the ritual makes it hate, it wants to ruin their life first and I'm trying to give it the ability to do just that and still put up a fight. And I realized halfway through that it could be used as a Huntsman in C:tL with a few changes</div> </div> </div> </div>Needs actual statistics. This thread is great for example critters, and there is no stat block there. I'd definitely throw in Hallucination and Dement in there as Dread Powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T11:46:14-07:00","id":1134536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1134535#post1134535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Needs actual statistics. This thread is great for example critters, and there is no stat block there. I'd definitely throw in Hallucination and Dement in there as Dread Powers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, I'll get you some stats. Was working on them as we speak. That said, why Hallucination and Dement?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:43:22-07:00","id":1134575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1134536#post1134536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ok, I'll get you some stats. Was working on them as we speak. That said, why Hallucination and Dement?</div> </div> </div> </div>To ruin the target mentally. Dement for longer lasting harm, Hallucination for more incidental havoc. Things like imaging worms are crawling all over you, are underneath other people's skin, stuff like that. Heck, it might not even need physical ability at all, driving targets into killing themselves (either directly, or through making themselves a danger and getting taken out by others).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:55:59-07:00","id":1134584,"title":"","content":"Ok, that works. Hell, you know what, sure.<br /> <br /> Also. do powers start with one dot in each attribute too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 08-27-2017, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:57:49-07:00","id":1134586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1134516#post1134516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's his first write-up <div align=\"center\"><b>Wormflesh</b></div><div align=\"center\"><i>The worms crawl in and the worms crawl out<br /> They'll eat your guts and spit <b>it</b> out<br /> Put the blood of your enemy in the worms' den<br /> and we shall see what <b>will</b> happen then</i></div></div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine, that makes for a better metric.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1134516#post1134516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most musical historians place the Hearse Song as we know it as originating from at least WWI. Some more fragmented reports of the story attribute to British soldiers in the Crimean War. There's even another song they won't admit is the same coming from the 1810s. .<br /> <br /> But the song is even older than that.<br /> <br /> The true song is known to few people (and we can thank many brave hunters for that), but its original form is a description of the ritual to summon the great beast, Wormflesh. The details can get tricky, but the gist is that you must find at least a mass of earthworms equal to at least your own weight. Then, you must give them compost containing enough of your enemy's blood to totally stain a 5x5 inch square of plot. This cannot just be someone you dislike, it has to be someone you truly hate. Someone who has truly ruined your life in your mind, whether they know it or not, whether it's even true or not. Someone for whose utter destruction you would kill strangers or even die to see it pass. For that is exactly what will happen.<br /> <br /> And as you sing the song and the worms make their gruesome feast, the worms will learn to taste your hatred, bath in it and form the monster. That monster's first victim will be you...</div> </div> </div> </div>Bit of an editorial advice:<br /> <br /> Details about &quot;someone you truly hate&quot; are irrelevant: you're drawing enough blood from them to display your hatred for them; Don't get relative all of a sudden with the &quot;in your mind&quot; statement.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T13:02:46-07:00","id":1134588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1134586#post1134586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Emphasis mine, that makes for a better metric.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Bit of an editorial advice:<br /> <br /> Details about &quot;someone you truly hate&quot; are irrelevant: you're drawing enough blood from them to display your hatred for them; Don't get relative all of a sudden with the &quot;in your mind&quot; statement.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Noted. Will change that. Anyway, is it too much blood? I was trying to go with an amount of blood small enough that you wouldn't need to capture them and drain them to get it. I mean, if you could do that, why summon Wormflesh when you could torment him yourself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T16:07:36-07:00","id":1134650,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Wormflesh</b><br /> <br /> Looking over your write up - here are a few notes -<br /> <br /> <b>Stats for the Horror</b><br /> <br /> I stick primarily to the format for Horrors as presented in CofD (pg. 140 - 148). I while it does not explicitly say Horrors start with 1 dot in each attribute, I still use that as my starting point.<br /> As far as Mortal Remains and Dread Powers, the format is somewhat different between the two sources. CofD treats Dread Powers like Numina (to the point that they are mostly interchangeable), with each Dread Power having a specific effect and only a few of them having ranks. With Mortal Remains rules, Dread Powers have varying ranks and costs, and operate more like Merits. So they are <i>not quite</i> compatible, and you may have to do some tinkering to get the powers to work correctly. Feel free to go over this this thread and snag any of my home brewed Dread Powers if you see any that would work for this creature.<br /> <br /> <b>How much Blood?</b><br /> <br /> I don't think you need to be as specific with the details of the summoning ritual. Stick to the main points - Compost Rich Soil, The blood of a Hated Foe, and the Summoners weigh in worms. Try to make the text evocative enough to inspire plot hooks.<br /> For the stats itself, the main considerations would be how will it oppose the player characters. Is it a physical bruiser that pummels and drowns in a squirming tide? Is it a subtle terror that warps perceptions and drives it victims mad? Does it have human patience and cunning, or is it a near-mindless thing? So on and so forth. Once you know what its main gimmicks and tactics will be , the selection of skills and abilities will fall into place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T18:59:41-07:00","id":1135019,"title":"","content":"posted Wormflesh's first character sheet. If it seems a bit unfocused, please know that I understand that and want to know how you would suggest to change it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T10:36:00-07:00","id":1138632,"title":"","content":"As a prelude to when I have my actual book, here's another fluff conversion from a superhero game:<br /> <br /> <b>The Grue Unity</b><br /> <br /> Quote: [Pitable solid, all alone. How foolish of you to think your chaotic wreck of a society is superior to us, the children of perfect Unity.]<br /> <br /> Earth has more horrors born in its universe than monsters. In the not-to-distant reaches of space (at least going by their method of FTL) a strange, hostile species looks upon the planet with cold and greedy eyes. They have no name for themselves, as they have no mouth. But their ancient rivals, the Lor, gave them one after an ancient demon of the dark, and they quite like it. To their many enslaved client planets, they are the All-Formed Ones, but to everyone else, they are the Grue Unity.<br /> <br /> The first thing to understand about the Grue is that they are shapeshifters-while they have a true form, a red-skinned humanoid with cold, white eyes that resemble cataracts, it is ultimately just a convinience, a resting state that the Grue return to when not actively trying at deception; every Grue, from the lowliest drone to the mighty Meta-Mind himself (while Grue do not have genders, they recognize most human societies view males as superior-a ridiculous concept when the primary difference between biological sexes is simply who bares young, but the Grue default to male pronouns for convinience), is a biokinetic and telepath whose flesh is fluid clay at a moment's thought, a necessity on their chaotic shifting honeworld and its panoply of clever, psychic predators. Even the all-but-mindless drones are instinctive masters of disguise, while intelligent, ensouled metamorphs are all that and living, ever-shifting weapons near impossible to corner due to their mastery of shape. They know this, and for that all other sentient life is inferior, for they cannot adapt and evolve like the Grue can. They cannot know things that the Grue do from the moment they are born.<br /> <br /> The second is, due to an accident of biology and telepathy, the Grue Unity got its name from a group mind; the primeval Grue learned that, by melding their bodies and brains into one, they could fuse into a mind capable of serving as king and network hub for the telepathic race. It was from these hubs that the first Grue civilizations were born, and how they conquered their home-and each other, in a devastating war that imprinted upon the last Joined, and through him th surviviors and all the others who came after, a simple truth; that which cannot be controlled, cannot be trusted. For this, all other sentient life is feared. They are so strange to the Omnifarious, the collective subconscious of the Grue, and that which is strange is, by definition, not controlled. &quot;Foriegn&quot; and &quot;evil' have the same word in the Grue written language.<br /> <br /> The third is that they are adaptable; if a carbon-based being is capable of breathing it, of eating it, of drinking it, then the Grue can; give them a day or so, they can adjust their metabolism and biochemistry to it. For this, they explore-the stars have never been particularly far away for them, and they wish to expand like most life does, to grow and incorporate more territory into their empire.<br /> <br /> So, then, how would you think they feel when they find that so much of the prime estate to colonize is already owned by beings they fear and look down upon?<br /> <br /> They feel the need to control those beings, of course. For this, they conquer.<br /> <br /> (Will crunch when I have pdf and am off phone).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 09-08-2017, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T20:02:40-07:00","id":1139339,"title":"","content":"<b>Grue Drone:</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Quote:</b> [<i>All. Hail. Meta-Mind.</i>]<br /> <br /> <b>Background: </b>Grue are not born with souls, under normal circumstances. As a testament to the deadliness and occult nature of their home, the vast majority are spawned (congealed, really) from &quot;gestation reservoirs&quot; (it's extremely offensive to call them pits), free of higher consciousness, being little more intelligence than extremely tame and cunning chimpanzees. The evolutionary strategy on the homeworld was that drones are decoys for the actually sentient Grue, serving as a way to feed predators psychic junk food until they were full or starved to death. Today, the drones are an easy source of cheap labor and muscle for their metamorph elders, and while they cannot shapeshift out of humanoid form, they don't need mastery of shapeshifting to utilize opposable thumbs or know how to aim a gun. And being able to imitate, say, a janitor makes them easy enough to smuggle in or serve as security.<br /> <br /> <b>Description: </b>In their true forms, Grue drones resemble all other Grue; androgynous, red-skinned, mouthless humanoids with eyes that, while they have comparable structures to sclera, are so pale they appear solid white until closer inspection. Drones can be distinguished from their metamorph superiors by their voices (for lack of of a better term, but it affects them when speaking in a disguise as well), which are halting and monotone; like parrots, drones do not have full communicative cognizance, and while they can pick up the basic context of words, they don't really understand them well and can't carry a conversation. In areas the Grue walk openly, their masters dress them in colorful uniforms meant to impress, with the Grue Unity symbol (the dim sun of their homeworld surrounded by five stars) displayed prominently.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints: </b>Metamorphs are not instinctively inclined to view drones as something worthy of care-their literal biological function is as cannon fodder. As a result, they are little more than muscle for the rest of the species. At most, their larval states are viewed as interesting pets if unusually intelligent, and most of <i>those </i>are the ones nearing Cultivation (ie, maturation into a metamorph). That being said, they're very disciplined and effective muscle, and their cunning, while animalistic, is quite capable of understanding the concept of ambushes, cover, and luring your opponent into a false sense of security (especially since drones are not instinctively attached to their own lives too much, if it protects the &quot;nest&quot; of the area they guard, metamorphs, or what the Omnifarious tells them is the Unity's plans). Their real weakness, as the Ban implies, is a lack of personal direction; without the Omnifarious to direct them, drones default to primal, instinctive behavior, usually to run away in confusion and panic and hide until the group mind is restablished.<br /> <br /> <b>Best At:</b> Ambushes, Disguises that don't require speaking, Feral melee onslaught, Shooting (Five Dice)<br /> <br /> <b>Worst At:</b> Pretending to be sentient, Understanding non-Grue language, Acting on own initiative (Chance Die)<br /> <br /> <b>All Others:</b> 2<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Chameleon Horror, Drain, Mortal Mask<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> Drones need the Omnifarious in order to function, and they panic when it is not present. If someone blocks the group mind in an area, all drones promptly lose the ability to take Mental actions,or communicate telepathically, even with other Grue (as they cannot hear the emotional emphasis in the &quot;words&quot;, and so have no ability to contextualize said &quot;words&quot;), and take a -2 penalty to all contested actions, including combat. This, understandably, wreaks hell on any plans.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T13:35:01-08:00","id":1168904,"title":"","content":"<b>The Voice In The Phone </b><br /> <br /> <b>Best At: </b>10 (Knowing What You Want, Bringing Out The Very Worst In You, Terrible And Subtle Murders)<br /> <b>Worst At:</b> 2 (Holding A Normal Conversation)<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Get Rid Of People You Hate<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 6<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 10<br /> <b>Durability:</b> 5<br /> <b>Size:</b> 1<br /> <b>Structure:</b> 6<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Eye Spy, Immortal, Influence (Hate 1), Know Soul, Miracle (Murder Only), Numen (Implant Mission, Sign)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T20:39:04-08:00","id":1169264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1168904#post1168904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Voice In The Phone </b><br /> <br /> <b>Best At: </b>10 (Knowing What You Want, Bringing Out The Very Worst In You, Terrible And Subtle Murders)<br /> <b>Worst At:</b> 2 (Holding A Normal Conversation)<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Get Rid Of People You Hate<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 6<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 10<br /> <b>Durability:</b> 5<br /> <b>Size:</b> 1<br /> <b>Structure:</b> 6<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Eye Spy, Immortal, Influence (Hate 1), Know Soul, Miracle (Murder Only), Numen (Implant Mission, Sign)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You had me at <b>Best At:</b> &quot;Bring Out The Very Worst In You&quot; but then you go on to make the disembodied voice Immortal and have Miracle (Murder Only)? Slow impressed clap for you, and +1 Internet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T09:38:52-08:00","id":1170202,"title":"","content":"Its been a while, so here are a few new Horrors <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Dimensional Shambler</b></span><br /> The enigmatic creatures known to occult scholars as \u201cDimensional Shamblers\u201d are creatures that can seemingly shift between varies planes of existence with relative ease. Their behavior is strange; they have been observed stealing items or abducting individuals and then vanishing with the items or persons taken. The reasoning for this behavior, and the ultimate fate of that which was taken is unknown. It is theorized that the creatures have a previously undiscovered \u201cnative\u201d dimension, but there has been no proof of this thus far. The beings are insect-like, with leathery, carapaced hide and elongated forelimbs that give it an apish bearing. Its dull, black eyes convey little emotion and have never spoken or otherwise communicated during any documented encounter.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Curiosity; <b>Vice</b>: Enigmatic<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To Explore and Collect<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 6, Dexterity 4, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 4<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 3(Grapple), Intimidate 3, Larceny 2, Occult (Dimensions) 2, Science 2, Stealth 3 (Ambush), Survival 3 (Navigation)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Grappling), Indomitable, Iron Skin 1 (Advanced), Style: Grappling 2, Trained Observer<br /> <br /> <b>Potency:</b> 3<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 1<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 14 (Species 4)<br /> <b>Health:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Talons [+0L melee; 9 dice]<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> <b><i>Dimensional Travel</i></b>, Madness &amp; Terror, Surprise Entrance<br /> <br /> <b>Dimension Travel:</b> This Dread Power is unique to the Dimensional Shambler, and allows them to move from one realm of existence to another with ease. By spending 3 Willpower, the creature can move into a roughly analogous location in a different realm of existence (such as the Hedge, the Primordial Dream, the Shadow, the Underworld, etc.) It takes the Shambler a full round to complete the transition. By spending an additional 1 Willpower, the Shambler can carry items or Grappled opponents with it when it travels (such items or individual can be no larger than Size 6).<br /> </div></div> </div> </div> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Invaders from Beyond</span></b><br /> \u201cInvaders from Beyond\u201d are creatures intent on taking over the Earth and have begun a campaign of infiltration in preparation for a full-scale invasion. The exact aims of the beings are unknown, and theories ranging from a desire to exploits Earth\u2019s resources to using humanity to jump-start their own stagnant evolution have been put forward. In their natural forms, they are thin gray-skinned beings, with dark eyes, enlarged craniums, and somewhat skeletal faces. They use their advanced technology to masquerade as humans and have infiltrated nearly every strata of human society to prepare the way for global conquest.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Cautious; <b>Vice:</b> Entitled<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Subjugate Humanity<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 4, Composure 4<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2, Athletics 1, Computer 3(Hacking), Crafts 2(Technology), Drive 2, Firearms 3(Blaster), Medicine 2, Science 3, Subterfuge 2 (Disguise)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Alternate Identity 2, Area of Expertise (Disguise, Technology), Indomitable, Untouchable<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 3<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 11<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee; 3 dice]<br /> Energy Blaster [+2L ranged; Initiative -2, AP 2, 8 dice]<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Pierce Mind, Regenerate, Skin-Taker<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T10:24:20-08:00","id":1170221,"title":"","content":"Granted, I'm not particularly knowledgeable about BtP, but wouldn't the Primordial Dream lack any ties to geographical locations in the material?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T10:31:33-08:00","id":1170227,"title":"","content":"What would be a good Dread Power to simulate mechanical beings? I was thinking of doing a robotic swarm (like Mousers from TMNT) as a Horde.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T10:50:25-08:00","id":1170230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1170221#post1170221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted, I'm not particularly knowledgeable about BtP, but wouldn't the Primordial Dream lack any ties to geographical locations in the material?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whenever a Mortal loses Integrity in an encounter with the supernatural, the event creates a Chamber within the Primordial Dream that reflects its immediate surroundings. The full extent of Dream geography has not been published yet, but we know that at least this overlap exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T11:21:48-08:00","id":1170240,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Primordial Pathways</b><br /> <br /> In addition to what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7593_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7593\" data-vbnamecard=\"7593\">Teatime</a> mentioned, a Hero has access to a Gift called &quot;Open Gate&quot; that allows it to intrude into Beasts Lair. While I might need to revise the language, the general idea is that if there is a Realm presented in the Chronicles of Darkness that can be physically accessed, then the Shambler can get there.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Dread Powers from Mechanical Creatures</b><br /> <br /> The following is a selection of powers that work well with Horrors that have a Technological Theme. Most are from the core book, but those marked with an asterisk are from Werewolf the Forsaken 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> *Armored Hide [Armor Plating]<br /> Chameleon Horror [light bending technology]<br /> Discorporate [Modular design with many independent units]<br /> Eye Spy [Surveillance Drones and Security Override systems]<br /> Gremlin [Remote Control and Direct EMP weapons]<br /> Immortal [Backup Programs and chassis]<br /> *Interface [Link up with Computers and other Devices]<br /> *Juggernaut [sledgehammer fists and reinforced frame]<br /> *Monstrous Resilience [mechanical creatures do not feel pain or discomfort]<br /> Natural Weapons [Implements to crush, stab and slice]<br /> Numen - Blast [Ranged Weapon Systems]<br /> Prodigeous Leap [Hydraulic Legs or Rocket Boosters]<br /> Regenerate [Automated Repair system]<br /> Reality Stutter [Teleportation]<br /> Snare [Non-lethal Containment Weapons]<br /> *Swift [Mechanical Precision and Speed]<br /> Unbreakable [Mechanical durability]<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T00:41:02-08:00","id":1171477,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:24px\">Eyeling</span><br /> It appears to be a pale blue human eye that is crawling around on its blood red optical nerve like it was a set of tentacles tucked away in a corner on a shelf above you out of normal line of sight. It notices you noticing it and it <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ParanoiaFuel\" target=\"_blank\">shimmers as it disappears</a>...<br /> <b>Image:</b><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1HfsPZm5kkoQTKoyemL-91RUET2tlvDIc/view?usp=sharing\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1HfsPZm5kkoQTKoyemL-91RUET2tlvDIc/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Hfs...ew?usp=sharing</a> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b><img src=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1HfsPZm5kkoQTKoyemL-91RUET2tlvDIc/view?usp=sharing\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>Stats:</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Best At: </b>5 (Devouring Supernal Magic by being a witness that causes a Paradox/Dissonance, Seeing through the Eyeling Hivemind, Being Unseen)<br /> <b>Worst At:</b> Chance Die (Communicating, Overpowering others, Inflicting Damage Directly)<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> See secrets, Devouring Supernal Magic by being a witness that causes a Paradox/Dissonance<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 2<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 10<br /> <b>Durability:</b> 5<br /> <b>Size:</b> 1<br /> <b>Structure:</b> 6<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Eye Spy (Can see what other Eyelings can See) , Miracle [by shoving a captured eye into your own empty eye socket you gain the ability to sometimes see through Eyeling's eye Granting the Merit Contact: Eyelings, and a level of semi-telepathic connection to the Eyeling in your head giving you the Merit Retainer 4: The Eyeling in your Head &lt;Three Retainer Skills: Investigate, Occult, and the third skill is it counts as a Sleeper Witness for a Paradox/Dissonance purposes for any spell that is in its line of vision&gt; at the cost of permanently losing a Personal Aspiration], Chameleon Horror<br /> <br /> Please note this is an Abyssal Creature, for where that matters.<br /> <br /> (Counts as an aware Sleeper Witness for a Paradox/Dissonance for any spell that is in its line of vision)</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T01:12:35-08:00","id":1171970,"title":"","content":"What if you don't want to use all the splat books but want to have werewolves, vampires, wizards/witches, and/or fae in your setting, with greatly simplified rules?<br /> <br /> <b>Feel free to try these generic monsters!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Werewolf</span></b><br /> This hulking nine-foot tall wolf headed wolf-man has thick fur, rippling muscles, and rending talons when in its natural form but can appear as it did while it was still human. It is thought the transformation is caused when a suitable human is exposed to supernatural predation and survives after being maimed on a night of a full moon. It seems to be a bit of a localized spiritual immune response to a supernatural ecology out of balance as restoring balance to the supernatural ecology and protecting its territory become its driving goals.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Horror Type:</b> Lone Terror<br /> <b>Best Dice Pool:</b> 10, Tracking, Brutally killing, Chasing<br /> <b>Worst Dice Pool:</b> 2 Remaining calm, Empathizing with non-predators, Resisting primal instincts<br /> <b>All Other Pools:</b> 5<br /> <b>Aspirations: </b>Kill those trespassing on Territory, Hunt those disrupting the local supernatural ecology<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Madness and Terror (Via Howl), Hunter's Senses ('Trespassers'), Home Ground (Territory), Regenerate, Unbreakable, Natural Weapons (Fang/Claw), Numen-Mortal Mask (Being Human isn't their true form, and while disguised as humans each has at least one classic lycanthropy Tells, though it vairies by individual)<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Silver<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 6</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Vampire Lord</b></span><br /> The mature stage of undead vampirism, where they are capable of creating others of their own kind, this happens after having been a Vampire Minion under another Vampire Lord, being released and then maturing as an Independant Vampire. Vampire Lords are no Longer able to feed directly from mortals and must feed from other vampires or superaturals, and thus normally feed by proxy through their Vampire Minions.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Horror Type:</b> Lone Terror<br /> <b>Best Dice Pool:</b> 10 Seducing others into their control, Crushing enemies, Executing subtle mechination<br /> <b>Worst Dice Pool:</b> 2 Acting in the day, acting while confronted with Banes<br /> <b>All Other Pools:</b> 5<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Maintain masquerade concealing vampire existence from humanity, Entrench personal influence in the mortal world, Drain supernatural beings<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Numen-Drain(Sucking through skin), Soul Thief (Having Drained all Willpower), Immortal (Resurrection Clause: Blood spilt on their ashes), Discorporate, Hypnotic Gaze, Mist form, Unbreakable<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Sunlight, Fire<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 6</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Independent Vampire</b></span><br /> This is a former Vampire Minion that has been released by their Vampire Lord, but has not yet matured into a Vampire Lord themselves yet.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Horror Type:</b> Horde<br /> <b>Best Dice Pool:</b> 7 Enacting their preferred feeding method, Executing subtle mechination<br /> <b>Worst Dice Pool:</b> 1 Acting in the day, acting while confronted with Banes<br /> <b>All Other Pools:</b> 3<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Maintain masquerade concealing vampire existence from humanity, Entrench personal influence in the mortal world, Drain mortals<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Numen-Drain(Sucking through skin), Soul Thief (Having Drained all Willpower), Immortal (Resurrection Clause: Blood spilt on their ashes), Hypnotic Gaze, Unbreakable<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Sunlight, Fire<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 3</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Vampire Minion</b></span><br /> Those Soulless killed by Vampire Lords and fed the Vampire Lords blood are made into its minions, loyal and eager slaves to its will and appetites. Should the Vampire Lord release them, a very rare act, they may after a century mature into a Vampire Lord themselves.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Horror Type:</b> Minion<br /> <b>Best Dice Pool:</b> 5 Enacting their preferred feeding method, Obeying commands of a Vampire Lord<br /> <b>Worst Dice Pool:</b> Chance Acting in the day, acting while confronted with Banes, Actively disobeying a Vampire Lord<br /> <b>All Other Pools:</b> 2<br /> Aspirations: Receive praise from Vampire Lord, Drain mortals<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Numen-Drain(Sucking through skin), Soul Thief (Having Drained all Willpower), Immortal (Resurrection Clause: A Vampire Lord's blood spilt on their ashes)<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Sunlight, Fire<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 2</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Wizard/Witch</b></span><br /> Those whom uncovered mystical secret so great as to warrant the title of wizard or witch are still human, though often their great power corrupts them towards dark self serving ends.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Horror Type:</b> Lone Terror<br /> <b>Best Dice Pool:</b> 10 Knowing obscure knowledge, Methodical ritualistic use of magic that takes a scene per power to use<br /> <b>Worst Dice Pool:</b> 2 Physical combat, Improvisational use of dread powers in as little as a turn<br /> <b>All Other Pools:</b> 5<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Study supernatural secrets, Wield power over the mortal world<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Eye Spy (Via Scying prop), Gremlin, Miracle, Surprise Entrance, Numen-Implant Mission, Numen-Omen Trance<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 6</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Fetch</b></span><br /> The replacement of a human being by a denizen of Faerie is called a Fetch. This appear via Surprise Entrance into a scene where the replaced person was exacted after a non-faerie enters the land of Faerie.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Horror Type:</b> Minion<br /> <b>Best Dice Pool:</b> 5 Impersonating the replaced person for aquaintances, Cause emotional distress to those that care about person replaced<br /> <b>Worst Dice Pool:</b> Chance Fooling those that truely love the replaced person<br /> <b>All Other Pools:</b> 2<br /> <b>Aspirations: </b>Impersonate the person they are replacing, Ensure the populace at large does realize the person it is impersonating has been replaced<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Numen-Mortal Mask (Is a sickly copy of the person replaced; The Tell is that it must answer ancient riddles when certain strange actions are taken in front of them, as according to certain folk lore), Madness and Terror (through revealing its true form or crying/wailing/bawling [This second one only affect people whom were intimate with the person it is replacing] ), Surprise Entrance (Any scene where the person it is replacing is expected in)<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 2<br /> &quot;Intimate&quot; applies to deep bonds, Mentors would apply, sometimes fellow PC if appropriate, some types of Retainers, and NPC who was a True Friend</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Unseelie Host</span></b><br /> These faerie fly through the night sky as dark silhouettes, snatching those they can for the land of Faerie, sometimes leaving a Fetch, other times not.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Horror Type:</b> Horde<br /> <b>Best Dice Pool:</b> 7 Chase people outside at night, Snaring people with Shadows, Scaring people<br /> <b>Worst Dice Pool:</b> 1 Acts of kindness, Anything when exposed to cold Iron or bright lights<br /> <b>All Other Pools:</b> 3<br /> Aspirations: Capture travelers at night, Fly through the night sky, Inspire fear<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Mist Form (A dark shadow flying through the air), Snare (Shadowy grasp projected over them), Hunter Senses (Lone Travelers at night), Immortal (Ressurection Clause: The rising of the New Moon), Maze (On those Ensnared, actually pulls them within the Unseelie Host, and finding an exit leads creepy sinister unseelie portions of Faerie realms)<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Cold Iron<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 3</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Faerie Lord/Ladies</b></span><br /> Faerie Lords come in two distinct flavors, neither of which have human sensibilities, Seelie and Unseelie. Faerie Lords or Ladies are the royalty in the land of Faerie and have dominion over lesser fae beings. Beings from Faerie are capricious and see humans as play-things or food, which which is worse being dependent on exactly what &quot;play-thing&quot; means to the particular faerie. When Faerie Lords or Ladies abduct those from the mortal realm they always bid a Fetch to take their place.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Horror Type:</b> Lone Terror<br /> <b>Best Dice Pool:</b> 10 Being inhumanly perfect, Being inhumanly cruel, Executing convoluted mechination<br /> <b>Worst Dice Pool:</b> 2 True empathy for others, Anything while touching Cold Iron<br /> <b>All Other Pools:</b> 5<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Immortal (Ressurection Clause: Either the Spring Equinox or Summer Solstice for Seelie, or Autumn Equinox or Winter Solstice for Unseelie), Miracle (Must be made as a Bargain with a Mortal), Numen-Awe, Numen-Hallucination (They call it Glamour), Numen-Mortal Mask (Tell is their shadow/reflection shows their true form), Home Ground (Land of Faerie), Maze (actually pulls them within the Unseelie Host, and finding an exit leads either unseelie or seelie portions of Faerie realms, depending on the type of Faerie Lord/Lady)<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Cold Iron<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 6</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 12-31-2017, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T20:29:58-08:00","id":1176449,"title":"","content":"A few new ideas that popped into my head <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Cultist of the Deep</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Certain individuals given to the worship of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1055417#post1055417\">unnameable things</a> begin to manifest physiological and mental aberrations ranging from the subtly off-putting to the inhumanly grotesque. These Cultist often congregate insular communities, where their practices can go unnoticed by the population at large for generations. At best, their lineages will eventual die out, rendered sterile and impotent over time. At worst, they can infect entire bloodlines with curious traits, and vile habits.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Loyalty; <b>Vice:</b> Fanaticism<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To venerate blasphemous Entities<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 2<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 1(Swim), Brawl 2(Grapple),Intimidate 2, Investigation 1, Larceny 2, Occult 2(Cult Rituals), Subterfuge 2, Streetwise 1(Isolated Community),Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Hardy 2, Mystery Cult Initiation 2, Striking Looks 1 (Weird)<br /> <br /> <b>Potency:</b> 2<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 5<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 1<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee; 6 dice]<br /> Club [+1L melee;-1 Initiative; 6 dice]<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Armored Hide, Home Ground (Isolated Village), Jump Scare </div></div> </div> </div></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>High Priestess of the Apocalypse</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">She remembers a time where she cut the hearts from virgins tied to stone alters, and wrote odes to the Gods in their blood. In her time she has led cults of utopian idealists as often she has led as sinister cabals rife with depravity. They all end the same way; blood, fire, torment, death. Then she begins again.<br /> The High Priestess of the Apocalypse has worn many names of the centuries, and builds cults gathering the lost and the gullible. She has been granted immortality for her service, and wields powers gathered over the course of countless lifetimes. All of this is done to perpetuate her immortality and to feed souls to the dark pantheons she venerates. One day, her Gods will rise and drown the world in a tide of blood. But until that blessed day, she will do what she must to advance their agenda.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Ambition; <b>Vice:</b> Misanthropy<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To bring about the End of Days<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 5, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 6, Dexterity 5, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 6, Manipulation 6, Composure 5<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 4, Athletics 2, Brawl 3, Intimidate 3, Occult 6 (Apocalypse), Persuasion 5(Indoctrination), Socialize 4(Cults), Subterfuge 5, Weaponry 3<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Mystery Cult Initiation 5, Sacrificial Offering 5, Staff 3(Cult Members)<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 6<br /> <b>Willpower</b>: 16<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 10<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee; 9 dice]<br /> Knife [+0L melee;-1 Initiative; 9 dice]<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Madness&amp; Terror, Immortal, Regeneration 1, Soul Thief </div></div> </div> </div></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 03-18-2018, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T04:54:00-08:00","id":1180667,"title":"","content":"I don't know if you've already mined this for ideas, but <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fearsome_critters\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> are a few. Some seem almost ideal for Cryptids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T17:13:54-08:00","id":1184140,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Fearsome Critters</b><br /> <br /> Nice! An entire section of folklore I was previously unfamiliar with! I will absorb it and see what it inspires.<br /> <br /> And here is a new horror! <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Project Einherjar</b></span><br /> \u201cProject Einherjar\u201d was an off-the-books program conducted government agencies researching next-generation augmentations and enhancements to create soldiers for the battlefields of the future. The test subjects were high-performing and elite soldiers, critically injured in the line of duty. Declared \u201ckilled in action\u201d, these soldiers were mentally and physically transformed with electronic and mechanical cybernetics, granting them strength, speed and endurance far beyond human limits. Their minds were altered to have little little cognizance beyond the current mission, and to remember nothing of their prior lives. The first several sorties of these augmented warriors proved promising, but increasing behavioral instability made the augmented soldiers violently unpredictable. The project was canceled and the soldiers were slated be be destroyed when the transport carrying the eight remaining subjects in cryogenic stasis disappeared. Those responsible for the expensive and deeply illegal program are actively searching for the missing subjects.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Obedient; <b>Vice:</b> Erratic<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Complete the Mission<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 5, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 7, Dexterity 5, Stamina 6<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 1, Composure 4<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 3(Run), Brawl 4, Crafts 2(Demolitions), Drive 2, Firearms 4(Assault Rifle), Intimidate 3, Stealth 3, Survival 3(Tracking), Weaponry 2 (Knife)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Indomitable, Iron Stamina 3, Professional Training 4 (Soldier; Athletics, Firearms, Survival), Style: Firefight 2, Trained Observer<br /> <br /> <b>Potency:</b> 4<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 13<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 3/4<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <b>Speed</b>: 20<br /> <b>Health:</b> 11<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Gains the <i>Insane</i> Tilt when one of their three rightmost Health boxes has damage marked<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0L melee; 11 dice]<br /> Assault Rifle [+3L ranged, -3 Initiative; 10 dice]<br /> Combat Knife [+1L melee, -1 Initiative; 10 dice]<br /> <b>Dread Powers*:</b> <i><b>Alternate Composition</b></i>* (Cyborg), Monstrous Resilience, Prodigious Leap<br /> <br /> <b>Alternate Composition:</b> As the Cryptid Adaptation [Demon: the Descent, pg. 230]. The subjects of Project Einherjar have had their limbs, spine, lower torso and most of their internal organs replaced with mechanical parts. In addition, their skeletons and remaining musculature have been reinforced and significant surgical modifications have been made to their brain and eyes. The overall changes grant Armor 3/ 4 and they are considered to always have access to the <i>Gas Mask</i>, <i>Night Vision Goggles</i>, and <i>Smartphone</i> equipment.<br /> <br /> <i>*Exchanged 1 Dread power for 3 dots of Merits. </i></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T21:33:30-08:00","id":1184238,"title":"","content":"Interesting if Project Einherjar is connected too Task Force VALKYRIE...<b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T22:08:21-08:00","id":1184245,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Project Einherjar</b><br /> <br /> I wanted to make a Horror that filled the &quot;Cybernetic Killing Machine&quot; trope. This is one part &quot;Robocop&quot;, one part &quot;HITMark&quot;, and a solid helping of &quot;Metal Gear Revengence&quot;.<br /> I intentionally gave the project a Norse Mythology name so anyone who uses this Horror can draw a connection to Task Force Valkarie if they wish- perhaps rather than soldiers the subjects could be TFV hunters killed in action, but not quite ready to end their Vigil.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T02:14:40-08:00","id":1184300,"title":"","content":"Neat, I think you succeeded. Maybe it should have some sort of datajack or onboard CPU, so it can do general tracking down of the people who would run away from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T23:25:05-08:00","id":1185835,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Project Einherjar</b><br /> <br /> I could add a few more tricks to these, but I will leave nuances like tracking programs and the like up to the needs of the campaign.<br /> <br /> New Horror Below <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Cain</b></span><br /> While it is unlikely that he was the first man to slay another, murder has dogged the steps of the creature named Cain for millennia. The legends surrounding him have grown and been distorted by time. What is true is that he was once a farmer that killed his brother and was cursed for this deed to walk the earth for eternity. And he has walked; from a time thousands of years before the start of recorded history, through the rise and fall of civilizations, through periods of warfare, disaster, peace and enlightenment. In his time he has been both penitent and monster and visited every corner of the earth known to man and beyond. In in all times and all places, he leaves death in his wake.<br /> For the last 30 years, Cain has lived in isolation on a secluded farm in rural Kansas, finding a small measure of peace in the solitude. Cain has hard to place features, belonging to an ethnicity long extinct. He appears to be an athletic man in early middle age of average height (he was considered quite tall in his day). He has dark eyes, a dark complexion, and wears his graying hair long and his beard full.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Philosophical; <b>Vice:</b> Weary<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To End His Curse<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 7, Wits 5, Resolve 7<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 7, Dexterity 5, Stamina 7<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 6 Manipulation 5, Composure 6<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 6(History), Athletics 3, Brawl 6, Crafts 3, Firearms 3, Intimidate 4(Ancient), Occult 5(Curses), Stealth 4(Hunting), Subterfuge 3, Survival 4(Farming), Weaponry 4(Knife)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Anonymity 4, Defensive Combat, Encyclopedic Knowledge (Occult), Hardy 2, Holistic Awareness, Indomitable, Iron Stamina 2, Untouchable<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 8<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 21<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 11<br /> <b>Defense</b>: 11<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 19<br /> <b>Health:</b> 12<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must claim a human life or consume human flesh once a month or gain the <i>Deprived</i> Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0L melee; 13 dice]<br /> Flint Knife [+1L melee, -1 Initiative; 12 dice]<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> <i>Elusive</i>, Immortal, Monstrous Resilience, Regenerate 2, Swift<br /> <br /> <b><i>Elusive:</i></b> Creatures with this dread power only ever appear on camera as a blurred silhouette of their actual shape. Humanoid monsters can easily be mistaken for humans or upright bears, while unusually large creatures blend into the scenery. Humans have a hard time remembering exact detail about creatures they encounter. Rolls to accurately describe or recall such events are made at a \u20133 modifier. </div></div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T01:59:00-08:00","id":1185854,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:24px\">Tooth Fairy</span><br /> These gossamer-winged sloped-headed almond-eyed teal-skinned denizens of Faerie crave teeth and often exchange coins they find from sifting through place humans tend to lose or toss them into,such as in couches or within wishing fountains when interacting with humans whom believe in fairies and have left their teeth in a place for this purpose. The ugly side of the Tooth Fairies' demeanor is when they are confronted by someone who doesn't hold the proper respect or awe for them, the sprite tend to spitefully snatch that being's teeth from their face as soon as the offensive being opens their mouth, and then carry the teeth back to Faerie. Given Tooth Fairies can become a mist to enter a home, and even if struck down trying to exit they transform into a swarm still capable of carrying its prize with it, they almost always fulfill their Aspirations.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Horror Type:</b> Minion<br /> <b>Best Dice Pool:</b> 5 Attacking for Damage in a Swarm, Snatching all the teeth from a being's open mouth with single swipe of the hand while in full size solid form, Sneaking into and out of homes<br /> <b>Worst Dice Pool:</b> Chance Doing anything during the day, Doing anything while in contact with Cold Iron<br /> <b>All Other Pools:</b> 2<br /> <b>Aspirations: </b>Trade coins for teeth with respectful believers, Steal teeth from disrespectful unbelievers, Keep the teeth hidden and safe in lair<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Discorporate (into a swarm of hornet sized Tooth Fairy, each able to carry merely a single human molar), Hunter Sense's (Teeth and any creature that currently has teeth), Mist Form<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Cold Iron<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 2<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-14-2018, 05:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T02:21:52-08:00","id":1185858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1185854#post1185854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\">Tooth Fairy</span><br /> These gossamer-winged sloped-headed almond-eyed teal-skinned denizens of Faerie crave teeth and often exchange coins they find from sifting through place humans tend to lose or place them,such as couches or within wishing fountains when interacting with humans which believe in them and have left their teeth in a place for this purpose. The ugly side of their demeanor is when they are confronted by someone who doesn't hold the proper respect or awe for them, they spitefully tend to snatch that being's teeth from their face as soon as they open their mouth, and then carry them back to Faerie. Given they can become a mist to enter a home, and even if struck down trying to exit they transform into a swarm still capable of carrying its prize with it.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Horror Type:</b> Minion<br /> <b>Best Dice Pool:</b> 5 Attacking for Damage in a Swarm, Snatching all the teeth from a being's open mouth with single swipe of the hand while in full size solid form, Sneaking into and out of homes<br /> <b>Worst Dice Pool:</b> Chance Doing anything during the day, <br /> <b>All Other Pools:</b> 2<br /> <u>Aspirations: Receive praise from Vampire Lord, Drain mortals</u><br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Discorporate (into a swarm of hornet sized Tooth Fairy, each able to carry merely a single human molar), Hunter Sense's (Teeth and any creature that currently has teeth), Mist Form<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Cold Iron<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 2<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Copy+Paste error?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T02:25:26-08:00","id":1185859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1185858#post1185858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Copy+Paste error?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. I've since edited it. Also fixed the pronoun vagueness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-14-2018, 05:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T17:47:40-08:00","id":1188352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Festival by H.P. Lovecraft</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The nethermost caverns...are not for the fathoming of eyes that see; for their marvels are strange and terrific. Cursed the ground where dead thoughts live new and oddly bodied, and evil the mind that is held by no head. Wisely did Ibn Schacabao say, that happy is the tomb where no wizard hath lain, and happy the town at night whose wizards are all ashes. For it is of old rumour that the soul of the devil-bought hastes not from his charnel clay, but fats and instructs the very Worms that gnaws; till out of corruption horrid life springs, and the dull scavengers of earth wax crafty to vex it and swell monstrous to plague it. Great holes secretly are digged where earth's pores ought to suffice, and things have learnt to walk that ought to crawl.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worms that Walk are Horrors that originate when a Mage with Wisdom lower than 5 dies with an unresolved Abyssal Imago Paradox Condition and whose body is allowed to fester, rot, and feed loathsome wriggling invertebrates. The Worms that Walks that arises from such a Mage is a Horror with as much Potency as the Mage had Gnosis, and has the memories/identity/consciousness of the Mage which spawned it, with the normal limitation of stats of a Horror of that Potency, meaning they will likely lose Attributes, Skills and Merits. Quite frequently being reduced to a Worms that Walks greatly strips a Mage of much of their power and even their most basic abilities, and what fragments of themselves that they do retain heavily leans towards the purely mental. Their consciousness reconstitutes by sliding back from the Abyss through the Taint of their corpse being collected within the living bodies of the worms and maggots that devour their remains. Pursuing the Obsessions they had before their death becomes their only Aspirations as a Worms that Walks, and their Anchors tend to remain the same or become more extreme versions of themselves. All Worms that Walk find themselves as high ranking Members of the Cult of Yonder as their Merit points will allow, which takes priority over any other way those Merits could be used to reflect what remains of the individual the Worms that Walks once was. Worms that Walk find the Cult of Yonder instinctive and innately comforting and their alien mind copes far better than those who did not undergo a transformation of consciousness like they did making it easy for them to rise to the top. Worms that Walk come back with no Wisdom nor Integrity to moderate its most heinous curiosities to reflect how the Abyss has warped its perspective into something wholly inhuman and alien even if it has most of the memories it had in life. All Worms that Walk have the Been Yonder [Persistent] Condition.<br /> <br /> Because universally Worms that Walk cause paradox as if they were a crowd of Sleeper witnesses they find reconnecting with former associates to resume studying their obsession, even if their associates wouldn't be phased by their new form. Also being driven to study Mysteries with a lack of Mage Sight or any of their Arcanum they are frequently frustrated and profoundly bitter, to say nothing of their writhing envy of still living Mages. Remembering the glory of Supernal Truth and being reduced to a being whose very nature is that of being Untrue more profoundly than the Lie is a jagged caustic pill to swallow. Worms that Walk have a single respite of their eternal life as a pile of maggots and worms and that is while they Astrally Travel or Dream they appear as they did in life, though they retain all their current Dread Powers. This has lead some to maintain former relationships through this state and others as a way to keep key allies of their pet projects in a position to assist them.<br /> <br /> While the Potency and other stats are roughly derived from the Mage (or rarely other type of unlucky being) whose corpse the Worms that Walks has risen from,but the Dread Powers gained by increased Potency follow the same pattern of priority regardless of what the character was capable of in life. Potency has a minimum of 1, and increases by 1 for every Gnosis, Primal Urge, Blood Potency, Wyrd, or Synergy the Major Template has beyond one.<br /> <br /> The three following Dread Powers every work that walks has is as follows:<ul><li>Discorporate (Worms and Bugs),</li> <li>Immortal (Resurrection Clause: Any organic object with a Strong temporal or spacial sympathetic connection to the dead Mage is fed to invertebrates appropriate to create a Worms that Walks)</li> <li>Presence of Paradox* (may not be turned off)</li> </ul>They gain the follow Dread Powers in the following Order:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Surprise Entrance (Suddenly Forming Out of Bugs and Worms to Enter the Scene)</li> <li>Jump Scare</li> <li>Burrow (WtF 2e Pg210)</li> <li>Eye Spy (Through invertebrates that once were part of the body)</li> <li>Beast Master (Except it Applies to Abyssal Horrors of animal Intelligence which are elephant size or smaller)</li> </ol>*=Abyssal Aspects and (Numina See Below)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/925972-2e-abyssal-aspects-and-numina?p=926097#post926097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[B]<br /> <b>Presence of Paradox</b><br /> The ephemeral being is thoroughly tainted by the stuff of the Abyss - treat it as if it were an entire crowd of Sleepers for the purposes of calculating Paradox dice pools, except it adds dice equal to its Rank rather than just one. In addition, it may spend Essence reflexively to cancel Mana spent to mitigate a Paradox dice pool on a one-to-one basis.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Example:</b> Jaquelyn Quixote, former Obrimos Silver Ladder<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 2, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 1, Dexterity 1, Stamina 1<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 1, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 3, Computers 1, Occult 4(Abyssal Blasphemies)<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Brawl 1<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Subterfuge 1<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Mystery Cult Initiation (Cult of the Yonder) 3, Dream 1, Familiar 2 (Jaquelyn's Invasiveness)<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 1<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Invasive (Formerly Curious)<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Fanatical (Formerly Stubborn)<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Map out the local leylines and other relevant occult phenomena.<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 4<br /> <b>Defense:</b><br /> <b>Speed:</b> 7<br /> <b>Health:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Attack</b> <b>Type</b> <b>Dice</b> <b>Special Effects</b><br /> Melee Grappling 2 Dice If within a grapple with a Worms that Walks a person without Tolerance for Biology must succeed a Roll of either Composure or Stamina, which ever is lower, or gain the Moderate Sick Tilt,<br /> Melee Overpower 2 Dice If the Target whose in a grapple with the Worms that Walks already has the Moderate Sick and the Worms that Walks succeed an overpower maneuver instead of normal damage it upgrades the Sick Tilt from Moderate to Grave.<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Discorporate (Worms), Immortal (Resurrection Clause: Any organic object with a Strong temporal or spacial sympathetic connection to the dead Mage is fed to invertebrates appropriate to create a Worms that Walks), Presence of Paradox*<br /> <br /> <b>JaqueLyn's Invasiveness (Rank 1 Acamoth)</b><br /> Crawling through Geotia's spectrum of Twilight is a squirming foot long centipede whose back and stomach plates are little multiple repeating fleshy faces of the same young girl whose countenance is frantically contorting in bug-eyed agony, and whose legs look like little human thumbs. Only as it slithers through something solid do you notice a flicker of expression on the little faces as they enter, which seems to be momentary near-orgasmic relief. It is disgustingly clear that it enjoys getting into places it shouldn't.<br /> <b>Power:</b> 3<br /> <b>Finesse:</b> 4<br /> <b>Resistance:</b> 1<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Twilight Form, Familiar<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Invasiveness 1<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Pathfinder. Rapture, Implant Mission<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must earnestly attempt to enter anything commanded to stay out of<br /> <b>Size:</b> 1<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 2<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 5<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 5<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 10/<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/799082-cofd-diy-mystery-cults?p=1279858#post1279858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had this mystery cult within a Horror Show entry, I am moving it here and quoting it there for ease of future reference<br /> <br /> <b>Cult of the Yonder</b><br /> Beyond all reality is the Abyss, a nonexistence that contains everything possible and impossible all constantly contradicting itself in a roiling chaos of stagnant abeyance. Members of the Cult of the Yonder universally have been in the Abyss either mentally or with their whole being. If the cult member is fortunate the way they entered the Abyss will be an event that transforms them into a creature which is no longer human in mindset(such as a being without Wisdom nor Integrity), so they don't suffer the negative affects of the Been Yonder [Persistent] Condition. This leads the Cult of the Yonder to be filled with the shaken, spooked, guilty, broken, mad, and those with alien minds. Frequently those that belong to this cult feel a strong need to make sense of their experience and this leads them look deeper into Abyss for answers, which in turn leads to more trauma that increases the desire to understand the source of their pain in a spiral going ever inward and downward.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Cultists:</b> Worms that Walk, Abyssal Beings Madmen<br /> <b>Initiation Benefits</b><br /> <b>\u2022</b> All initiates learn many unspeakable secrets of the Abyss. They gain a Occult Specialty in<br /> Abyssal Blasphemies.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022</b> Full members have their unconscious mind linked to horrific astral realms that reflect abyssal concepts within the Temenos which causes them to always have nightmares instead of dreams, but those nightmares become a source of terrible revelations. They gain a dot of the Dream Merit free of charge.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022</b> As a cultist delves into the mysteries that their sleeping mind wrestles with night after night, they become metaphysically tethered to a Rank 1 Acamoth of their own Virtue in a relationship which grants them the Familiar (\u2022\u2022) Merit free of charge.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b> The crazed insane priests of the Yonder gain the Astral Adept (\u2022\u2022\u2022) Merit. The ceremony they must perform is to sleep un-medicated in a dark room with no one else present, and in relative silence. This will cause a horrendous night terror which will shape itself into a journey beyond their own soul in order to escape.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b> Those of the Yonder Cult which have traveled the deepest pits of raving Abyssal madness within the Astral find they able to give fellow Astral Travelers they meet in their Astral Journeys the Been Yonder [Persistent] Condition if they ask to have revelations of the Abyss revealed to them.<br /> <br /> <b>Been Yonder</b> [Persistent]<br /> You've been in the Abyss either mentally or with your whole being, experiencing in each moment as countless eternal epochs of cosmic apostatizing exposure to things minds were not mean to know. Suffer a Breaking Points simply by thinking about your experience within the Abyss, remembering it, or being reminded of it as long as you have either Wisdom or Integrity to lose. You also qualify to join the Mystery Cult of the Yonder if you explore your subconscious connection to it.<br /> <b>Causes:</b> Experience being within formless timeless portions of the Abyss, Having Amnesia of that experience removed, Have the mental totality of that experience artificial transplanted within your mind (Which require Mind 5, or an appropriate Influence 4 by an Acamoth to Create an exact copy of an existing experience, mere modification of things that can be mundanely known does not suffice)<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Gain the Amnesia Condition concerning time in the Abyss</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-20-2019, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T11:43:43-08:00","id":1188587,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a> Since you have 4 major threads in your sig, what about something that ties them all together? Like a Relic that makes a Strange Place that becomes host to a Twilight entity which makes Horrors? Or something. Cross-posting fun!<br /> <br /> Ideal-Mate is close, just missing a few references.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 02-22-2018, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T07:32:42-08:00","id":1189219,"title":"","content":"Another idea: A multi-form Horror. Like a Caterpillar it has one state, then matures into another different state (or more). Bonus points if one of them can pass as human.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://i0.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/facebook/000/591/899/85e.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> More Fun: <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=this+isn%27t+even+my+final+form&amp;source=lnms&amp;tbm=isch&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0ahUKEwjwo6-Q777ZAhVHoVMKHZD3CcMQ_AUICigB&amp;biw=1920&amp;bih=949#imgrc=_\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.google.com/search?q=this...ih=949#imgrc=_</a><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T16:50:52-08:00","id":1189311,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Crossovers</b><br /> <br /> While I have yet to create a all-in one idea that bridges the gap between the various ideas that bubble out of my mind, I often weave threads as one idea inspires another. For the most part, these just serve as easter eggs mostly for my own amusement, but kudos to anyone that can spot them. That being said, its a cool idea and one I will have to think about in the future.<br /> <br /> <b>RE: Multi-Form Horror</b><br /> <br /> This idea has inspired what I think is a good approach to the concept. The easiest thing I found would just be to have different stat blocks at different Potency. I considered a &quot;transformation&quot; mechanic, but felt the most elegant solution was to leave such a thing to whenever and however the Storyteller deems appropriate. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Chosen of Muoi</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Chosen of Muoi are individuals chosen by a secretive cult that originates in Vietnam several hundred years ago. The cult venerates an entity named \u201cM\u00e1u Luu Dong\u201d, which translates roughly to \u201cThe Blood Swarm\u201d. In return for its favor and protection from its mosquito children, the cultist offer a young women to become the entities avatar. This is considered both blessing and curse. It bestows great power, but curses the Chosen with an insatiable thirst for blood. The Chosen gains the ability to assume a \u201clarval\u201d form, a pale, grotesque blood-drinking creature, and an \u201cAvatar\u201d form \u2013 a giant, winged horror that combines the traits of a human and a mosquito. So far, the Chosen have only been seen in Vietnam, and in Vietnamese communities in France and the United States.<br /> <br /> <b>Human/Larval Form</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Surreptitious; <b>Vice:</b> Gluttonous<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To Serve the Cult of Muoi<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 4, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 3(Bite), Intimidate 3, Medicine 2(Blood), Occult 3, Subterfuge 2, Survival 2(Jungle), Stealth 3<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Fast Reflexes 1, Hardy 2, Mystery Cult Initiation 4<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 3<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 14<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must consume fresh human blood are part of diet or suffer deprivation<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee; 8 dice]<br /> Bite [+1L ranged; 8 dice; Armor Piercing 1]<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Natural Weapon (Bite), Numina (Mortal Mask), Toxic (Sick) </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Avatar Form</b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 6, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 6, Dexterity 6, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 5, Manipulation 2, Composure 4<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 4, Brawl 5(Bite), Intimidate 5, Medicine 2(Blood), Occult 3, Subterfuge 2, Survival 4(Jungle), Stealth 5<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Fast Reflexes 1, Hardy 2, Indomitable, Mystery Cult Initiation 4, Striking Looks (Horrific), Trained Observer<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 5<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 14<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 11<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 10<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 17/ Flight 27<br /> <b>Health:</b> 11<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can only maintain Avatar form for one 1 hour per day<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Claws [+0L melee; 11 dice]<br /> Bite [+1L ranged; 12 dice; Armor Piercing 1]<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Natural Weapon (Bite), Regenerate, Swift, Toxic (Sick) </span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Mystery Cult: Cult of the Blood Swarm</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> The Cult of the Blood Swarm began almost 300 years ago in Vietnam. When a remote village was beset by vicious, plague carrying mosquitoes, the villagers made a deal with an entity they named \u201cThe Blood Swarm\u201d. In return for good health and protection from his biting, hungry children, they must ritually set aside one of their own to be fed upon to sate the hunger of the swarm. Occasionally, one favored by the Blood Swarm would become its Avatar, to act as its strongest servant in the mortal world. Since that time, the Cult has continued on in secret, obeying the will of its patron. In recent years the cult has been making efforts to breed and smuggle species of mosquitoes into new regions, and provide sacrifices as demanded by the Blood Swarm.<br /> <br /> <b>Cult of the Blood Swarm</b><br /> <b>Purpose:</b> To honor the demands of the Blood Swarm in exchange for health and good fortune<br /> <b>Relic:</b> The Idol of the Blood Swarm. A jade statue depicting a half woman, half mosquito creature.<br /> <b>Doctrine:</b> The cult is sworn to secrecy, and inducts only relatives of current members. The dictates of the Blood Swarm are communicated by the High Priestess, and every member routinely receives orders directly from her.<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation Benefits</i><br /> \u25cf - Cult Members become resistant to disease, gaining a dot in the <i>Hardy</i> Merit. Cult Members become completely immune to discomfort from and non-supernatural ailments transmitted by Mosquito bite.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf - Cult Members are gifted a measure of a Mosquitoes speed and alertness, gaining a dot in the <i>Fast Reflexes</i> Merit.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - Cult Members become versed in the deeper lore of the Blood Swarm and gain a dot in Occult.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - Cult Members gains access to significant resources gathered by the Cult overtime. The may divide three dots of Merits between <i>Allies</i>, <i>Resources</i> and <i>Safe Place</i>.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - A High Priest or Priestess of the Cult has the favor of the Blood Swarm, and make sacrifices in its Name, gaining three dots in the <i>Sacrificial Offering</i> Merit (Hurt Locker, pg. 76). In addition, once a month they may call upon \u201cThe Chosen of Muoi\u201d - a hideous, powerful creature to do their bidding. </div></div> </div> </div></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 02-25-2018, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T12:58:15-08:00","id":1189448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1189311#post1189311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: Crossovers</b><br /> <br /> While I have yet to create a all-in one idea that bridges the gap between the various ideas that bubble out of my mind, I often weave threads as one idea inspires another. For the most part, these just serve as easter eggs mostly for my own amusement, but kudos to anyone that can spot them. That being said, its a cool idea and one I will have to think about in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I saw that you referenced Elysium Concepts in your latest Relic (<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). The combinations are (not endless, but many). I can spitball some other flows/combinations later, if you want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1189311#post1189311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: Multi-Form Horror</b><br /> <br /> This idea has inspired what I think is a good approach to the concept. The easiest thing I found would just be to have different stat blocks at different Potency. I considered a &quot;transformation&quot; mechanic, but felt the most elegant solution was to leave such a thing to whenever and however the Storyteller deems appropriate. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Chosen of Muoi</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Chosen of Muoi are individuals chosen by a secretive cult that originates in Vietnam several hundred years ago. The cult venerates an entity named \u201cM\u00e1u Luu Dong\u201d, which translates roughly to \u201cThe Blood Swarm\u201d. In return for its favor and protection from its mosquito children, the cultist offer a young women to become the entities avatar. This is considered both blessing and curse. It bestows great power, but curses the Chosen with an insatiable thirst for blood. The Chosen gains the ability to assume a \u201clarval\u201d form, a pale, grotesque blood-drinking creature, and an \u201cAvatar\u201d form \u2013 a giant, winged horror that combines the traits of a human and a mosquito. So far, the Chosen have only been seen in Vietnam, and in Vietnamese communities in France and the United States.<br /> </span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><br /> <br /> Yay! Mosquito monsters! And blood drinkers, which will throw off Hunters that see an exsanguinated corpse and think &quot;Vampire!&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1189311#post1189311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Human/Larval Form</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Merits:</b> Hardy 2, <u>Mystery Cult Initiation 5</u><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Avatar Form</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Merits:</b> Hardy 2, Indomitable, <u>Mystery Cult Initiation 5</u>, Striking Looks (Horrific), Trained Observer<br /> ...<br /> <b>Ban:</b> <u>Can only maintain Avatar form for one 1 hour per day</u><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Mystery Cult: Cult of the Blood Swarm</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> The Cult of the Blood Swarm began almost 300 years ago in Vietnam. When a remote village was beset by vicious, plague carrying mosquitoes, the villagers made a deal with an entity they named \u201cThe Blood Swarm\u201d. In return for good health and protection from his biting, hungry children, they must ritually set aside one of their own to be fed upon to sate the hunger of the swarm. Occasionally, one favored by the Blood Swarm would become its Avatar, to act as its strongest servant in the mortal world. Since that time, the Cult has continued on in secret, obeying the will of its patron. In recent years the cult has been making efforts to breed and smuggle species of mosquitoes into new regions, and provide sacrifices as demanded by the Blood Swarm.<br /> <br /> <b>Cult of the Blood Swarm</b><br /> <b>Purpose:</b> To honor the demands of the Blood Swarm in exchange for health and good fortune<br /> <b>Relic:</b> The Idol of the Blood Swarm. A jade statue depicting a half woman, half mosquito creature.<br /> <b>Doctrine:</b> The cult is sworn to secrecy, and inducts only relatives of current members. The dictates of the Blood Swarm are communicated by the High Priestess, and every member routinely receives orders directly from her.<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation Benefits</i><br /> \u25cf - Cult Members become resistant to disease, gaining a dot in the <i>Hardy</i> Merit. Cult Members become completely immune to discomfort from and non-supernatural ailments transmitted by Mosquito bite.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf - Cult Members are gifted a measure of a Mosquitoes speed and alertness, gaining a dot in the <i>Fast Reflexes</i> Merit.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - Cult Members become versed in the deeper lore of the Blood Swarm and gain a dot in Occult.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - Cult Members gains access to significant resources gathered by the Cult overtime. The may divide three dots of Merits between <i>Allies</i>, <i>Resources</i> and <i>Safe Place</i>.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - A High Priest or Priestess of the Cult has the favor of the Blood Swarm, and make sacrifices in its Name, gaining three dots in the <i>Sacrificial Offering</i> Merit (Hurt Locker, pg. 76). <u>In addition, once a month they may call upon \u201cThe Chosen of Muoi\u201d - a hideous, powerful creature to do their bidding.</u> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div></span>So, looking at this, it is more of a Transformation as opposed to a maturation, then? Since the Avatar can only exist for a limited time.<br /> <br /> Also, MCI 5 on the creature seems odd given the 5th dot benefit. They can summon themselves, or another of their kind, once a month?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T14:39:31-08:00","id":1189471,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Crossover</b><br /> <br /> Sure! I always love seeing with others can do with some of the ideas I have posted.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Chosen of Muoi</b><br /> <br /> I knew that I was going to base this horror on some type of hideous blood drinking vermin (fleas, ticks and lice also come to mind). But mosquitoes are nasty and almost omnipresent (and spreading. Thanks Climate Change!)<br /> I went with a reversible transformation because I think it opens more flexibility with how the creature is used. A one-way evolution mechanic would work in a similar fashion but with no time limit Ban.<br /> And for the Mystery Cult of Initiation, I had meant to scale that back and re-distribute the merit dot. Updated up thread.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T16:05:16-08:00","id":1189485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1189471#post1189471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: Crossover</b><br /> <br /> Sure! I always love seeing with others can do with some of the ideas I have posted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant more as general inspiration ideas, but I'll see what I can do (I'm still meaning to write up the Verminators - CofD <a href=\"http://turtlepedia.wikia.com/wiki/Mouser_(1987_TV_series)\" target=\"_blank\">Mousers</a> - as a Horde-type Brief Nightmare, so this might take some time).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T18:27:19-08:00","id":1189506,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Verminators</u></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Background</span></b><br /> These autonomous drones were created to solve various pest problems that infest the urban sprawl. Their small size enables them to squeeze into confined spaces after their targets, and their coordinated swarm intelligence lets them surround nests to prevent any from escaping. They've been programmed with some basic architectural information, to prevent their occasional burrowing (to access and surround entrenched vermin) from causing more damage or collapse. Despite initial tests proving successful, high start-up costs and some linger safety concerns led to the project and commercial release getting scrapped. The remaining prototypes have since been sold off to various collectors, corporations interested in niche robotics, or stolen from storage.<br /> <b>Description</b><br /> Ironically, considering their function and primary targets, Verminators most resemble stainless steel rats, with four locomotive appendages, a barrel-like main fuselage, and leading with its primary sensor and &quot;elimination&quot; manipulator. There was even discussion about clothing them in faux rat coverings as a form of camouflage, before being dismissed as ghoulish.<br /> <b>Storytelling Hints</b><br /> Verminators primarily serve as pests, such as when they've gone haywire or been reprogrammed to undermine foundations. They can serve as a more serious threat if they've been reprogrammed to target humans, and groups will have individual units grapple limbs (inflicting the respective Tilt) to bring down larger &quot;prey&quot;. Since they are programmed and built by others, they always point to another antagonist as the responsible actor.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Best At (7 Dice):</b> Locating targets, swarm tactics, burrowing through buildings<br /> <b>Worst At (1 Die):</b> Innovative tactics, swimming<br /> <b>Other (3 Dice)</b><br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 3<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Locate and eliminate programmed targets from the area.<br /> <b>Initiative:</b><br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Size:</b> 1<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks:</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Type</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Damage</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Range</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Dice Pool</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Bite</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1L (AP 1)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Melee</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">7 (in group), 3 (alone)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Grapple</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">0B</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Melee</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">7 (in group), 3 (alone)</td> </tr> </table></div> <b>Banes:</b> Electricity<br /> <b>Bans:</b> none<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Burrow, Hunters Senses (Programmed Target), Natural Weapons (\u2022), Surprise Entrance<br /> <br /> If enough Verminators have gathered in the area, it may be appropriate to use the <b>Zombies!</b> Tilt (CofD, p.150) reskinned to represent scores of the little drones grappling with characters and taking chunks out of them.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 02-26-2018, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T19:16:45-08:00","id":1189747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1189311#post1189311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: Multi-Form Horror</b><br /> This idea has inspired what I think is a good approach to the concept. The easiest thing I found would just be to have different stat blocks at different Potency. I considered a &quot;transformation&quot; mechanic, but felt the most elegant solution was to leave such a thing to whenever and however the Storyteller deems appropriate. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Chosen of Muoi</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Chosen of Muoi are individuals chosen by a secretive cult that originates in Vietnam several hundred years ago. The cult venerates an entity named \u201cM\u00e1u Luu Dong\u201d, which translates roughly to \u201cThe Blood Swarm\u201d. In return for its favor and protection from its mosquito children, the cultist offer a young women to become the entities avatar. This is considered both blessing and curse. It bestows great power, but curses the Chosen with an insatiable thirst for blood. The Chosen gains the ability to assume a \u201clarval\u201d form, a pale, grotesque blood-drinking creature, and an \u201cAvatar\u201d form \u2013 a giant, winged horror that combines the traits of a human and a mosquito. So far, the Chosen have only been seen in Vietnam, and in Vietnamese communities in France and the United States.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Slightly Modified Mechanics to fit a maturation and life cycle that involves the creation of Strange Places and fleshed out their Relic of the Mystery Cult, and the Ephemeral Entity which they worship.<br /> <br /> <b>Human/Larval Form</b><br /> Humanity is the pond in which these horrors plant their eggs, swimming as predators among us because they can look as we do. Their true form has compound eyes, tough pale blubbery skin covered in plague-bearing bulbous and instead of a nose or mouth it has a terrible proboscis for draining blood from its living and undead victims. Being the disguised predators of humanity they are they also have the ability to mask themselves as humans, specifically the attractive human female who was transformed into this Larval stage at specially sanctified fountains call &quot;b\u1ec3 nu\u00f4i c\u00e1&quot;, translated Spawning Pools. The transformation is similar to baptism, except the submersion lasts three day and creates a blood drinking monster.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Surreptitious; <b>Vice:</b> Gluttonous<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To Serve the Cult of Muoi<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 4, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 3(Bite), Intimidate 3, Medicine 2(Blood), Occult 3, Subterfuge 2, Survival 2(Jungle), Stealth 3<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Fast Reflexes 1, Hardy 2, Mystery Cult Initiation 3 Striking Looks 1 (Beautiful in Mortal Mask, Horrific in true form)<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 3<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 14<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must use Drain Numen Dread Power each week or suffer the Deprived Condition<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Being without a Spawning Pool due to its destruction, or being Created beyond the limits of the local Spawning Pool (1 Resistant Aggravated Damage per Round)<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee; 8 dice]<br /> Bite [+1L ranged; 8 dice; Armor Piercing 1]<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Numina (Mortal Mask), Numen-Drain (This takes the for of a Proboscis bite turning lethal blood loss in living Humans or Vitae loss into the Horror Willpower pool), Toxic (Sick) </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If the Avatar Chosen of Muoi of a Spawning Pool is is slain but the Strange Place in intact and there are surviving Larval Chosen of Muoi then the remaining Larval Chosen of Muoi take their true form and pupate and transform into Avatar Chosen of Muoi. The first one to finish the transformation to Avatar Chosen of Muoi claims the existing Spawning Pool as their own, with the others forced to disperse to found a new Spawning Pool elsewhere. During the time they become capable of this transformation the Larval Chosen of Muoi temporarily have the Wall Climbing Dread Power which they use to pupate tucked up off the ground.<br /> <br /> <b>Avatar Form</b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 6, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 6, Dexterity 6, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 5, Manipulation 2, Composure 4<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 3, Brawl 4(Bite), Intimidate 5, Medicine 2(Blood), Occult 5(Blood), Subterfuge 2, Survival 4(Jungle), Stealth 4<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Fast Reflexes 1, Hardy 1, Indomitable, Mystery Cult Initiation 5, Striking Looks (Horrific) 2<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 5<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 14<br /> <b>Size:</b> 8<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 11<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 10<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 17/ Flight 27<br /> <b>Health:</b> 12<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must use Drain Numen Dread Power each day or suffer the Deprived Condition<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Claws [+0L melee; 11 dice]<br /> Bite [+1L ranged; 12 dice; Armor Piercing 1]<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Numen-Drain (This takes the for of a Proboscis bite turning lethal blood loss in living Humans or Vitae loss into the Horror Willpower pool), Toxic (Sick), Regenerate, Swift, </span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1189311#post1189311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Mystery Cult: Cult of the Blood Swarm</b><br /> <br /> The Cult of the Blood Swarm began almost 300 years ago in Vietnam. When a remote village was beset by vicious, plague carrying mosquitoes, the villagers made a deal with an entity they named \u201cThe Blood Swarm\u201d. In return for good health and protection from his biting, hungry children, they must ritually set aside one of their own to be fed upon to sate the hunger of the swarm. Occasionally, one favored by the Blood Swarm would become its Avatar, to act as its strongest servant in the mortal world. Since that time, the Cult has continued on in secret, obeying the will of its patron. In recent years the cult has been making efforts to breed and smuggle species of mosquitoes into new regions, and provide sacrifices as demanded by the Blood Swarm.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Cult of the Blood Swarm</b><br /> <b>Purpose:</b> To honor the demands of the Blood Swarm in exchange for health and good fortune<br /> <b>Relic:</b> The Idol of the Blood Swarm. A jade statue depicting a half woman, half mosquito creature.<br /> <b>Doctrine:</b> The cult is sworn to secrecy, and inducts only relatives of current members. The dictates of the Blood Swarm are communicated by the High Priestess, and every member routinely receives orders directly from her.<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation Benefits</i><br /> \u25cf - Cult Members become resistant to disease, gaining a dot in the <i>Hardy</i> Merit. Cult Members become completely immune to discomfort from and non-supernatural ailments transmitted by Mosquito bite.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf - Cult Members are gifted a measure of a Mosquitoes speed and alertness, gaining a dot in the <i>Fast Reflexes</i> Merit.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - Cult Members become versed in the deeper lore of the Blood Swarm and gain a dot in Occult.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - Cult Members gains access to significant resources gathered by the Cult overtime. The may divide three dots of Merits between <i>Allies</i>, <i>Resources</i> and <i>Safe Place</i>.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I modified the fifth dot of the cult to integrate it with the Spawning Pool Strange Place<br /> <br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - A High Priest or Priestess of the Cult has the favor of the Blood Swarm, and may sanctify a new Spawning Pool in a blood ritual that completely drains ten young pregnant Vietnamese women into the water. Please note this ability even applies to High Priest and Priestess whom are not Chosen of Muoi, and if used by those the Avatar Chosen of Muoi which takes residence is obligated to each Lunar month take Leveraged Condition in relation to the non-Chosen of Muoi High Priest or Priestess who made their Spawning Pool.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Spawning Pools (b\u1ec3 nu\u00f4i c\u00e1)</b></span><br /> Each Spawning pool needs a nearby population of ethnically Vietnamese in a minimum of tens of thousands and may be no closer than 20116 tr\u01b0\u1ee3ng (About 50 miles) and must be founded on an even numbered Vietnamese lunar year. The Pool must be waist deep still water that is concealed from the sky in the summer months, either in doors or under a thick canopied tree. Powered by the blood taken from those whom where in the prime of health while they were creating a new life within themselves this pool takes that power an perverts into a sick mockery that turns people into monster, and takes lives to fuel desires of monsters. Draining or filling in the pool so that it is less than knee deep, or exposing it to clear sky on a sunny day destroys all distinct supernatural properties of the site.<br /> <b>Traits</b><br /> <b>Die Pool:</b> 5<br /> <b>Gauntlet:</b> 3<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 1<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 2<br /> <b>Environments:</b><br /> <b>Create Larval Chosen of Muoi:</b> Each Spawning Pool is able to support five Larval Chosen of Muoi, who decompose into a surup of rotting blood if the site is destroyed. As long as there are less than five Larval Chosen of Muoi supported by the the Spawning Pool a young beautiful Vietnamese woman may be submerged within the pool by an Avatar Chosen of Muoi for three days and on the third day rise as a Larval Chosen of Muoi, with the memories of the woman before her transformation and an instinctive drive to serve the cult and feed on blood.<br /> <b>Wishing Well:</b> The Place has an ability to linked to a single Avatar Chosen of Muoi and can fulfill its hearts desire. Each wish is paid for with the price of a blood ritual that completely drains a less than a lunar month old Vietnamese infant into the water. Fulfilled Wishes can include removing or applying a condition or tilt, granting a Merit, Skill or Attribute at 5 dots, fulfilling of an Aspiration, or simply causing death and misfortune to befall someone else. The Soul of the victim is also consumed in the ritual and it creates no ghosts nor unused Essence.<br /> <b>Inhabited:</b> The local Cult of the Blood Swarm considers the Place its home, and that familiarity grants it a distinct advantage against intruders. Any creature that lives within the Environment gains 3 dots of the Safe Place Merit and gains a +2 bonus to its rolls to resist supernatural effects. The creature that inhabits the location is also immune to the effects of any other Environments the Place might possess This Environment is always active for as long as the creature resides at the location. Additionally the location and those within it are considered Open for the Manifestations and Numina of M\u00e1u Luu Dong.<br /> <br /> <b>The Idol of the Blood Swarm (Relic)</b><br /> <b>Description:</b> A half-meter tall jade statue depicting a half woman, half mosquito creature writhing in a dance-like pose, with the base being carved to resemble a mound of lifeless beautiful women upon which the figure is atop.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Doorway of M\u00e1u Luu Dong:</b> While placed next to a Spawning Pool this relic allows M\u00e1u Luu Dong to acts as the Spawning Pool's Avatar Chosen of Muoi for purposes of creating Larval Chosen of Muoi and the Wishing Well Environment even if it is Possessing/Claiming a mere human. Additionally it allows those with 5 dots Mystery Cult Initiation (Cult of the Blood Swarm) to call M\u00e1u Luu Dong who will Discorporate and reform at the current location of the Idol.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:24px\">&quot;M\u00e1u Luu Dong&quot; Farsekh Muth Eren </span></b><br /> <b>Spirit of blood-thirst and disease</b><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 5<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 15, Finesse 12, Resistance 15<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 50<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 27<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 12<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 37<br /> <b>Size:</b> 9<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 17<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Blood-thirst 5, Blood born-Disease 4<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Discorporate, Gauntlet Breach, Fetter, Possess, Claim, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Dement, Drain, Essence Thief-(Vitae), Mortal Mask, Speed<br /> <b>Ban:</b> May only Possess/Claim Vietnamese Women or Chosen of Muoi, Must Discorporate and reform at the current location of the Idol of the Blood Swarm if a High Priest/Priestess of the Cult of the Blood Swarm touches the Idol and calls M\u00e1u Luu Dong.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Daoist talismans against sickness (Which are created via Abjuration Rituals with sincere Daoist Belief)<br /> This spirit almost always has Claimed an Avatar Chosen of Muio, making it a terror that rules over its Spawning Pool, and using the power of that pool to increase the power of the cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-26-2018, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T19:47:37-08:00","id":1189750,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: The Chosen of Muoi</b><br /> <br /> Fantastic work!<br /> <br /> Keeps the main themes of the Horror and the Cult, and expands them greatly. This is fully usable as an in game antagonist that can challenge a variety of character types, from blue book mortal investigators, to Hunters, all the way to being a challenge for Vampire, Werewolves, and Mages.<br /> I particularly like keeping the origins and themes linked to the ethnic Vietnamese (I chose that group mainly because I don't see it represented in role playing games that often).<br /> <br /> Again, awesome stuff. Reminds me why I love collaborative projects!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T19:09:42-08:00","id":1190103,"title":"","content":"I'm going to list these ideas here for now. If someone wants to complete them (or variants of them) before I do, feel free.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dream Larvae - Create generates a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places?p=1190102#post1190102\">field</a> around it that makes the world as pliable as dreams.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Embodied - Manifest monsters made from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1190100#post1190100\">Links</a> that have completed their quest to become \u201creal\u201d.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[Crawling Ones] - Larval-stage monsters that consume humans and eventually mutate into [Great Ones]. EDIT: I might call this creature-line Urhimora, unless someone has a better idea. Naming the type is important for later Influence: [Urhimora] effects.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[Great Ones] - Creatures that resemble humans near-perfectly - physically and mentally. Given appropriate conditions, they can mutate into <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1190100#post1190100\">[Ascended Ones]</a>.</span></span> <hr /><br /> Work-in-Progress for Crawling Ones<br /> <br /> <b><u>Urhimora-Crawling Ones</u></b><br /> &lt;<i>Hissing Whispers</i>&gt;<br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Background</span></b><br /> [Document the sparse history of the cave dwelling degenerates. Then list their unnerving life-cycle.]<br /> <b>Description</b><br /> These pallid, worm-like humanoids are terrible to look at - when one can see them clearly, considering they shun the light. Imagine a pale, pudgy human the size of a large child, with lips pulled back over the teeth, bat-like ears, a pig-like nose, and eyes that are barely there.<br /> <b>Storytelling Hints</b><br /> [Pretty much serve as cave dwelling Morlocks. The two other notable things about them are their resistance to supernatural effect - meaning charms and Hunter Endowments become less effective, and their &quot;life-cycle&quot; change to Great Ones.]<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Best At (5 Dice):</b> Smelling intruders, attacking from ambush, resisting supernatural powers<br /> <b>Worst At (Chance Die):</b> Acting in bright light, independent thought<br /> <b>Other (2 Dice)</b><br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 2<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Consume Intruders, Defend Territory<br /> <b>Initiative: </b><br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 4<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks:</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Type</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Damage</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Range</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Dice Pool</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Crude Spear</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2L</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Melee</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Grapple</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">0B</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Melee</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5</td> </tr> </table></div> <b>Banes:</b> none<br /> <b>Bans:</b> Avoid Bright Light<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Chameleon Horror, Influence: Urhimora 1, <i>Adaptive Resistance</i>*<br /> <br /> <i><b>Adaptive Resistance</b></i>: The Horror is capable of developing a resistance to supernatural forms of attack after a brief exposure. After succeeding at a Resisted or Contested roll against a Dread Power or supernatural ability, the Horror gains an automatic +2 to its resistance attributes (which stacks with Willpower spent) against further uses of that power. Attacks incorporating the Horror's Bane always bypass this defense. The Storyteller may decide that certain abilities are different enough in nature to warrant separate exposures, even if modeled on the same Dread Power.<br /> <b>Note</b>: Urhimora's Adaptive Resistance never applied against any uses of Influence: Urhimora against them.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> [Placeholder for listing what triggers the Crawling One change into a Great One.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-15-2018, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T10:39:37-08:00","id":1193197,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a> What about a Dread Power (or Numina or Relic power, for that matter) that lets the being's attacks get treated as a Bane under certain circumstances? Like <b>Bane Strike (Intruders)</b> or <b>(Those who have violated the Oath of the Unspoken)</b> or <b>(Dead Things)</b>?<br /> <br /> I was actually rereading the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1133723#post1133723\">Langoliers</a> and thought it might be appropriate for them to have <b>Bane Strike (Time Travelers)</b> to make them more dangerous to their chosen prey.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I mean, instead of merely saying &quot;Monster can do Aggravated Damage&quot; it restricts it into making it circumstantial, but still leverages existing rules. Like, any Silver will harm a Werewolf, but if the Keeper of the Oath hits a Werewolf that has violated the Oath of the Unspoken (whatever that is), then furball is still eating Agg.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":".  Elaborating reasoning 03-08-2018, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T18:46:57-07:00","id":1201499,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Dream Eating Vermin</b></span><br /> <br /> There is a crawling, many-armed thing that lives in your house. You don't know it because it hides very well.<br /> <br /> It watches you when you are sleeping, and keeps the things that go bump in the night away so you can rest easy. Sometimes it plays tricks on and leaves gifts for you while you are awake to try and cheer you up so you will have good dreams.<br /> <br /> In return for its protection, it eats pieces of your dreams to sustain itself. Sometimes it gets bloated and happy with what it eats, and leaves little eggs for you as thanks for letting it stay.<br /> <br /> Protect these eggs. Bad things happen to those who don't.<br /> <br /> <b>Best At:</b> 10 (Protecting Those Under Its Care, Hiding And Playing Tricks)<br /> <b>Worst At:</b> 2 (Communicating Verbally, Understanding The Nuances Of What Humans Enjoy)<br /> <b>All Other Pools:</b> 5<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Ensure People Rest Well So It Can Eat Their Dreams<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 6<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 10<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 15 (Flight 25)<br /> <b>Health:</b> 12<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Very, Very Cold Proboscis [+1L, Armor Piercing 1, Melee, 10 Dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Bane:</b> Sunlight<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can only eat the dreams of those who have indulged their Vice at least once within the week<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Chameleon Horror, Influence (Vice 1), Madness And Terror, Natural Weapon 1, Numen (Drain, Hallucination), Surprise Entrance<br /> <br /> EDIT: Should I write the eggs as a Relic? I imagine they grow into more instances of this Brief Nightmare, but offer good luck while you protect them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-30-2018, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T19:09:37-07:00","id":1201503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1201499#post1201499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Should I write the eggs as a Relic? I imagine they grow into more instances of this Brief Nightmare, but offer good luck while you protect them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, the more the better. Would the hatchlings be lesser Horrors, or (to mix it up) would they be a kind of pseudo-Goetia/Dreamborn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T22:17:31-07:00","id":1202450,"title":"","content":"I dunno which of your threads to post this in but I would like to see you make up some slashers based on each of the undertakings, like brute, mask, legend, charmer, etc etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24087-mattl1222","name":"MattL1222","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T07:41:56-07:00","id":1202574,"title":"","content":"I'll leave this here for inspiration: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bogeyman\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bogeyman</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T20:06:56-07:00","id":1202852,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: The Bogeyman</b><br /> <br /> I set the up the Bogeyman <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1164036-a-hodgepodge-of-hobs-2nd-ed?p=1175760#post1175760\">here</a>. I used the Hobgoblin creation rules from the Changeling 2E preview,so I figured that write up was more comfortable over there.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Slashers</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Since it it will be a while before we see the Slasher rules from Hunter 2E, I am using a modified version of the Horror rules for the next write ups. Here are my modification notes -<br /> <br /> In most cases, Slashers are still (mostly) human. Consider \u201cparanatural\u201d slashers, ones that are still capable of presenting themselves as regular individuals, to be equivalent to Potency 1-2 Horrors. While \u201csupernatural\u201d slashers, ones that have abandoned any pretense of normalcy are equivalent to Potency 3-4 Horrors.<br /> Slasher trade raw power for more cunning and resources. Slasher have a Trait Limit of 5 for paranatural slashers and 6 for supernatural Slashers. In exchange, Slasher gain 5+Potency additional dots of skills and 5+Potency additional dots of Merits. In addition, Slashers receive one fewer Dread Powers than an equivalent Horror and have the talent and frailty appropriate to their Undertaking. </span> <hr /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Ashley Chase</b></span><br /> Ashley Chase is a young woman who has been plagued by tragedy her entire life. From her sister\u2019s suicide, to the botched robbery that ended the lives of her parents, to the accidental overdose that killed her grandmother, she has faced this adversity with bravery, good cheer, and faith. Of course, she has been quietly behind each of these incidents, growing bolder and more inventive with her plans as time goes by. She has cultivated a group of friends that share a taste for true crime and other macabre fare, who she hasn\u2019t grown bored with yet. Her appreciable inheritance has allowed her to begin college for few concerns about tuition, and she has plans to join a sorority. Once she is more educated (both academically and practically), she will resume her \u201chobby\u201d in earnest.<br /> Ashley is a tall, slender blond with blue eyes, who dresses in a fashionable if somewhat conservative manner. She plays the part of a cheerful and pious young woman, and keeps her darker interests a well-guarded secret.<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Genius<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Cautious; Vice: Vindictive<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Arrange the perfect murder<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 4, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 3, Athletics 1, Empathy 3, Investigation 3, Larceny 2, Socialize 2, Stealth 3, Subterfuge 4, Weaponry 1<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Eidetic Memory, Encyclopedic Knowledge (Investigation), Hobbyist Clique (The Murder Club-Larceny), Patient, Resources 3, Striking Looks 1 (Pretty), Untouchable<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 2<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 6<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 10<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 2 dice]<br /> Knife [+0L melee;-1 Initiative; 3 dice]<br /> <b>Talent:</b> Profiling; <b>Frailty:</b> Intolerance for Chaos<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Hypnotic Gaze, Know Soul<br /> <br /> <i><b>Profiling:</b></i> Even on casual observation, a Genius can predict what a given person will do in a basic way based on appearance, body language and bearing. The Genius\u2019 player rolls Intelligence + Empathy, contested by the targets Manipulation + Subterfuge. If the Genius succeeds, he has a good enough understanding of the person to predict his actions. The Genius wins all ties in contested rolls against the target(s), and always wins initiative against him.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Intolerance for Chaos:</b></i> Geniuses might understand on some level that they can\u2019t allow for every freak of chance, but in practice, they get frustrated if they miss something or if something happens that they couldn\u2019t have predicted. If a Genius\u2019 player fails an<br /> Intelligence roll, the Genius loses two points of Willpower. </div></div> </div> </div></span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Gravedigger</b></span><br /> The man called \u201cThe Gravedigger\u201d lives in a dilapidated house squatting on a hill over looking a large property with a large collection of rusted and broken vehicles and an old cemetery occupying a remote corner of the acreage. The house and property serve as a focal point of the local community, who have long since abandoned conventional religion to secretly worship a God of Harvest and Sacrifice. The Gravedigger is his chosen servant. Made strong by the will of the God he provides the flesh and blood that must be interred in the soil to keep the crops growing, and the God appeased.<br /> The Gravedigger is nearly 7 ft tall and weighs over 300lbs. His craggy face is scarred and his eyes are dark. He wears a denim coverall and a hooded coat.<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Brute<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Dutiful; <b>Vice:</b> Jealous<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To serve the will of the Harvest God<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 3, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 4<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Animal Ken 2(Dogs), Athletics 2, Brawl 4, Crafts 3, Firearms 3(Rifle), Intimidate 4, Stealth 1, Weaponry 3(Improvised)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Choke Hold, Danger Sense, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Hardy 2, Indomitable, Iron Will, Style: Improvised Weaponry 1<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 2<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 1/0 [Reinforced Clothing]<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 14<br /> <b>Health:</b> 11<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 9 dice]<br /> Shovel [+1L melee;-3 Initiative; 9 dice; Knockdown]<br /> Rifle [+4L ranged; -5 Initiative; 7 dice]<br /> <b>Talent:</b> Unstoppable; <b>Frailty:</b> Blinded by Blood<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Jump Scare, Surprise Entrance<br /> <br /> <i><b>Unstoppable:</b></i> Brutes do not suffer wound penalties of any kind, and need not make the reflexive roll to stay conscious when the Brute\u2019s Health track is full of bashing damage. Instead, when the Brute\u2019s track fills with lethal damage, the player makes a reflexive Stamina roll to remain conscious and active. If this roll fails, the Brute falls unconscious and begins to bleed out. If it succeeds, the Brute can remain active until he suffers one more wound, at which point he is Incapacitated.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Blinded by Blood:</b></i> All Perception rolls made for Brutes suffer a \u20133 penalty, and on opposed rolls made to notice a hiding opponent, ties always go against the Brute. </div></div> </div> </div></span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Mr. Suit</b></span><br /> Mr. Suit is a name given to a suspected serial killer by the FBI agents that have been tracking the case for over 15 years. Unlike many such killers, who display obsessive and repetitive behaviors, Mr. Suit frequently switches methods and tactics; at different points using blades, guns, strangulation and even explosives to dispatch his victims. If not for his habit of periodically leaving a witness alive, it is likely his murders would never have been connected to each other. So far 18 known victims have been attributed to Mr. Suit.<br /> Mr. Suit is described as a tall, athletic man who wears a well-tailored suit (typically black or gray). He sports black gloves and an apron if the work is going to be messy. He always wears a mask; the masks design varies but he seems to favor a rubber gas mask. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Psycho<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Clever; <b>Vice:</b> Competitive<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To be the most successful killer that ever lived<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 4, Composure 4<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2, Athletics 3, Brawl 3, Crafts 2(Explosives), Firearms 3, Investigation 3(FBI procedure), Stealth 3(evade pursuit), Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 3, Weaponry 4<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 2 (FBI), Defensive Combat (Weaponry), Indomitable, Resources 4, Style: Fast Talking 3, Style: Light Weapons 2, Untouchable<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 3<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 11<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 7 dice]<br /> Knife [+0L melee;-1 Initiative; 8 dice]<br /> 9mm Pistol [+1L ranged; 7 dice]<br /> <b>Talent:</b> Deadly Distraction; <b>Frailty:</b> Obsessive<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Hunter\u2019s Senses (victims), Jump Scare<br /> <br /> <i><b>Deadly Distraction:</b></i> When the Psycho engages a target in conversation, they can cause the target to drop their guard enough for the Psycho to exploit the moment. This cannot be attempted in combat or when other witnesses are about. The Storyteller rolls Presence + Persuasion, contested by the victim\u2019s Wits + Composure. If the Psycho\u2019s is successful, the target lowers their defenses. Depending on what the Psycho is trying to accomplish, this might allow them to access to a building to recover a weapon or tamper with evidence. If the slasher wishes to attack the victim, he can make a Killing Blow with whatever weapon he has at hand, inflicting damage equal to the relevant dice pool with no roll required. This might not actually kill the victim, but it certainly inflicts a terrible wound, leaving the victim at the Psycho\u2019s mercy.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Obsessive:</b></i> Psychos just can\u2019t let something go. Once a Psycho chooses a victim, and attempts to charm her (either by using Deadly Distraction or mundane Social attempts) and fails, the Psycho cannot just leave her be. He must break her down, hurt her, scare her and finally kill her. The Psycho can be patient, but most of them aren\u2019t equipped for it, and wind up impulsively attacking the victim (who is by no means unsuspecting and helpless). If the victim inflicts damage upon the Psycho, the Frailty\u2019s effects end and he can flee. The Psycho will eventually return to finish the job, however, which is problematic for the victim, but can also be used to track or trap the Psycho. </div></div> </div> </div></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 08-30-2018, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T23:00:50-07:00","id":1202881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MattL1222</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1202450#post1202450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno which of your threads to post this in but I would like to see you make up some slashers based on each of the undertakings, like brute, mask, legend, charmer, etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WoD Slashers pg 125</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernatural Slasher?<br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">Is a vampire who always kills her victims a slasher? How about a werewolf that leaves only partially chewed bodies? or, better yet, what about a changeling that, for reasons known only to himself, hunts people down and scares them half to death... and then uses an ax to take care of the other half? Are any of these creatures \u201cslashers\u201d in the Hunter sense? </span></div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader?p=845248#post845248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Slashers</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Where that book said no, Frailty chronicles says a resounding \u201cYes!\u201d</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">That is because were that book defined Slashers solely in context to Hunter\u2019s that prey upon mere humans, we are looking at it as a phenomenon universal to all beings with a soul, dealing with extremely painful isolation from the mundane world and irrevocable severing of their capacity for the most important type of relationship.</span></span><br /> <br /> Slashers are horrors which were once beings with freewill and a soul but have lost all emotional ties that tether their psyche to the mundane world so it floats, off to the dizzying altitudes of utter madness and reduce them to mere puppets to monstrous instincts that lay at the core of every persons\u2019 being. Slasher are the monsters that have lost the spark which is the source of having a conscious, a soul, and thus freewill.<br /> <br /> There are two tiers for becoming a slasher, a Lesser Undertaking and a Greater Undertaking; the first is gained when an ensoulled character only has one Stability Advantage and the second is gained when the character is reduced to zero Stability Advantage. While both Undertakings grant power they come with a steep metaphysical price, freewill and even being considered an ensoulled being; In concrete game terms ensoulled beings are the only ones suitable to be player characters and gaining the Greater Undertaking makes the character a NPC which should not be played by its original player. (This is important for those that play LARP to keep the mechanic as a meaningful loss caused by the behaviors that lead to becoming a slasher, sever emotional ties the other players may have had to the character while portrayed by the player in question, and represent the startling internal change of the character that would deeply disturb those that once knew them).<br /> <br /> A Character with only a Lesser Undertaking is flirting with total corruption but still has a chance to be redeemed. If they gain a Support which raises their Stability Advantage to two or greater they lose all lose the Lesser Undertaking. An impressive story arch for a character can be seeking Vengeance for a Support and losing Support relationships along the way until they gain a Lesser Undertaking and either come back from the brink through the strength of their remaining Support, their supernatural friends, or something within themselves. Having tasted that power, woe to those that transgress to far against such a character because they are faced with the temptation of going down the road again when their Supports are killed.<br /> <br /> There are five Lesser Undertaking and Five Greater Undertakings, feel free to mix and match. There are \u201cnatural\u201d combination, and those are as follows: Avenger/Legend, Brute/Mask, Charmer/Psycho, Freak/Mutant, Genius/Maniac.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Lesser Undertakings</b></span><br /> All those with a Lesser Undertakings gain the Jump Scare dread power on page: CoD 146<br /> They also add the following Tag every kill of an ensoulled being they take part in.<br /> <br /> <b>Calling Card</b><br /> There is a clue which conveys a message for potential investigators. The message must be a hint towards one of the Slasher\u2019s Aspirations. Upon discovering the Clue the investigator understands the message, which is usually a leap in logic to understand the connection of several facts known to the investigator about the killing. Noticing a Calling Card requires an exceptional success on a roll using Investigation on the records or evidence of the killing.<br /> <br /> Sample Messages:<br /> Pack Aspiration: \u201cDefend the family from outside attacks.\u201d Resulting Message: \u201c\u201dFamily is very important\u201d<br /> Guardians of the Veil Aspiration: \u201cMaintain the conspiracy protecting the supernatural from the wilting touch of the mundane \u201c Resulting Message: \u201cAnything seemingly supernatural is a hoax.\u201d<br /> Daeva Aspiration: Gather love and adoration of others\u201d Resulting message: \u201cBeing the center of someone\u2019s world is all that matters.\u201d<br /> Lost Aspiration: \u201cNever be trapped in Arcadia again.\u201d Resulting Message: \u201cImprisonment is worse than death.<br /> Personal Aspiration: \u201cDefeat a worthy opponent.\u201d Resulting Message: \u201cThis is an offer to play a deadly game with investigators.\u201d<br /> <br /> List of Lesser Undertakings<br /> <b>Avenger</b><br /> Kills to avenge right or imagined wrong. These slashers gain the Hunter\u2019s Sense dread power on page: CoD 148 This is always focused on their preferred prey.<br /> <br /> <b>Brute</b><br /> Brute is big guy (or gal) who just wants to kill. Not very smart, and also very crude, he just kills. But he can still understand the potential risks, and can plan his attack. As a benefit brute doesn't feel pain. These slashers gain the Unbreakable dread power on page: CoD 148<br /> <br /> <b>Charmer</b><br /> Charmer is nice guy who charms others and lures them into false sense of security. When time is right, he strikes. Charmer's benefit is that he if he makes good first impression, person will believe him, even if it is against common sense or logic. These slashers gain the Hypnotic Gaze dread power on page: CoD 145<br /> <br /> <b>Freak</b><br /> Every freak has his own reason for killing, but it is usually related to his appearance or what it has caused. As a benefit, Freak quickly learn his surroundings. These slashers gain the Surprise Entrance dread power on page: CoD 148<br /> <br /> <b>Genius</b><br /> Genius kills his targets with his intellect. He tends to play mind games with his enemies and lure them into trap, but they can't relate to worms that are beneath them. As a benefit, Genius can profile target when he is met. These slashers gain the Know Soul dread power on page: CoD 146<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Greater Undertakings</b></span><br /> All those with a Greater undertaking gain the following persistent conditions that can\u2019t be resolved:<br /> <br /> <b>Obvious Lunatic</b><br /> It is obvious to anyone not on the brink of becoming a Slasher themselves that you are dangerously without moral compunction or need to comply with even the most fundamental social norms. -5 to any social interaction with any being with more than 1 Stability Advantage except hostile intimidation.<br /> <br /> <b>Putrefied Metaphysical Miasma</b><br /> Ephemeral Beings, Horrors, Major Templates, Minor Templates, and Complete Templates with two Stability Advantage or higher experience an extremely unpleasant sensation when in your presence, a profound impression of your \u201cwrongness\u201d and they feel no instinctual hesitation toward engaging in violence against you. For those with minor, major or complete templates the Compunction, Hesitation and PTSD rules do not apply when dealing with you.<br /> <br /> List of Greater Undertakings<br /> <b>Legend</b><br /> Legends have become one with their urban myth and now their actions conform to seemingly arbitrary rules that children make rhymes out of. These slashers gain the Immortal dread power on page: CoD 145 . Additionally they gain a simple Ban for every Bane they possess, Personal or otherwise.<br /> <br /> <b>Mask</b><br /> Masks aare nothing more than killing machines and are often portrayed as wearing a mask because it remove the appearance of any human emotion. Even when a Mask doesn\u2019t wear an actual mask their face is speechless and expressionless. These slashers gain the Regenerate: 1 dread power on page: CoD 148. Masks are completely incapable of most social interaction. They are unable to Open Doors in social contests against others and their doors may only be opened when confronted with their Banes and/or Bans, to put it into mechanical terms. They also have the Mute Condition which may not be resolved.<br /> <br /> <b>Mutant</b><br /> Twisted into aberrant shape by their own corruption the Mutant sheds the camouflage of appearing human, because they don\u2019t, and becomes visibly identifiable as a monster. These slashers gain the Natural Weapons: 3 dread power on page: CoD 147. Mutants automatically gain the Hunted Condition when in urban and semi-urban environments.<br /> <br /> <b>Psycho</b><br /> The Psycho is always a Slasher heavily tied to a location and broken relationships. It may be his family home and motel where his mother emotionally abused him until he murdered her, a lakeside campground where her son was neglected and bullied to death, or the neighborhood where he looked to \u2018gain his manhood\u2019 from a prostitute that scorned him and his violent insecurities remade him into a killer. These slashers gain the Homeground dread power on page: CoD 145. If this Slasher ever intends to kill someone they gain the Obsession Condition focused on killing that person until they believe that person is dead.<br /> <br /> <b>Maniac</b><br /> Some Slasher have a way of getting into the minds of other. Maniacs are masterminds or demagogues that manipulate or radicalize other to cause the death and carnage they crave. These Slashers gain the Implant Mission numina as a dread power on page: CoD 137. Each one has a specific die pool appropriate for their machinations, chosen then they gain this Undertaking. If a Maniac fails in an attempt to use Implant Mission against someone the Maniac Gains the Competitive Condition in relationship to that person.</div> </div> </div> </div>So using that system a Slasher with a combination of Lesser and Greater Undertakings has three dread powers putting them on part with potency 1-3 Horrors. Of course the above is written presuming my homebrew which has Atrocity, a universal applicability for Personal Banes and a version of Hell is Other people updated to second edition and made universally applicable as well, but for a general guide for assigning Dread Powers for Slashers, it's handy.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T03:25:37-07:00","id":1202933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1202852#post1202852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: The Bogeyman</b><br /> <br /> I set the up the Bogeyman <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1164036-a-hodgepodge-of-hobs-2nd-ed?p=1175760#post1175760&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. I used the Hobgoblin creation rules from the Changeling 2E preview,so I figured that write up was more comfortable over there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant the sheer variety of regional variations offer a wealth of inspiration for different Horrors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T17:43:01-07:00","id":1206202,"title":"","content":"A few more slashers - I am aiming to have a Slasher for each archetype. <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hell\u2019s Belle</span></b><br /> As the story goes, a young woman was stranded on the side of a lonely desert road, her car broken down and the nearest town a few hours away. While trying to flag down help, she was instead set upon by a roving gang of criminals, who kidnapped her and spent days abusing and torturing her before leaving her for dead. But she survived her ordeal and gained a burning desire for revenge. One by one, she tracked down and killed each one of her assailants, before vanishing into the night behind the wheel the gangs leader\u2019s muscle car. She is still out there, they say. Prowling the night, seeking the sort of men that have committed acts of violence and cruelty against women. While her goals are sympathetic, her methods are brutal and sadistic. She prefers to use a heavy revolver and stained baseball bat, but will use any tool necessary to enact her revenge. Belle is an athletic, statuesque beauty with cropped black hair and green eyes. Her flesh is crisscrossed with raised scars that seem to accentuate her looks. Her clothing is rugged jeans and tee shirts and she sports a silver crucifix, stained with so much blood it appears red. She wanders the roadways of the southwest in a black Ford Mustang.<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Legend; <b>Virtue:</b> Survivor; <b>Vice:</b> Vengeful<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Seek Revenge upon \u201cBad Men\u201d<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 2, Composure 4<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 4, Drive 4(Muscle Car), Firearms 3(Pistols), Intimidate 3(Men), Investigate 2, Stealth 2, Streetwise 2, Weaponry 4(Clubs)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Crack Driver 3, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Iron Stamina 2, Iron Will, Striking Looks 2(Dangerous Beauty), Style: Street Fighting 2, Style: Stunt Driver 2<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 3<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 12<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 10<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 8 dice]<br /> Baseball Bat [+1L melee;-1 Initiative; 9 dice]<br /> Heavy Revolver [+2L ranged;-2 Initiative; 8 dice]<br /> <b>Talent:</b> Strength from the Tales (any act of violence against a woman);<b> Frailty:</b> Trapped in the Story (Ban: Cannot harm a Woman (but can defend herself), Bane: Cactus Flower)<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Immortal, Surprise Entrance<br /> <br /> <i><b>Strength from the Tales:</b></i> The Legend can draw strength from those acting in accordance with her myth. Once per scene, when someone fulfills one of the tenets of the slasher\u2019s supernatural \u201crules,\u201d the Storyteller can roll Presence + Intimidate. Successes on this roll can be applied to one of the following: restoring spent Willpower, healing damage (one success for a bashing wound, two for a lethal, three for an aggravated wound) or applying bonuses to rolls made in pursuit of the Legend\u2019s agenda. The Legend does not have to use the successes in the same way each time, but cannot split the successes on any given chapter.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Trapped in the Story:</b></i> All Legends have a weakness. and they come in two forms: Bans and Banes. The Legend selects one of each. A Ban is either a compulsion or a behavioral restriction. These occur in certain situations unique to each Legend. A Bane is a weakness similar to those many supernatural creatures possess, something that can cause the Legend great harm. Banes cut instantly through all forms of armor, and damage suffered from a bane cannot be healed until the bane it is removed. </div></div> </div> </div></span> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Kind Fellow</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Kind Fellow considers what he does to be a higher calling. To those that are in pain and suffer, he frees them from this life to continue on to a better place. He moves from place to place, adopting new names and using false documents to gain employment. He prefers to work in hospitals, retirement homes, and hospices, typically as a nurse, orderly, or even janitor. He ingratiates himself to the patient, subtly convincing them that death is the only way out. He prefers to kill using gentler methods, such as suffocation or poison, but will strangle if necessary. The Kind Fellow sees stabbing and bludgeoning as needlessly cruel, and will rarely employ these methods.<br /> \u201cThe Kind Fellow\u201d is a pleasant faced, slightly balding, dark haired man in his mid-thirties. He has a stout build, but cultivates a slightly paunchy physique to appear less intimidating. He changes hair style or sports glasses or other accessories to conceal his true identity. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Charmer; <b>Virtue:</b> Caring; <b>Vice:</b> Envious<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Help the Sick and Injured<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 3 (Grapple), Crafts 1, Empathy 3, Medicine 2(Poison), Persuasion 3(Patients), Science 1(Chemistry), Stealth 3,Subterfuge 2(Impersonation), Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Anonymity 1, Choke Hold, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Numbing Touch 2, Professional Training 2 (Orderly; Brawl, Medicine), Style: Grappling 2, Sympathetic<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 2<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 6<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 7 dice]<br /> <b>Talent:</b> Disarming; <b>Frailty:</b> Thin Veneer (Rebuking his \u201cKindness\u201d)<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Home Ground (Hospitals), Hunter\u2019s Senses (The Dying)<br /> <br /> <i><b>Disarming:</b></i> When a Charmer meets a new person, the Storyteller rolls Presence + a Social Skill. The Skill might be Expression, Socialize or Persuasion. This roll is contested by the listener\u2019s Intelligence + Subterfuge. If the Charmer wins, that victim gains the Charmed Condition.<br /> Note that Charmers get one chance at this for a given person. First impressions are everything. If the Charmer fails to meet or exceed the target\u2019s successes, she sees through the Charmer to the Psycho beneath. She might just feel that the Charmer is a phony, not necessarily dangerous, but the warning bells definitely go off (which probably makes her the Charmer\u2019s first target).<br /> <br /> <i><b>Thin Veneer:</b></i> All Charmers have a trigger, chosen by the Storyteller. This might be bringing up a certain topic, a particular song, being touched in a sexual manner, or just being called by name rather than by title. When this trigger occurs, or when someone who resists the slasher\u2019s charms calls him out (\u201cYou\u2019re fucking creepy, dude\u201d is enough), the Storyteller rolls Composure. If this roll fails, the slasher lashes out \u2014 usually verbally, but sometimes physically. At this point, anyone who fell under the Charmer\u2019s wiles before has a chance to snap out of it (players roll Wits + Subterfuge; success means the Charmed Condition is resolved).</div></div> </div> </div></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 08-30-2018, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T14:51:37-07:00","id":1207022,"title":"","content":"More Slashers <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Red John</span></b><br /> Even as a boy, John Everett was a strange individual. Despite a fairly typical suburban upbringing by moderately religious parents, John was noted for sardonic sense of humor, fondness for pranks, and problems with authority. When John was sixteen, his family perished in a house fire (which was due to faulty wiring) and he himself suffered severe, disfiguring burns. After recovering from his injuries, John began to display curious abilities, such as heightened strength, resistance to pain, and a strange affinity with fire. He claims that the flame speaks to him, and compels him to burn away the world to make room for a new beginning. He has little regard for the life and well being of others, and will burn people as readily as he burns objects and structures. After getting kicked out of the foster care system for acts of arson and vandalism, John has become a drifter, supporting himself with odd jobs and petty theft.<br /> Red John is a plain-faced young man, with pale, freckled skin and bright red hair he keeps at shoulder length. He has ugly burn scars on this hands, arms and left side of his face, and dresses in dark clothing. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Freak; <b>Virtue:</b> Mirthful; <b>Vice:</b> Rebellious<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Burn down the old to make way for the new<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Computers 2, Brawl 3, Expression 2(Jokes), Larceny 3, Persuasion 2 (Pity), Science 1 (Fire), Streetwise 3 (Homeless), Stealth 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Anonymity 2, Iron Stamina 1, Professional Training 2 (Criminal; Larceny, Streetwise), Psychokinesis 3 (Fire), Style: Fast Talking 3, Untouchable<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 2<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 1/1<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 14<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 8 dice]<br /> <b>Talent:</b> Revulsion (body heat); <b>Frailty:</b> Deformity (burn scars)<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Fire Elemental, Numina (Firestarter)<br /> <br /> <i><b>Revulsion:</b></i> Fighting a Freak is hard, because it might mean touching them. All attempts to grapple or touch a Freak in combat suffer a -3 penalty. Once a grapple is established, attempts to immobilize or perform other maneuvers incur a -1 penalty, and the grappling character\u2019s Strength is considered one lower for purposes of escape attempts.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Deformity:</b></i> All Freaks are hideous to the eye. No matter what the source of their ugliness, birth or accident, normal people cannot help but stare at them. Many mock them, or shun them thinking that their disgusting visage is contagious (and maybe it is). Apply a \u20132 penalty on all Social rolls if the other parties involved can clearly perceive the Freak\u2019s Deformity, and treat any Presence and Manipulation failures as dramatic failures. This penalty does not apply to Intimidation attempts, of course. </div></div> </div> </div></span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Wyatt James</b></span><br /> Wyatt James was once a member of an organization called \u201cThe Church of Revelation\u201d. He and his wife joined the organization as a way to cope with trauma he experienced while serving in the military. The Church of Revelation was an apocalyptic cult, preparing for the impending End of Days. After moving to the Churches sprawling compound, Wyatt became disenchanted (and frightened) by the increasingly radical tone of the churches sermons. When he and his wife tried to escape, they met with armed resistance, and she was killed in the attempt.<br /> Over the course of a year, Wyatt murdered the leaders of the organization, and burned its compound to ashes.<br /> Wyatt continues his crusade, rooting out and extinguishing cults and organizations that he deems \u201cfalse\u201d or \u201cevil\u201d. He tries to limit the carnage to leaders and organizers, but more than a few lay members have been caught in the crossfire, which only compels Wyatt to make sure \u201ctheir sacrifice was not in vain\u201d.<br /> Wyatt James is a solid, athletic man in his early thirties with dark hair and brown eyes. He crops his hair close, wears a full beard and favors rugged practical clothing. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Avenger;<b> Virtue:</b> Faithful;<b> Vice: </b>Unforgiving<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To destroy those that pervert or corrupt the Gospel<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 1(Bible), Athletics 2, Brawl 3, Crafts 2(Explosives), Drive 2, Firearms 4(Pistols), Intimidate 2, Investigate 3, Occult 1(Cults), Stealth 2(Surveillance), Subterfuge 2, Survival 2(Doomsday Prep), Weaponry 3<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Defensive Combat (Brawl), Iron Stamina 2, Iron Will, Professional Training 3 (Soldier; Crafts, Firearms, Survival), Style: Close Quarters Combat 2, Style: Firefight 2<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 2<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 1/3 [Kevlar Vest]<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 7 dice]<br /> Knife [+0L melee;-1 Initiative; 7 dice]<br /> Heavy Pistol [+2L ranged; -2 Initiative; 9 dice; 9 again]<br /> <b>Talent:</b> Working the Room; <b>Frailty:</b> Nothing but the Mission<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Hunter\u2019s Senses (Cultists)<br /> <i>*Wyatt James exchanged a Dread Power for an additional 5+Potency points of Skills</i><br /> <br /> <i><b>Working the Room:</b></i> Avengers might try to kill their victims one by one, but sooner or later they wind up with a roomful of people that require their attention. The rules for Defense vs. multiple opponents do not apply to Avengers. No matter how many times in a turn an Avenger is attacked, apply his full Defense to all incoming attacks.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Nothing but the Mission:</b></i> Most slashers are obsessive, but Avengers take it to a whole new level. The Avenger has the Obsession Condition in regards to pursuing their chosen targets. When faced with the choice between pursuing a target and taking some other course of action, the Storyteller\u2019s must roll Resolve + Composure. If this roll succeeds, the Avenger can choose to let the target go (for now). If the roll fails, the Avenger remains focused on his mission and ignores the other situation. </div></div> </div> </div></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 04-22-2018, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T10:55:40-07:00","id":1210096,"title":"","content":"More Slashers <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Eris</span></b><br /> Simone Delacour, from even an early age, was as rebellious as she was intelligent. Her love of philosophy, mathematics, and especially computer sciences earned her admission to special schools for the gifted and talented, but her difficulties with those in positions of authority always made her an outsider. During her college years, she began associating with anarchist and discordian organizations, becoming increasingly radical overtime. She adopted the pseudonym \u201cEris\u201d, and dedicated herself full-time to tearing down a society that she perceives as hopelessly flawed and corrupt. She is brilliant programmer, hacker, and blackmailer, and she uses the information she gathers to manipulate individuals, inflame conflicts, and erode institutions. She takes a particular delight in orchestrating the death or ruin of key individuals, then watching the often far-reaching fallout.<br /> Eris is an African-American woman in her late thirties, with a dark complexion and close cropped hair. She dresses for comfort and has a \u201cpunk\u201d sense of style. She is reclusive and lives comfortably on money earned through blackmail and laundered through various business ventures. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Maniac; <b>Virtue:</b> Idealistic; <b>Vice:</b> Anarchist<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Disrupt the Status Quo<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 5, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 4, Composure 4<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2(Philosophy), Athletics 1, Computers 5(Hacking, Viruses), Crafts 2, Firearms 2, Intimidation 2, Investigation 4(Blackmail), Persuasion 3, Politics 3, Science 2, Socialize (Anarchists)1, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Anonymity 3, Area of Expertise (Hacking), Investigative Aid (Computers), Professional Training 4 (Hacker; Computer, Investigation, Science), Resources 3, Safe Place 2, Untouchable<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 3<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 11<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 3 dice]<br /> Heavy Pistol [+2L ranged; -2 Initiative; 5 dice]<br /> <b>Talent:</b> Compelling Madness; Frailty: Obvious Lunatic<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Eye Spy (Hack Surveillance), Madness &amp; Terror (Online Interaction)<br /> <br /> <i><b>Compelling Madness:</b></i> Maniacs only need a few minutes of observation to know a victim better than he knows himself. If a Maniac observes a character for five minutes, the Maniac can profile him. The Maniac rolls Intelligence + Resolve resisted by the targets Wits+Subterfuge. If successful, this functions as the Know Soul Dread Power (Chronicles of Darkness, pg. 146).<br /> In addition, if the target has a current Integrity of 5 or less, the Maniac may also use Social Maneuvering to influence that targets beliefs and goals; whenever the Maniac opens the targets final Door, they may spend a point of Willpower to substitute a targets Virtue, Vice or Aspiration for one of the Maniac\u2019s own.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Obvious Lunatic:</b></i> Maniacs are dangerous, and it\u2019s obvious to anyone who talks to them. They can keep it under wraps for a few minutes, but beyond that time, people around them feel threatened. Maniacs suffer a \u20133 penalty to all Social actions with others, unless that person is susceptible to their logic (currently suffering the Guilty or Leveraged Condition, or having a similar Virtue, Vice or Aspiration). The Maniac may spend a point of Willpower to negate this penalty until the end of the scene. </div></div> </div> </div></span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Maria Muerte</span></b><br /> The woman named \u201cMaria\u201d began her life abandoned on the steps of a church in Mexico City when she was only a few weeks old. The child was marked (some would say cursed) with a strange deformity that rendered her hairless, and with atrophied facial muscles that gave her a skull-like countenance and limited range of expression. Even at an early age, she demonstrated unnatural strength and outbursts of anger that left her peer terrified and the nuns convinced she was the spawn of demons, and all were relieved when she ran away from the orphanage as a teen. Since then, she has become an infamous enforcer for the Cartels, employing her inhuman strength to maim and kill at their behest. True, she would probably murder on a whim for free, but has come to appreciate money and notoriety.<br /> Maria is a tall woman with a hard, muscular physique. She is completely hairless, and has thin lips, sunken eyes, and hollow cheeks which make her face a living skull. Her skin (except for her face) is covered in elaborate, beautiful, tattoos. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Mutant; <b>Virtue:</b> Bravery; <b>Vice:</b> Violence<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Finds ways to channel or indulge her violent impulses<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 6, Dexterity 5, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 3, Composure 4<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 3, Brawl 4, Drive 2, Firearms 3, Larceny 3(Pick Pocket), Intimidate 4(Torture), Investigation 2, Occult 2(Superstition), Subterfuge 2(Disguise), Stealth 3, Streetwise 3(Cartel), Weaponry 3<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Closed Book 2, Fame 1, Iron Will, Multi-Lingual (English, Portuguese), Professional Training 3 (Criminal; Intimidate, Larceny, Streetwise), Resources 2, Status 3 (Cartel), Style: Street Fighting 4<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 4<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 12<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 16<br /> <b>Health:</b> 10<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+1L melee, 10 dice]<br /> Machete [+2L melee; -2 Initiative; 9 dice]<br /> Light Pistol [+1L ranged;-0 Initiative; 8 dice]<br /> <b>Talent:</b> Natural Weaponry (Hideous Strength)<br /> <b>Frailty:</b> Sensitivity (Cold Temperatures)<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Jump Scare, Numina (Awe), Regenerate 1<br /> <br /> <b><i>Natural Weaponry:</i> </b>The deformities of a Mutant work for him, at least with respect to murder. A Mutant might have sharp fangs, gnarled claws or even bony outgrowths from his forehead. His skin might be as tough as leather, or covered in a heavy layer of callus. The Mutant has either a natural attack method (claws, teeth, horns, etc.) that inflicts lethal damage as a +1 weapon or to have 1/1 points of armor<br /> <br /> <i><b>Sensitivity:</b></i> Mutants inspire fear and revulsion in all who see them. The Mutant suffers a -2 penalty to dice pools for Social rolls (except for Intimidation) against any character that can see or has seen his face, and any failures in such circumstances become dramatic failures. In addition, Mutants are all hypersensitive to some form of stimulus \u2014 bright light, powerful antiseptic scents, certain textures, sudden shifts in temperature, and so on. When the Mutant is confronted by their particular stimuli, they must make a Resolve+Composure roll or gain the Frightened Condition in regards to that stimuli until the end of the scene. </div></div> </div> </div></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T19:45:57-07:00","id":1250146,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Green</b></span><br /> The entities known only as \u201c<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places?p=1250123#post1250123\">The Green</a>\u201d are strange vegetable lifeforms, existing across a multitude of bodies but sharing a rudimentary conjoined consciousness. The organism has slender, leafy vines that blossom with fragrant yellow flowers and sprout plump seed pods near its roots. The creatures are nocturnal, and are capable of moving under their own power once the sun sets. They seem to have a remarkable aggression towards (some would even say hatred of) animal life, and will ambush such creatures when they are vulnerable (such as when asleep or distracted). The plants can produce cruel weaponry when it chooses to attack, manifesting sharp thorns dripping with digestive enzymes, poisonous secretions, busts of irritating pollen, and strangling tendrils.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Best At:</b> 7 (Attacking Animals, Ambushing its prey)<br /> <b>Worst At:</b> 1 (Mental or Social Actions)<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Grow and Devour<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 3<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 8<br /> <b>Size:</b> 4<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Only active at night, dormant in temperatures colder than freezing<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Jump Scare, Natural Weapons, Regenerate, Snare, Toxic </div></div> </div> </div></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T05:52:17-07:00","id":1261928,"title":"","content":"If you're still here, Reighnell, could you help me write up the Celebrants from that endgame scenario in the God-Machine Chronicle? Though they might be ephemeral. It's hard to tell. They are just so interesting and they seem to have been an abandoned major setting element","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T15:42:02-07:00","id":1262009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1261928#post1261928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're still here, Reighnell, could you help me write up the Celebrants from that endgame scenario in the God-Machine Chronicle? Though they might be ephemeral. It's hard to tell. They are just so interesting and they seem to have been an abandoned major setting element</div> </div> </div> </div>I will look into this and see what I can come up with. Besides, it will be a good excuse to get in some writing practice!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T19:06:25-07:00","id":1262032,"title":"","content":"Thanks a bunch. I'll try to help however I can too","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T17:17:38-07:00","id":1262437,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Celebrants</b><br /> <br /> I had kind of forgotten much much good material is in the God Machine Chronicle.While I can see why subsequent books haven't picked up on the Celebrants - the setting is already filthy with &quot;Demons&quot; of all sorts, the idea of a &quot;Devil Machine&quot; that opposes the GMis very intriguing. But toying with the idea, here is what I have come up with. I decided on a specific Celebrant using the Horror rules(not quite enough meat on the concept to run a full set of new mechanics)<b>.</b> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Laughing Massacre</b></span><br /> The universe demands balance. Not even the God Machine is exempt from this rule. And as the God Machine is served by Angels, whatever enigmatic force that serves as its opposite number is attended by Devils. If asked, these creatures might call themselves \u201cCelebrants\u201d. They rebel against the passionless, sterile order of the god Machine in favor of pleasure, pain, and reckless abandon, finding wisdom in excess. Whereas the Unchained seek a version of Hell free from their former master, the Celebrants are Hell.<br /> The Celebrant known as the Laughing Massacre appears during celebrations, the more bacchanal, the better. When it arrives, it drives and intensifies the revelry, turning normal gatherings into drunken, orgiastic debauches, which nearly always culminate in depravity, violence and death.<br /> Th Laughing Massacre almost always assumes the form an attractive woman, except for her rows of needle sharp teeth and shifting, runic scars covering her skin. Despite this, no one seems to notice these peculiarities blood and treat her like a welcome guest. She smiles constantly and speaks with a hint of a laugh in the edge of her voice.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Joyous; Vice: Excess<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To experience and share the limits of sensation<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 5, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 6, Dexterity 6, Stamina 6<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 6, Manipulation 5, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 4, Empathy 4, Expression 4, Intimidate 4, Occult 3, Persuasion 6, Socialize 6, Survival 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Hardy 2, Inspiring, Indomitable, Iron Stamina 2, Striking Looks 2, Sympathetic<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 6<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 13<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 17<br /> <b>Health:</b> 11<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0L melee; 10 dice]<br /> Bite [+1L melee; 10 dice; Armor Piercing 1]<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Natural Weapon (Bite), Numina (Emotional Aura, Mortal Mask), Immortal</div></div> </div> </div></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-02T21:09:06-07:00","id":1264373,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a> What do you think of this Slasher that I made using your rules?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I was told that he is too sane and human to qualify for a Scourge. Any tips on how to make him more monstrous?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">They say that one can swear their firstborn child to the Devil in exchange for wealth, power or whatever else one desires. The decadent and corrupt parents of young Daniel Pierce had more wealth and power than most could dream of having, but that wasn't enough for them. They made a pact with a creature of the Inferno, and their son was marked from birth by red skin, completely black eyes and horrific natural weapons. What they didn't know is that the Infernal didn't want to take away the child, but to groom him into a servant of evil in the mortal world. Daniel wasted no time in murdering his parents in order to transfer the inheritance to himself, but then donated almost all of his wealth to charitable causes. Nowadays he lives in a cabin inside the woods, hoping no one comes around to see his demonic visage and tempt him toward sin. But his Infernal heritage and painful childhood have left him withdrawn and maladjusted, resulting in a terrible desire to be loved and accepted. Wherever he goes, Daniel tries to make others believe he is still worth saving but ends up making more victims than friends. His agonized lamentations can occasionally be heard in the woods, earning him the name of &quot;The Dirge Devil&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Mutant<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Kindness<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Isolation<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To manipulate others into showing him compassion<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 6, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 4, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 1, Manipulation 5, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics (Literature) 2, Crafts 1, Investigation 3, Medicine 1, Occult 2, Athletics (Chasing) 3, Brawl (Natural Weaponry) 4, Stealth (Stalking) 3, Survival (Tracking) 4, Empathy 1, Expression (Singing) 3, Intimidation (Displays Of Strength) 5, Persuasion (Guilt) 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Investigative Aide 1 (Survival), Greyhound 1, Closed Book 3, Iron Will 2, Pusher 1, Sympathetic 2, Untouchable 1, Killer Instinct 3 (Advanced 1), Aura Reading 3<br /> <br /> <b>Potency:</b> 4<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 13<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 14<br /> <b>Health: </b>11<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+1L melee, 10 dice]<br /> <b>Talent:</b> Natural Weaponry (Claws, Fangs, Horns And Impaling Tail)<br /> <b>Frailty:</b> Sensitivity (Religious Symbols)<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Numen (Hallucination, Mortal Mask, Perfect Lie)<br /> <br /> <b>Natural Weaponry:</b> The deformities of a Mutant work for him, at least with respect to murder. A Mutant might have sharp fangs, gnarled claws or even bony outgrowths from his forehead. His skin might be as tough as leather, or covered in a heavy layer of callus. The Mutant has either a natural attack method (claws, teeth, horns, etc.) that inflicts lethal damage as a +1 weapon or to have 1/1 points of Armor.<br /> <br /> <b>Sensitivity:</b> Mutants inspire fear and revulsion in all who see them. The Mutant suffers a -2 penalty to dice pools for Social rolls (except for Intimidation) against any character that can see or has seen his face, and any failures in such circumstances become Dramatic Failures. In addition, Mutants are all hypersensitive to some form of stimulus \u2014 bright light, powerful antiseptic scents, certain textures, sudden shifts in temperature, and so on. When the Mutant is confronted by their particular stimuli, they must make a Resolve+Composure roll or gain the Frightened Condition in regards to that stimuli until the end of the scene.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-24-2019, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-04T05:20:40-08:00","id":1264591,"title":"","content":"How about making Daniel stuck in a vicious cycle? When loneliness becomes unbearable he goes forth to buy love from others. He showers gifts and help onto whoever catches his eye. However, whether through his infernal powers or corrupting behavior, the outcome is always tainted. Inevitably one of two things happen. Either the recipient recognizes him for a harmful presence he is and rejects him, or becomes comfortable not just with his demonic appearance but with his corrosive influence. In the former case, rejection makes Daniel respond in a lethal manner, and then flee into hermitage, saddled with grief. In the latter case, Daniel recognizes history of his parents repeating itself, and punishes his former friend for betraying his hopes. It's always one of these outcomes. It's hard to tell whether Daniel is cursed, or whether, on some level, he wants this to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-04T21:11:52-08:00","id":1264687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1262437#post1262437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: Celebrants</b><br /> <br /> I had kind of forgotten much much good material is in the God Machine Chronicle.While I can see why subsequent books haven't picked up on the Celebrants - the setting is already filthy with &quot;Demons&quot; of all sorts, the idea of a &quot;Devil Machine&quot; that opposes the GMis very intriguing. But toying with the idea, here is what I have come up with. I decided on a specific Celebrant using the Horror rules(not quite enough meat on the concept to run a full set of new mechanics)<b>.</b> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Laughing Massacre</b></span><br /> The universe demands balance. Not even the God Machine is exempt from this rule. And as the God Machine is served by Angels, whatever enigmatic force that serves as its opposite number is attended by Devils. If asked, these creatures might call themselves \u201cCelebrants\u201d. They rebel against the passionless, sterile order of the god Machine in favor of pleasure, pain, and reckless abandon, finding wisdom in excess. Whereas the Unchained seek a version of Hell free from their former master, the Celebrants are Hell.<br /> The Celebrant known as the Laughing Massacre appears during celebrations, the more bacchanal, the better. When it arrives, it drives and intensifies the revelry, turning normal gatherings into drunken, orgiastic debauches, which nearly always culminate in depravity, violence and death.<br /> Th Laughing Massacre almost always assumes the form an attractive woman, except for her rows of needle sharp teeth and shifting, runic scars covering her skin. Despite this, no one seems to notice these peculiarities blood and treat her like a welcome guest. She smiles constantly and speaks with a hint of a laugh in the edge of her voice.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Joyous; Vice: Excess<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To experience and share the limits of sensation<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 5, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 6, Dexterity 6, Stamina 6<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 6, Manipulation 5, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 4, Empathy 4, Expression 4, Intimidate 4, Occult 3, Persuasion 6, Socialize 6, Survival 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Hardy 2, Inspiring, Indomitable, Iron Stamina 2, Striking Looks 2, Sympathetic<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 6<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 13<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 17<br /> <b>Health:</b> 11<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0L melee; 10 dice]<br /> Bite [+1L melee; 10 dice; Armor Piercing 1]<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Natural Weapon (Bite), Numina (Emotional Aura, Mortal Mask), Immortal</div></div> </div> </div></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Quite like what you did here. Please don't take me chiming in as criticism, I admire the work and wish to contribute a couple insights I have. <br /> <br /> My first insight is the Immortal Dread power is a <i>perfect</i> fit, but a reminder it comes with a Resurrection Clause, which would be good to define. In this case my suggestion would be the clause be something like &quot;The completion of a Summoning Ritual which brings that Celebrant from Hell to Earth&quot;, whether the ritual be an occult ceremony with multiple cultist practitioners culminating in a bloody sacrifice or completing some arcane infernally enchanted puzzle box depends on what suits a particular chronicle. Also, I think Rapture would be a better fit than Emotional Aura.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-05T06:02:52-08:00","id":1264729,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>RE:The Laughing Massacre</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">This is a good observation. It was actually a deliberate choice to avoid filling in certain details, like the &quot;resurrection clause&quot; in the Immortal Dread Power. This is primarily to leave such a thing up to the individual Storyteller that might use the Horror. It is always my intent that any of the things I create can and should be modified to taste. That being said,I am considering going over some of my older builds to see if they can be tweaked or updated, so I will keep this suggestion in mind.<br /> Also, I went with Emotional Aura over Rapture since Emotional Aura is an area of effect while Rapture is single target - I see the Laughing Massacre encouraging wanton behavior by mere presence rather than by directly targeting people (which isn't set in stone, and the gaming police won't show up if you give her both).</span><br /> <br /> <b>Re: The Dirge Devil</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">@</span></span>GibberingEloquence - Your mechanics are solid, and I like a Slasher that is driven by something other than pure misanthropy. I would take <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7593_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7593\" data-vbnamecard=\"7593\">Teatime</a> suggestion to heart. Crank up the creatures ugly cycle of behavior - When a victim is chosen<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">, it is almost impossible for them to satisfy the creatures desires. Sooner or later, they will do ~something~ to disappoint this monster, and then they will die, and then the Devil will be sad and lonely. Repeat. This feels like a good one for a Hunter game,since there is enough of a sympathetic nature at work to challenge the cells convictions. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T22:10:40-08:00","id":1269755,"title":"","content":"<b>Rasputin</b><br /> Gregori Rasputin, The Mad Monk, that acted as friend, adviser, and healer to Tzar Nicholas II. A legendary figure whose existence is historically confirmed but whose true history has been white-washed with both mortal governments' and various supernatural conspiracies' misinformation campaigns to enforce a sane mundane materialistic world view where no one really believes in the supernatural. Especially certain mystery cults within the Seers of the Throne in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1164738-classic-wod-traditions-and-technocracy-converted-into-22-mystery-cult-initiations#post1164738\">Ouroboros Institute</a> or other such Mystery Cult Initiations which also vanguard both the the actual timeline <u>and</u> the official narrative of history, but also <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1164738-classic-wod-traditions-and-technocracy-converted-into-22-mystery-cult-initiations#post1164738\">Illuminati</a> or similarly functioning Mystery Cult Initiations that hype conspiracies theories and obvious hoax to produce cynics and skeptics.<br /> <br /> Despite how outrageously exaggerated some accounts of historical,or even how fictionalized in comic book series or movie franchise may seem, the truth is he dabbled in forces no mortal should dare contemplate, and the legends fall short of his mortal death in 1916, and especially what he became after. His death was actually worse than the standard mortal accounts since the enchanted nature of the knives of the angry mob, that Judas Iscariot's Relic Noose was used to hang and drain his life leaving him a corpse husk still struggling against his bonds, and the soul severing Death magic on the bullets wielded by the British Secret Agent Seer of the Throne are not part of the legendary account. The Seer of the Throne pylon assassinating him with the help of an angry mob was just following orders from the Hegemony due to being Fate Seers foretold that Gregori Rasputin was a potential danger to the whole of the Exarchs prison and plan, and Time Seers peered into the future and saw that Gregori Rasputin's designated time to die in those at time and his presence in history would end at that point. It had been planned to kill and delete Gregori from the time line. After the official autopsy was staged a Pylon of Seers of the Throne attempted to sequester the body and began a ritual to edit him from history. The spell wouldn't work because after his death it appears that Gregori Rasputin had already become an invalid target for Time Effects before they even cast the spell, and since that discovery, it became even retroactive. The Pylon was extremely apprehensive and one of their members went mad from gazing too deep into the Mystery with Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> After the Rasputin's first resurrection, the Seers of the Thrones chain of command developed protocols for killing him, doing damage control, and then dealing with the horror he releases when he is killed when his bane is triggered. Rasputin has effectively devoured a massive amounts of both Seer of the Throne and Pentacle resources, not to even mention the mayhem Rasputin causes because he relishes being an out of context for other supernatural communities.<br /> When in the Abyss due to using Abyssal Egress, Rasputin uses Eyes of the Master to locate a suitable point re-enter reality.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Sacrilegious <b>Vice:</b> Devoted<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Remake the cosmos into a literal hell filled with sanity-rending horrors; Serve the will of his elder god master from outside the cosmos;<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 6, Wits 6, Resolve 7<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 7<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 8, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 5, Crafts 2, Investigation 3, Medicine 2, Occult 5, Politics 3, Athletics 1, Brawl 1, Larceny 1, Stealth 3, Survival 1, Weaponry 2, Animal Ken 1, Empathy 2, Expression 1, Intimidation 4, Persuasion 4, Socialize 2, Street Wise 3, Subterfuge 4<br /> <b>Merits:</b> &lt;Insert Supernatural Site Last Resurrected At&gt; 4, Mystery Cult Initiation 5 (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1188352#post1188352\">Cult of the Yonder</a>), Mystery Cult Initiation 5 (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/799082-cofd-diy-mystery-cults?p=1209625#post1209625\">Mystery Cult &amp; Nameless Order: Secret Order of the Gate</a>), Mystery Cult Initiation 5 (Please insert Lovecraftian or demonic Mystery Cult relevant for your Chronicle here)<br /> <b>Merits from Mystery Cult Initiations:</b> Destiny (Doom: Releasing his God from the Abyss) 3, Dead Pan 3, Occultation 2, Language (Parametric) 1, Astral Adept 3, Familiar (Rasputin's Sacrilege) 2, Dream 1<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 9<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 10<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Being killed in such a way as to release an avatar of Elder God master into the world.<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee; 4 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b><br /> <b>EYES OF THE MASTER</b><br /> The Rasputin has a specific form of remote viewing he can practice. He is able to see and hear through the eyes and eyes of any member of Mystery Cult Initiation with fewer points in the particular type merit than he. Using this ability requires the expenditure of 1 Willpower per hour, and the cult member being seen through can be chosen by whatever criteria Rasputin can imagine as long as the definition can limit the definition to a single individual. The Rasputin remains aware of its surroundings while surveilling.<br /> <br /> <b>IMMORTAL</b><br /> Rasputin isn\u2019t bound by mortal laws of life and death. He\u2019s not indestructible, per se, but if he\u2019s killed by anything other than his Bane, he just comes back in a later scene like nothing happened. Even if he\u2019s destroyed with his Bane, he\u2019s never really gone \u2014 an accursed ritual of a bloody human sacrifice with the intention of resurrecting him done at a location which holds extreme supernatural power (any such supernatural site like a Hallow, Locui, Strange Place as would be covered by a 5 point merit) can always bring the Rasputin back for a sequel story. That location now belongs to Rasputin, but loses a Merit dot of potency as part of the Price, making it a 4 point version of itself. If the site was controlled by someone else when this sacrifice is preformed, the former owners benefit from Sanctity of Merits, as the site is no longer considered theirs.<br /> <br /> <b>KNOWING GAZE</b><br /> Rasputin can see into the depths of his victim\u2019s soul. By spending 1 Willpower, he automatically learns the victim\u2019s Virtue, Vice, Aspirations, and current Integrity (or Major Template Equivalent). By spending an additional Willpower point, it learns the circumstances of the character\u2019s most recent failed breaking point. Subsequent Willpower points reveal older breaking points. If Rasputin uses his knowledge against the victim, he earns an exceptional success on a roll of three successes or more.<br /> <br /> <b>DARK MIRACLES</b><br /> The Rasputin is capable of performing miraculous feats at the request of humans. Dark Miracles include, but aren\u2019t necessarily limited to:<br /> \u2022 Removing (or applying) any Condition or Tilt (or<br /> similar affliction not modeled by these mechanics).<br /> \u2022 Granting any Merit, Skill, or Attribute at 5 dots.<br /> \u2022 Causing someone to die.<br /> \u2022 Fulfilling an Aspiration of the victim.<br /> \u2022 Produce either a group of Minion Horrors, or a single Potency 5 Horror<br /> The Rasputin cannot do any of these things unless explicitly asked to by a living human being. Rasputin can only grant requests which represent one of the victim's Aspirations. Doing so requires Rasputin perform an extended action (1 Minute Interval) ritual Resolve + Occult with 10 + 1-5 (depending on relative power of Miracle) Successes, requiring the presence of either an Supernatural Object or Location represented in Merit Dots equal to the relative potency of the Dark Miracle.<br /> Finally, all magic of this sort comes with a price. When the Rasputin grants a victim\u2019s wish, the victim\u2019s Aspirations which was the bases of the request is destroyed utterly. The character will never be able to fulfill it or replace it with another Aspiration. Rasputin can't perform Dark Miracles for humans without Aspirations to lose. They also gain the Tainted Condition. Due to Rasputin's sensibilities and own Aspirations he uses this power by twisting the intention of the Aspiration so that it's technically fulfilled but in a manner to make the world a much more horrific place. It is the wording of the Aspiration, not the request which matters in this case.<br /> <br /> <b>ABYSSAL ENTRANCE</b><br /> No matter how secure his victims think they are, by spending 1 Willpower the Rasputin may suddenly appear in the scene. He manifests out of the Abyss via any patch of darkness. Any character witnessing this entrance must succeed on a reflexive Resolve + Composure roll or gain the Shaken Condition.<br /> If the characters have actively taken appropriate measures to keep Rasputin out (lighting the area to an extreme extent that there are no patches of darkness, etc.) it will take the creature one full turn to manifest, as a preternaturally black silhouette of Rasputin forms on a surface as he casts the shadow that he can step from the Abyss, giving the characters time to react. If not, he\u2019s just there as a reflexive action and can take one more action before anyone can react.<br /> <br /> <b>ABYSSAL EGRESS</b><br /> No matter how secure against egress a location or situation maybe, by spending 1 Willpower the Rasputin may suddenly leave in the scene. He steps into the Abyss via any patch of darkness. Any Sleeper witnessing this egress must succeed on a reflexive Resolve + Composure roll or gain the Shaken Condition.<br /> If the characters have actively taken appropriate measures to keep Rasputin from escaping (lighting the area to an extreme extent that there are no patches of darkness, containing him in an pocket realm where supernatural power don't work, incapacitating him in any ways that'd normally prevent him from using a power or spending a Willpower Point, etc.) it will take the Rasputin one full turn to disappear, in that case of this type of resistance leaving behind a preternaturally black silhouette psychically traumatizing Abyssal stain (Examining the Abyssal stain with supernatural senses results in a variety of unpleasant conditions, from various Paradox Conditions, Tainted Condition, up to possibly even the Been Yonder Condition for extreme cases), giving the characters time to react. If not, he\u2019s just disappears as a reflexive action and no one can react, but doesn't leave an Abyssal stain.<br /> If Rasputin is without Willpower, he can still use this power, because temporally paradoxically leaving the Abyssal stain fulfills his Aspirations &quot;Remake the cosmos into a literal hell filled with sanity-rending horrors&quot;, allowing the power to be used but leaves him at 0 Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>ABSENCE OF TIME</b> (By <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\">amechra</a>)<br /> Rasputin is always considered to be an invalid target for Supernal magic belonging to the Time Arcana. In addition, any spell of that Arcana that interacts (even indirectly) with the Rasputin unravels as if exposed to 9 successes on a Dissonance roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rasputin's Sacrilege</b> (Rank 1 Acamoth)<br /> Crawling through Geotia's spectrum of Twilight is a hulking burbling self-devouring mass of nuclear chaos constantly erupting eyes bearing witness to that which shouldn't be known, mouths muttering foul truths too terrible for the sane to comprehend, and other features boiling to the surface which defy description which melt back in and are slurped by hungry mouths.<br /> <b>Power:</b> 3<br /> <b>Finesse:</b> 4<br /> <b>Resistance:</b> 1<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Twilight Form, Familiar<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Sacrilege 1<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Presence of Paradox, Dement, That-Which-Must-Not-Be-Seen<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Items Blessed via Religious Abjuration Rituals which are Sacred<br /> <b>Size:</b> 10<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 11<br /> [B]Defense: 4<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 5<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 5<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 10/<br /> <br /> <b>Presence of Paradox</b> (by <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\">amechra</a>)<br /> The ephemeral being is thoroughly tainted by the stuff of the Abyss - treat it as if it were an entire crowd of Sleepers for the purposes of calculating Paradox dice pools, except it adds dice equal to its Rank rather than just one. In addition, it may spend Essence reflexively to cancel Mana spent to mitigate a Paradox dice pool on a one-to-one basis.<br /> <br /> <b>That-Which-Must-Not-Be-Seen</b> by <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader\">Pale_Crusader</a><br /> The ephemeral being is antithetical to the discovery of secrets and powers that reveal information. Such active or deliberate use of powers while the entity in the perception of the user applies Broken, Madness, or Fugue Condition those attempting to use the power. This applies from Auspex, various Uratha gifts that reveal information, Numina like Omen or Seek, to anything more than Peripheral Mage Sight, and any other power which is reasonably similar to those examples. Also the Condition is considered to be caused as if from resistant source meaning supernatural affects fail to remove the condition, and they must be resolved naturally. Additionally rolls of Failure are downgraded to Dramatic Failures, Success are downgraded to Failures, and Exceptional Success are downgraded to a mere success, after the completion of all the rolls in the case of extended rolls.<br /> <br /> Conditions Rasputin Has:<br /> <br /> <b>Been Yonder</b> [Persistent]<br /> You've been in the Abyss either mentally or with your whole being, experiencing in each moment as countless eternal epochs of cosmic apostatizing exposure to things minds were not mean to know. Suffer a Breaking Points simply by thinking about your experience within the Abyss, remembering it, or being reminded of it as long as you have either Wisdom or Integrity to lose. You also qualify to join the Mystery Cult of the Yonder if you explore your subconscious connection to it.<br /> <b>Causes:</b> Experience being within formless timeless portions of the Abyss, Having Amnesia of that experience removed, Have the mental totality of that experience artificial transplanted within your mind (Which require Mind 5, or an appropriate Influence 4 by an Acamoth to Create an exact copy of an existing experience, mere modification of things that can be mundanely known does not suffice)<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Gain the Amnesia Condition concerning time in the Abyss<br /> <br /> <b>Tainted </b>(9 Dice) [Persistent]<br /> Your character committed diablerie (or the equivalent act of supernatural self-damnation), and now retains traces of her victim\u2019s soul. Once per chapter, the victim can come back to haunt your character and try to force her destruction. This brief burst penalizes any one dice pool by the victim\u2019s Blood Potency dots, or adds to a dice pool opposing your character.<br /> This takes the form of subtle manifestations, or whispers that urge and distract. Your character may have multiple instances of this Condition, reflecting different victims.<br /> <b>Possible Sources: </b>Diablerie, Palpable Damnation<br /> <b>Beat:</b> n/a<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Rasputin was built to be a non-combat threat designed to fill a whole Chronicle, which is highly resistant to brute force solutions. He can enter or exit scenes as needed, and is in no danger from the PCs until they are potent enough to be world shakers. Even then, they'd need a lot of prep or out of the box thinking to be able to enact his Bane, which causes a whole other set of issues since it releases &quot;His Elder God Master&quot; into the material world. The challenge he really presents is his ability to make the Aspirations of mere mortals real in horrific ways, and the effort needed to clean up those messes. Also he acts a catalyst for stories of politics if he gets involved with a supernatural community, and in the beginning of the Chronicle I'd expect it may be easy to underestimated him at first for the havoc that can be done with he merely lending support to a particular faction to further his ultimate ends.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd like to see other peoples' interpretation of a 10 Potency Horror that could be made if they borrowed some Dread Powers from the Idigam from Werewolf: Forsaken, and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/925972-2e-abyssal-aspects-and-numina#post925972\">Abyssal Aspects &amp; Numina</a> to make what manifests when he dies. Thank you in advance,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 12-04-2018, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T16:57:10-08:00","id":1269934,"title":"","content":"Is this a OWOD reference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T17:50:52-08:00","id":1269948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1269934#post1269934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this a OWOD reference?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Pieces of it do, though.<br /> <br /> If you're referring to the Mystery Cult Initiations linked from the description, I created those based on <i>Mage: Ascension</i> Traditions and Conventions, but as Mystery Cult Initiations which overlay over top current Mage Setting as an addition instead of a substitution, but those Mystery Cult Initiations represent archetypical roles that Seers of the Throne sub-organizations for the oppression and snuffing out of the potential for the masses to Awaken. Guard the timeline, keep the official historic narrative intact, make people cynical and skeptical, make people not believe in the supernatural, are all agendas the Seers of the Throne seek, which is why I made the link to my content for the Old World Technocracy conversion I made, but other Mystery Cult Initiations with similar function and goals fit right in if you aren't interested in borrowing those pieces too.<br /> <br /> Since &quot;Guard the timeline, keep the official historic narrative intact, make people cynical and skeptical, make people not believe in the supernatural&quot; are really impressive goals in scope and scale having whole Cults dedicated to them is adventurous and makes sense. As a side note I also filled out the other 6 Prelacy, and created a bunch of Conversions for the Technocracy (Genuinely new content) for the conversion and keep it balanced with the Traditions, fleshed out, and enjoy a little world building at the same time. Including the whole conversion I did isn't required for Rasputin to fit in a setting, those are just there for ease of reference, instead just have your own Mystery Cult Initiations, cherry pick the sub-mystery cults and not the Technocracy, or even eschew that and just have certain powerful international groups of Seers dedicated to the tasks without having any mechanical aspects. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1164738-classic-wod-traditions-and-technocracy-converted-into-22-mystery-cult-initiations\"> Here is the Link to the Conversion I did.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 11-22-2018, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T03:32:51-08:00","id":1270301,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Sammael</b> </span>(Horde)<br /> <a href=\"https://hellboy.fandom.com/wiki/Sammael\" target=\"_blank\">Aside from the obvious superior strength and agility he possesses, Sammael also possessed incredible regenerative abilities, earning him the title of &quot;Hound of Resurrection&quot;. This allowed him to dislocate his limbs to reach in directions that most creatures cannot, with any broken bones or sustained injury inflicted on his body can be regenerated back to its original form. However this does not mean that Sammael is immune to death as grievously injuring his body is known to incapacitate him for several minutes. Therefore, it was shown to be extremely difficult to fatally injure the creature, as it took explosions, electricution, incineration, and otherwise extreme bodily damage, such as being crushed, to for him to be killed. This was negated by Sammael's ability to split his essence into two, allowing him to be reborn and grow in numbers each time one falls.<br /> <br /> Each Sammael was capable of laying a cluster eggs, specifically in dark and wet environments, as they were sensitive to heat and light. When one Sammael was killed, two of these eggs break away and rapidly matured until there were twin clones of the monster. This process repeated itself every time one was killed, thereby allowing Sammael to multiply himself and grow in numbers</a><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Violently cause death and destruction, Serve being which triggered Resurrection Clause of Immortal Dread Power<br /> <b>Best Dice Pool:</b> 7 (Attacking Savagely, Chases using its climbing and jumping abilities, Placing its eggs in places for its Immortal Dread Power)<br /> <b>Worst Dice Pool:</b> 1 (Anything requiring beyond bestial intellect or monstrous social graces)<br /> <b>All Other Pools:</b> 3<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 3<br /> <b>Ban:</b> May not Regenerate a particular body if it died from cellular death, such as acid submersion, complete immolation, certain poisons, significant radiation, or electrocution.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Completely Destroy every Egg laid and cellular death of all current bodies in a single.<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> 5<br /> <b>IMMORTAL</b><br /> Sammael isn\u2019t bound by mortal laws of life and death. He\u2019s not indestructible, per se, but if he\u2019s killed by anything other than his Bane, he just comes back in a later scene like nothing happened. This happens because Sammael's off screen regeneration from even death, but also because it is a prolific egg layer. Each time Sammael is killed in a way that its ban prevents Regeneration, two of its grape-sized eggs hatch and instantly mature to full adult copies. Even if Sammael is destroyed in a what which is his Bane, he\u2019s never really gone \u2014 he leaves a single glimmer of his infernal presence which may be contained in a blessed, consecrated, or sacred reliquary. If the infernal presence is not in an intact reliquary, an accursed incantation near his presence with the intention of resurrecting him can always bring the Sammael back for a sequel story.<br /> <br /> <b>WALL CLIMB</b><br /> Sammael can walk up walls or even cling to the ceiling, and can move its full Speed while doing so.<br /> <br /> <b>PRODIGIOUS LEAP</b><br /> Sammael can make great, bounding leaps; by spending 1 Willpower, it can jump about four stories straight up or across a six-lane highway (or the equivalent distance).<br /> <br /> <b>EGG LAYER</b><br /> Sammael's lashing tongue injects the eggs it uses for its Immortal Dread Power with each vicious bite or tongue grab. This Dread Power inflicts the moderate version of either the Implanted Tilt. This happens automatically when the Sammael inflicts damage with its bite, or it can spend 1 Willpower and roll an 7 dice contested by the victim\u2019s Stamina, as it lashes out with its 5 meter ranged tongue grab, which inflicts only 1 Bashing but counts as a grab, and inflicts Implanted (Moderate) Tilt. The Trigger for the eggs to erupt from the host is the triggering of any of Sammael's clone's Ban, thus cause eggs within hosts to hatch first. Each success in either the tongue grab or bite deposits an egg.<br /> <br /> <b>REGENERATE</b><br /> The creature possesses incredible powers of regeneration. As a reflexive action once per turn, the creature can spend 1 Willpower, healing one point of lethal damage or two points of bashing damage for each Willpower expended in this way.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">New Tilt!</span><br /> <br /> <b>IMPLANTED (Moderate or Gave)</b><br /> You have eggs or otherwise immature offspring of horrors within your body. These unwanted guests will violent erupt from your body given a trigger defined by the source of the Dread Power to inflict this Tilt.<b><br /> Moderate: </b>You need to take 1 lethal damage (bashing on exception success) while you or someone else makes a Dexterity + Medicine with at least a field surgery kit to extract the unwanted stowaways, one success per stowaway. If one of the implanted are triggered you gain the Knocked Down and take a lethal wound as it erupt from your body and matures.<br /> <b>Grave:</b> Requires advanced operation done by a full surgical team in a proper medical facility, 10 Success on an extended Dexterity + Medicine roll with each check representing an hour of surgery. If successful it leave them with the Immobilized Tilt for a day while they recover. If the hatching is triggered in a Grave Implanted tilt the person with the tilt takes the adult creature's highest full attack die pool, ignoring Defense as lethal damage (aka a Coup de Grace) as the creature emerges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 11-24-2018, 06:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-04T00:19:54-08:00","id":1272792,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Anak'vog'soth</b></span><br /> The Collector-of-the-Lost, Grasping-Giant-of-the-Deepest-Darkness, God-of-Those-That-Are-Not, are but a couple of the epitaphs this Elder God has. An eyeless towering mass of slick gray whipping tentacles as large as a sky scraper dwells within the Abyss, and is ever hungry for influence over the Lie and Supernal Realms. It has the power to reform people, places, and things which are attempted to be removed from reality if there is a sliver of Abyssal taint for it to transmit its influence through. Anak'vog'soth craves existence like a junkie wants their fix, like a deeply sick perverse lecher wants profane sexual gratification, it wants to be with the constant fierceness of the intensity found distilled in the last seconds of the insane fever dreams of consciousness of a person whose fight to breath but can't draw air. Its ability to transform things people have attempted to erase from existence into abyssal versions twisted towards its ultimate goal to exist and the horror it'd inflict upon the world if it did and the two most frightening things about this Abyssal Intrusion.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Incomprehensibly Alien <b>Vice:</b> Existential<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Create of web of abyssal agents to promote its material existence;<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 10, Wits 5, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 10, Dexterity 10, Stamina 10<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 5, Manipulation 1, Composure 5<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 5, Crafts 5, Investigation 5, Occult 5, Athletics 5, Brawl 5, Stealth 5, Survival 5, Empathy 5, Intimidation 5, Subterfuge 5<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Mystery Cult Initiation 5 (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1188352#post1188352\">Cult of the Yonder</a>), Grappling 3, Choke Hold 2, Telepathy 5<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 10<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 100<br /> <b>Initiative: 15</b><br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 45<br /> <b>Health:</b> 110<br /> <b>Ban:</b> May not directly attack those in a ritual powered by souls and human sacrifice until the ritual is over unless an adherent of the ritual causes it to be damaged.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Ritual powered by the sacrifice of 100 Humans along with their Souls for the sole purpose of banishing Anak'vog'soth from reality, which as the keystone element of the ritual at the final moment the last human sacrificed must be a Human Cultist of an Abyssal Mystery Cult whom must then be attempted to be sincerely intended to be erased from reality is preformed in its presence. Completing the Ritual inflicts 1 Aggravated wound each round until it is back in the Abyss. (This Keystone individual is always transformed into an Immortal servant of Anak'vog'soth in the process, acting as a note if additional of those sacrificed qualify for Anak'vog'soth to make servants, it The Seers of the Throne accomplish sincere intension to erase the cultist from reality by not telling their subordinates that the ritual actually create another Servant for Horror for Anak'vog'soth because knowing the truth would cause the ritual to fail. Depending on the politically advantageous the Pylon's untimely demise may or may not be will often dictate if they are informed that they are able to be attacked by spiteful Anak'vog'soth while its flesh flakes away after the ritual.)<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+5B melee; 15 Dice pool 8 again vs &gt; Size 100]<br /> Throwing Compact Car or similar object [+8L ranged(12 yards, 24 yards, 48 yards );15 dice pool]<br /> Throwing Sports Car or similar object [+10L ranged(10 yards, 20 yards, 40 yards );15 dice pool]<br /> Throwing Luxury Car or similar object [+12L ranged(8 yards, 16 yards, 32 yards );15 dice pool]<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b><br /> <b>IMMORTAL</b><br /> Anak'vog'soth isn\u2019t bound by mortal laws of life and death. It\u2019s not indestructible, per se, but if it\u2019s killed by anything other than its Bane, it just comes back in a later scene like nothing happened. Even if it\u2019s destroyed with its Bane, it\u2019s never really gone \u2014 a specially arranged death of its servants t prevent the Immortal Dread power its servants have, can always bring the Anak'vog'soth back for a sequel story. Since Anak'vog'soth always grants Immortal Dread Power when transforming its Servants into Horrors and their Banes are always &quot;Being killed in such a way as to release an avatar of Elder God master into the world&quot; means avatar.<br /> <br /> <b>COLOSSUS</b> (By <i>Werewolf: The Forsaken</i>)<br /> Anak'vog'soth is immense of form, a towering monstrosity that can simply shrug off lesser attacks. Anak'vog'soth increases its Health by its Size, and gains general Armor equal to its Stamina. This armor is completely ignored by attacks made with the Anak'vog'soth\u2019s bane. Against creatures and objects of smaller Size than the Anak'vog'soth, its attacks benefit from the 8-Again rule.<br /> <br /> <b>JUGGERNAUT</b> (By <i>Werewolf: The Forsaken</i>)<br /> Not much can stop Anak'vog'soth; bricks, concrete, steel, it brushes all aside. The Anak'vog'soth adds its Strength as automatic points of damage when it strikes an object or structure.<br /> <br /> <b>TRANSFORMATION OF THE OBLITERATED</b><br /> The Anak'vog'soth is capable of performing a miraculous transformation of people, places, or items which carry both abyssal taint and the sincere intention to edited from reality. Transformations of the Lost include, but aren\u2019t necessarily limited to:<br /> \u2022 Make the Cultist whom someone sincerely attempts to edit from existence into a Horror with a Potency equal to 4 + Highest level currently held at death of a Mystery Cult Initiation which is empowered by Abyssal influence, phenomenon forces, or entity.<br /> \u2022 Take a item which a human wished didn't exist and preformed either extensive conspiracy cover up to destroy and conceal it ever existed or someone preformed supernatural steps to actually edit it from reality, but the item or a being involved in the attempt must also be significantly fettered to Abyssal influence, phenomenon forces, or entity, and turn it into an Abyssal flavored Relic which only work positively servants for Anak'vog'soth, acts the Relic to start an Abyssal Mystery Cults Initiations, or helps produce Horror which are Servants of Anak'vog'soth.<br /> \u2022 Take a place which was destroyed and then extensive conspiracy cover up to hide the fact it ever existed, or supernatural steps to edit it from reality were taken, but the location or person involved in the attempt is significantly fettered to Abyssal influence, phenomenon forces, or entity, and turn it into an Strange Place which either makes servants for Anak'vog'soth, acts as a place of power for Abyssal Mystery Cults Initiations, or helps produce Relics which have Abyssal taint that empower Abyssal Mystery Cult Initiations.<br /> The Anak'vog'soth cannot do any of the above unless a beings with the sincere intension to make the item, place or person &quot;gone&quot; &quot;erased from existence&quot; or other similar sentiment, killing or destroying the person/place/thing with an extensive cover-up trying to erase them from existence, genuine supernaturally erased from time, or sequestered into a pocket realm in a way that also kills the person, or ruins the object or place. When or where of the mortals wish or whether it was spoken aloud doesn't matter, meaning the stricter criteria is the actual attempt to remove it from reality. The limitation for the location, person, item to sincerely be erased from reality is what keeps those who'd want to create abyssal intrusions into our world from invoking Anak'vog'soth's Transformation of the Obliterated Dread Power, and makes attempt to edit things from reality as an ultimate solution so dangerous.<br /> Finally, all magic of this sort comes with a steep price. When the Anak'vog'soth transforms the person into a Horror, the Horror has one less Aspiration than they could otherwise have, no longer have an Integrity or equivalent Advantage, and gain the Tainted [Persistent] Condition with a die pool equal to their Horror Potency. When the Anak'vog'soth transforms the an item into an Abyssal Relic, or a location into Abyssal Strange Place, the lead actor.<br /> <br /> <b>NIGHTMARE PLAGUE</b><br /> Anak'vog'soth is a font of nightmares, its presence a heavy weight in the world of dreams. Each night, anyone attempting to sleep within 10 miles of Anak'vog'soth must succeed at a Resolve + Composure roll or suffer debilitating nightmares, regaining no Willpower from rest and gaining the Paranoia Condition. If attempting dream-based travel, soothsaying, or similar supernatural power or gift during meditation or sleep and fails the previous Resolve + Composure roll also fail that which relied upon dreams or peaceful meditation even if it normally doesn't require a roll and gain the Soul Shocked Condition in addition to the Paraniod Condition. This excludes Abyssal Horrors, but not lesser Abyssal servants like cultists. For those unable to get back to their bodies they may attempt again the next night.<br /> <br /> <b>ABSENCE OF TIME</b> (By <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\">amechra</a>)[modified for this Horror]<br /> Anak'vog'soth is always considered to be an invalid target for Supernal magic belonging to the Time Arcana. In addition, any spell of that Arcana that interacts (even indirectly) with the Anak'vog'soth unravels as if exposed to 10 successes on a Dissonance roll. Additionally supernatural powers which look into or affect the future or past of Anak'vog'soth also treat Anak'vog'soth as an invalid target.<br /> <br /> <b>ABSENCE OF SPACE</b> (By <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\">amechra</a>)[modified for this Horror]<br /> Anak'vog'soth, and the space in which even a single of its tendrils are in, are always considered to be an invalid target for Supernal magic belonging to the Space Arcana. In addition, any spell of that Arcana that interacts (even indirectly) with the Anak'vog'soth unravels as if exposed to 10 successes on a Dissonance roll. Additionally supernatural powers which scry upon, affect via sympathy, or remotely also treat Anak'vog'soth as an invalid target.<br /> <br /> <b>DISCORPORATE</b><br /> If Anak'vog'soth suffers damage that would kill it in a way that'd invoke it's Bane (or even if it merely wants to escape the scene), it may discorporate: its body dissolves into a huge swarm of squirming tendril creatures about 100 meters in diameter(causing the Masses of Tendrils Environmental Tilt &lt;see below&gt; in that area), writhing in all directions, especially burrowing to scape. If the area under Anak'vog'soth is able to be burrowed through the Tilt resolves itself in a sound or two as the masses escape the screne. If even one escapes, the Anak'vog'soth survives. Anak'vog'soth may be able to reform in the next scene if much of its mass remains, or it might take an hour, a day, or even longer to pull itself back together as they reassemble or if needed, grow to full size.<br /> <br /> <b>Straggling Masses of Tendrils escaping tentacle masses from Anak'vog'soth upon its discorporation</b><br /> If slick gray masses of tentacles are isolated from the Masses of Tendrils Environmental Tilt they create<br /> <b>Best At:</b> 5 (Borrowing through concrete, stone, steel, or earth to escape; Damaging anything or one restraining them)<br /> <b>Worst At:</b> Chance Die (Non-Telepathic Communication,)<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Escape the threat to Anak'vog'soth's current Avatar<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 2<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 10<br /> <b>Durability:</b> 5<br /> <b>Size:</b> 1<br /> <b>Health:</b> 3<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> 3<br /> <b>BURROW</b><br /> Burrowing through earth and rock is easy for the these wriggling slick gray tentacle. It can tunnel through such materials at a speed equal to its Strength dots in yards per turn.<br /> <b>ABSENCE OF TIME</b> (By <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\">amechra</a>)<br /> Anak'vog'soth's escaping tentacle masses are always considered an invalid target for Supernal magic belonging to the Time Arcana. In addition, any spell of that Arcana that interacts (even indirectly) with the Anak'vog'soth unravels as if exposed to 10 successes on a Dissonance roll. Additionally supernatural powers which look into or affect the future or past of Anak'vog'soth also treat Anak'vog'soth as an invalid target.<br /> <br /> <b>ABSENCE OF SPACE</b> (By <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\">amechra</a>)<br /> Anak'vog'soth's escaping tentacle masses are always and the space in which even a single of its tendrils are in, are always considered an invalid target for Supernal magic belonging to the Space Arcana. In addition, any spell of that Arcana that interacts (even indirectly) with the Anak'vog'soth unravels as if exposed to 10 successes on a Dissonance roll. Additionally supernatural powers which scry upon, affect via sympathy, or remotely also treat Anak'vog'soth as an invalid target.<br /> <br /> <b>Masses of Tendrils</b><br /> The Straggling Masses of Tendrils Traits presented here work for when you need to focus in on an action scene involving<br /> a few characters and a modest number of Straggling Masses of Tendrils, but when you want to highlight the sheer, swarming mass of the aberrant tentacles creatures, they\u2019re not practical. This Tilt represents any area that\u2019s packed full of Masses of Tendrils.<br /> <b>Effects:</b> Characters moving through the Masses of Tendrils are slowed by the mindless, grasping tentacles and sheer press of slimy bodies. Within the area affected by the Tilt, characters lose their bonus to Speed (so normal humans have a Speed equal to Strength + Dexterity). Characters who move at anything less than full speed (that is, using an Instant action to run) are subject to an attack using the Masses of Tendril\u2019s best dice pool. An exceptional success on this attack inflicts the Knocked Down Tilt.<br /> In addition, the Masses of Tendrils are especially slimy and foul, moving through the area might require characters to make a reflexive Stamina + Composure roll every minute or suffer the moderate version of the Sick Tilt.<br /> <b>Causing the Tilt:</b> Any large group of mostly passive monsters could cause this Tilt.<br /> Ending the Tilt: The whole point of the Tilt is that it represents too many creatures to fight effectively, but characters might be able to draw the Horde off (maybe by firing guns or operating loud, heavy machinery elsewhere), or drive them back if the Horde suffers from a Bane (if your zombies are afraid of fire, for example, Molotov cocktails or simply carrying torches might disperse them).<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Please note this is an Abyssal Creature, for where that matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-17-2019, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T23:53:20-08:00","id":1274149,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:24px\">Hungry Doorway to Nowhere</span><br /> Ever have a sense of foreboding when looking at a pitch black threshold you couldn't see beyond? What is the worst that could beyond it? For those that have escaped one of these horrors they know the answer is nothing. People disappear, sometimes without a single trace, thousands of times every year. Even supernatural predators vanish mysteriously from their communities, and this creature is one of the causes for both types of disappearance. These creatures are the result of experimentation by vampires who've discovered a technique to infuse their curse of undeath into the consciousness of a self-aware supernatural site through &quot;killing&quot; the location, and then the application of the properties of their Vitae focused through specific Disciplines and arcane ritual. The resulting undead creature is not tethered to a physical location but instead feeds on those that parish within the hellish pocket realm it acts as a portal to. It exists as a doorway to a pocket realm filled with decaying, twisted versions of the sites it has abducted its prey, with only one escape built in.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Horror Type:</b> Minion<br /> <b>Best Dice Pool:</b> 5 (Stealthily setting in places to use Threshold of Darkness; Escaping through routes it can't be followed; Engulfing stragglers if not everyone in a group goes through the threshold it chose; Making sure it isn't exposed to its Banes)<br /> <b>Worst Dice Pool:</b> Chance Die (Preventing a since of foreboding to those that are situationally/supernaturally/psychically aware; acting while exposed to Fire Electricity, or Bright Light)<br /> <b>All Other Pools:</b> 2<br /> <b>Tags:</b> Undead, Abyssal Intrusion<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Have an Ephemeral Entity or being with a Soul die while within its associated Tumor of Nowhere Cells<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Engulf, Threshold of Darkness, Insubstantial<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Fire, Electricity, Extremely Bright Lights do a single Aggravated wound each round. Each month that goes by without an Ephemeral Entity or being with a Soul die within its associated Tumor of Nowhere Cells it takes an Aggravated Wound which can't be healed until some being does die.<br /> <b>Health:</b> 6<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 2<br /> <br /> <b>ENGULF</b><br /> The creature can be a snare that will entrap victims, an inky blackness that leads to a terrible imprisonment. By spending 1 Willpower, the creature expands to an area of up to 10 square yards, and can attempt to forcible use Threshold of Darkness Upon those caught within it victims in the area using the snare, using its own Best Dice Pool with a +3 bonus to the dice pool to grapple them. Those unaffected by the rapid expansion but that witness it or those that dodged the grapple are granted immunity to that particular Door to No Where's Engulf and Threshold of Darkness Dread Powers until the next Sunset.<br /> <br /> <b>THRESHOLD OF DARKNESS</b><br /> While the Hungry Door to No Where is entirely still after moving into place to cover a threshold of some sort while unseen by its potential victims, beings whom step through, climb through or descend through the creature willingly are valid targets for this ability and are automatically affect. Being spotted moving by a victim grants that particular being immune to the free use of the Threshold of Darkness Dread Power of Hungry Door to No Where until the sun sets the next day. Alternatively those that are successful caught within an expanding Engulf Dread Power and fail to dodge the grapple are also affect though for the cost of that power. Affected beings are deposited into an otherworld pocket, the immediate area of which is a dimly lit twisted parody of the location they were abducted from. If this power is used in roughly the same general vicinity then it deposits those affected into the same section of the otherworldly pocket realm. The <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places\">Strange Place</a> this Dread Power deposits those abducted is an instance of Tumor of Nowhere Cells distinct to the Hungry Doorway to Nowhere that used the power. Each time this Dread Power is used in a new location it creates a new room sized section of Tumor of Nowhere Cells known as a Cell. Each Cell is a rusted, rotten, twisted, accursedly condemned caricature of the room-sized material location those the being who passed through the Hungry Doorway To Nowhere from or were in when it used Engulf, and attempting to exit any of the room-sized Cells requires a Wits + Composure - 8 and if unsuccessful they re-enter the Cell from the point of egress after a moment, and if successful they instead enter another Cell within the Tumor of Nowhere Cells in a non-linear M. C. Escher painting style of spatially inconsistent connection which constantly shift between Cells, creating an insane maze. If the character has the Informed Condition about particular Hungry Doorway To Nowhere or its Tumor of Nowhere Cells, are successful in leaving a particular Cell they may choose criteria of the Cell they wish go to and if there is a Cell which matches the criteria then they and anyone in physical contact with them while exiting go into the Cell which matches their choice for the cost of resolving the Informed Condition. Tumors of Nowhere Cells only have a single innate point of egress which has prerequisites to leave. Any being which has all their health filled with aggravated damage or Ephemeral Entities reduced to zero corpus within the Tumor of Nowhere Cells have their bodies vanish leaving behind only clothing, things carried, dental fillings, or surgical implants as trace evidence. Those beings with Souls that die or Ephemeral entity vanishing upon losing all its corpus nourishes the Hungry Doorway To Nowhere; For this reason Doors to No Where take particular delight in capturing lethal supernatural predator (vampires in particular are a favorite denizen of darkness due to the Tumors of Nowhere Cells lacking Sunlight and all vampires only technically need a steady supply of victims) to kill the prey inside the the Tumor of Nowhere Cells. Doors to No Where are unable to enter these Tumors of Nowhere Cells, and only sense three things inside its Tumor of Nowhere Cells: deaths inside which feed it Willpower, writing done on surfaces which are not beings, and when beings escape.<br /> <br /> <b>INSUBSTANTIAL</b><br /> The creature fluid opaque completely non-reflective black shape, that is not solid. It doesn't even give physical resistance to those passing through it without using its Dread Power. The creature can flow down drains, under doors, through cracks, flows over surfaces regardless of gravity or traction, and fill roughly door sized area by clinging to the edges of the threshold. Both ephemeral and physical matter other than its Banes inflict no harm upon it.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">Tumor of Nowhere Cells</span><br /> There are many instances of these Strange Places. Each instances is discretely separate from every other and acts as the digestive chamber for the Hungry Doorways to Nowhere are a cluster of rooms-sized areas, each of which are morbidly disturbing decrepit nightmare reflections of the room or immediate vicinity of a material world location where the Hungry Doorway To Nowhere used its Threshold of Darkness Dread Power. When an entity or character first enters a Tumor of Nowhere Cells they enter the particular mockery of the location they were abducted from the threshold they attempted to leave the material version equivalent. Commonly for indoor locations paint is peeling, metal objects are both rusty and sharp, drywall falls away revealing sharp jagged rusty metal mesh are wood panels underneath filled with moist black mold rot, carpet or linoleum is gone revealing board which are weakened and have holes to be dangerous for a foot to go through or injure an ankle or knee tripping, and foul stains of murder and trace evidence horrific crimes litter as the how the location is different from the material location but noticeable as the same location by those not blind to the supernatural and are even mildly perceptive. Outdoor location reflected as cells are surrounded by a darkness which can't be penetrated by light when there aren't walls to block progress, even the sky above, the vegetation is dead thorny mockeries, and the area treats the expanses of preternatural darkness surrounding the area as thresholds of egress from that particular Cell, the same as indoor locations. Attempting to leave a particular cell through one of its means of inky black routes of egress means simply stepping back in from the same threshold a breath later, unless the person resists the effects of the Maze Environment of the Tumor of Nowhere Cells, and even if they are successful they merely enter another one of the Tumor's Cells. Each time a Hungry Doorway To Nowhere uses its Threshold of Darkness Dread Power from which beings enter from a new and distinct room-sized material world location it creates a new room-sized Cell to deposit those beings into, but if the Dread Power is used and there is already a Cell representing the location they are entering from then no new Cell is made and the beings are deposited into the Cell which that particular Hungry Doorway To Nowhere already made (even if it is occupied, but please note if two different Hungry Doorway To Nowhere makes Cell based a material location the Cells are just two copies of the same place because Tumors of Nowhere Cells are distinct and don't have overlapping cClls). Tumors of Nowhere Cells can grow quite large, being the functional volume of a city block of significantly tall multi-story apartment complexes, if the particular Hungry Doorway to Nowhere has survived a significant amount of time, but connections between Cells is non-linear and ever shifting and there is alway only one Gateway out, the vitae infused ornate door used to in the Vampire Devotion that turned the consciousness of an Awakened <a href=\"http://Strange Place\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Place</a> into a Hungry Doorway To Nowhere Horror and the door exists within the original area of the Tumor of Nowhere Cells, turned into an other worldly mockery of its original self with the Material World being filled in with solid matter and Vitae by the Vampire to turn a location into an object, symbolically killing it. The door in that location can only be opened by committing a murder or &quot;sacrifice&quot; of an Ephemeral or being with a Soul while directly in front of the ornate door within that original Cell and pleading to be released. Further details covered in the specific Environments.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Traits</b><br /> <br /> <b>Die Pool:</b> 13<br /> <b>Gauntlet:</b> This Strange Place is not cosmologically adjacent to the <i>Hisil</i><br /> <b>Potency:</b> 5<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> Strange Places don\u2019t have Willpower rating or Willpower points, instead it can spend a number of Willpower per scene equal to 1+ (Potency).<br /> <b>Environments:</b> Tumor of Nowhere Cells has 4<br /> <br /> <b>Otherworldly Domain:</b> Tumor of Nowhere Cells does not exist in the mortal world, and is located in a pocket realm isolated from the rest of reality. Tumors of Nowhere Cells are subject to distinct natural laws which are covered here or within the other Environments. First is there is no state of Twilight in this realm so Ephemeral beings are solid, visible and able to interact with the objects and other beings in the realm. Second is the realm has no access to the Hedge, the Primordial Dream, the Shadow, the Underworld, the Astral, and it is impossible to dream while within the realm or have similar inward mental journeys. This lack of dreaming sleep causes beings which need to dream to gain the Paranoid Condition after a number of missed nights of dreaming equal to greater than their Stamina. Third the realm is adjacent to only two places in a cosmological sense, the Darkness from which the Strix come hail and the Abyss (Since the Abyss by definition just beyond to everything that exists). Entering the realm is done via a particular Hungry Doorway To Nowhere's Threshold of Darkness Dread Power, the appropriate application of certain types of Miracle (or Equivalent) Dread Powers, appropriate applications of the Wishing Well Strange Place Environment, specially attuned Devotion called &quot;Go to Nowhere&quot;, or Surprise Entrance Dread Powers which don't rely upon access to the Hedge, the Primordial Dream, the Shadow, the Underworld, the Astral. Spacial Pockets made while within the domain merely count as another Cell being added to the Tumor, and is subject to the other environments as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Dilapidated:</b> The each Cell within a Tumor of Nowhwere Cells contains structures that are decayed, rusted, and are in stages of falling apart. All items and structures (even the walls) within the affected area have their Durability reduced by 2 to a minimum of 0. Characters that suffer a Dramatic Failure in the affected area suffer two points of bashing damage as they injure themselves on an element of the decaying structure (crumbling masonry, exposed rebar or jagged nails). This Environment is always active.<br /> <br /> <b>Maze:</b> The Strange Place is a disorienting mass of room sized areas with all means of leaving a particular room sized area (known as a Cell) an inky blackness which can't be seen though and attempts to leave a particular loop back upon themselves without difficult effort, and even if successful without gaining the Informed the best those trapped can hope for is merely end up in another random Cell which represents another site where the Hungry Doorway To Nowhere abducted someone or something else. Each Cell is a rusted, rotten, twisted, accursedly condemned caricature of the room-sized material location those the being who passed through the Hungry Doorway To Nowhere from or were in when it used Engulf, and attempting to exit any of the room-sized Cells requires a Wits + Composure - 8 and if unsuccessful they re-enter the Cell from the point of egress after a moment, and if successful they instead enter another Cell within the Tumor of Nowhere Cells in a non-linear M. C. Escher painting style of spatially inconsistent connection which constantly shift between Cells, creating an insane maze. If the character gets an exceptional success moving between the Cell they will enter will contain a Clue about the history and how to escape the Tumor of Nowhere Cells that may be uncovered, and for the cost of 3 such Clues they figure out the conditions to leave and also gains the Informed Condition about the particular Tumor of Nowhwere Cells. If the character has the Informed Condition about particular Hungry Doorway To Nowhere or its Tumor of Nowhere Cells, are successful in leaving a particular Cell they may choose criteria of the Cell they wish go to and if there is a Cell which matches the criteria then they and anyone in physical contact with them while exiting go into the Cell which matches their choice for the cost of resolving the Informed Condition. Tumors of Nowhere Cells only have a single innate point of egress which has prerequisites to leave. Any being which has all their health filled with aggravated damage or Ephemeral Entities reduced to zero corpus within the Tumor of Nowhere Cells have their bodies vanish leaving behind only clothing, things carried, dental fillings, or surgical implants as trace evidence. Those beings with Souls that die or Ephemeral entity vanishing upon losing all its corpus nourishes the Hungry Doorway To Nowhere; For this reason Doors to No Where take particular delight in capturing lethal supernatural predator (vampires in particular are a favorite denizen of darkness due to the Tumors of Nowhere Cells lacking Sunlight and all vampires only technically need a steady supply of victims) to kill the prey inside the the Tumor of Nowhere Cells. Doors to No Where are unable to enter these Tumors of Nowhere Cells, and only sense three things inside its Tumor of Nowhere Cells: deaths inside which feed it Willpower, writing done on surfaces which are not beings, and when beings escape. This Environment is always active.<br /> <br /> <b>Gateway:</b> This particular type of Strange Place always contains a single a portal back to the material realm. With only a single exist point, and that the gate is always in the Cell which represents the Strange Place which was filled in to create the Hungry Doorway To Nowhere and unlike other Cells can be as small as a room or as large as a whole city block of Sewer system. Opening the exit Gateway requires a specific action to be performed, sacrificing an Ephemeral Entity, or murdering a being with a Soul (Diablerie doesn't count because it doesn't release the soul) for each character to be released in front of the ornate false door which sealed this location's fate while pleading to be let out. Within the Cell the false door appears in the location in the Cell which Corresponds to where it was placed to lead in at the the Devotion use. The site doesn't even need to exist anymore in the physical world because exiting Tumor of Nowhere Cells always leads to an unobserved swinging door hidden in darkness in any city the Hungry Doorway To Nowhere has collected Cells from, chosen instinctive by the character exiting.<br /> <br /> <b>Weirdness:</b> The Hungry Doorway To Nowhwere can automatically sense writing upon any material surface within the Tumor of Nowhere Cells and can cause writing to appear writing to appear on surfaces as well, in blood stains, creping rust, ink, pencil, or even as scratches if the material is walls, furniture, or floors. When a character chooses to actively interact with this Environment, the Hungry Doorway To Nowhere can roll its Dice Pool of 8, resisted by the characters Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance Trait. If the character is successful, the character gains the Spooked Condition until the end of the scene, but if the Hungry Doorway is successful the character gain Shaken, unless they already are in which case they gain Paranoid Condition, unless they aleady have that too at which point they gain the Obsession Condition about killing other in order to escape. This Environment is always active.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>PARANOID (From W:tF)</b><br /> Your character has been reduced to a state of rampant paranoia. She jumps at shadows, sees threats everywhere, and finds it hard to trust. She suffers a \u20132 penalty to Perception rolls, Social actions, and dice pools to draw upon the Allies, Contacts, Mentor, Retainer, Staff, and Status Merits.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Some Gifts.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> A week without any threat actually manifesting; a friend or ally achieving an exceptional success on a Social action to convince you of their trustworthiness.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> n/a<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">Vampire Devotions</span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">Go to Nowhere</span><br /> Protean \u2022<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Vitae<br /> <b>Requirement:</b> Must use this power in a material world location which corresponds to a Cell in a Tumor of Nowhere Cells which belongs to a Hungry Doorway To Nowhere which you have a relationship expressed in terms of Merits (Such as Mentor, Retainer)<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> You appear to meld into a surface of the location but instead of actually merging with physical materials at that location you instead rise up within the Tumor of Nowhere Cells which belongs to the Doorway To Nowhere you have the relationship with in the Cell which corresponds to the physical location where you used this Devotion. Once inside you are bound by the same rules which applies to others within this otherworldly domain, ranging from the lack of day or night, non-linear constantly shift inward looping nature of traversing the Tumor, and limited means of Egress. However no amount of excavation in the material world could location you.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">Embrace the Genuis Loci</span><br /> Obfuscate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Animalism \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Protean \u2022, Voivode Scale: Mass Embrace<br /> There are many members of Ordo Dracul whom develop a remarkably keen curiosity about supernatural sites, known as &quot;wyrm nests&quot; among those in the field. Even those with only minor knowledge in the field will have heard rumors of what the Romans called Genius Loci, which are self-aware locations, which raises interesting questions like what properties of Vitae can be applied to such places, are they subject to the Blood Bond, can they be Ghouled, <i>could it be possible to</i> Embrace <i>them</i>? This Devotion is the result of a particularly obsessed Ordo Dracul who found a way to inflict an undead transformation upon the consciousness and infecting with decay, hunger, and darkness. The transformation involves filling in the space of the location with solid material n while infusing it with the Vampire's entire full Blood Pool worth of spilled Vitae, turning a location into an object, which mimics the process of death turning living being into an object, then within the same night installing a specially designed and crafted false door where the primary entrance of the location once stood and the Vampire focusing their Vitae (including the entirety of their whole full Blood Pool again) into the doorway through a mixture of the Disciplines and Arcane principles of the Scale of the Dragon.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> Entire full Vitae pool spilled twice, once during the last stage of physically filling in the location with solid material, and then when sealing the specially prepared false door to the location in a mockery of putting Vitae in a Childer's mouth.<br /> <b>Requirement:</b> Must be used on a Strange Place with the Awakened Environment, which is filled in with solid material and a specially designed ornate false door with occult glyphs and symbols etched around base relief depictions of the site before it was filled in with macabre skeletal scenes portraying an important moment in the site's history history installed over where the site once was entered from before being filled in<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Resolve + Occult + Animalism<br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended<br /> Physically filling in a location which is self-aware and may have an array of powers or supernatural hazards to wield against assailants is both logistically challenging and potentially risky, but for a vampire that is able to successfully use this Devotion, by paying the costs, meeting the requirements they create a Hungry Doorway To Nowhere, with its first Cell in its Tumor of Nowhere Cells a twisted version of the space the vampire filled in and added the false door to. Transforming a sentient magical location in this way has similar advantages to Embracing a mortal, it creates another undead being whom the vampire understands better than most, gives the vampire the chance to shape the useful beings views on undeath, and affords the vampire an opportunity to forge symbiotic predatory alliances with the being which is now free to move. The diligent research needed to have the false door properly created to represent a death tainted version of a moment of the location, and the familiarity akin to Blood Ties, due to the perverting the process Embracing to apply to a location, allows the vampire which used this Devotion to gain the Informed Condition about the Hungry Doorway To Nowhere and/or its Tumor of Nowhere Cells with a reflexive Wits + Composure check while perceiving either. This strange Embrace-like status even affords vampires a solitary step removed from the vampire which used this Devotion to sense a familiarness they can recognize the relation similar to Blood Ties with a reflexive successful Wits + Composure check, which they may further investigate with a follow-up successful Instant Action Wits + Composure check to also gain the Informed Condition but must also pay a Vitae for them to resolve the condition due to their weaker connection.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 12-13-2018, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T22:55:18-08:00","id":1274838,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:24px\">Kyle Owen</span><br /> Kyle's mother died in childbirth and he was raised by his father, Arthur Owen, a former Marine turned security guard. Kyle's father was Military Police, and had friends in the police force whom he served with in the Marines. Due to partial disability was why Kyle's father ended up doing security instead of regular police work. Unfortunately security guards sometimes get in the way of a Uratha pack's Sacred Hunt, and for careless packs whom disregard the purpose behind &quot;The herd must not know&quot; that's often a death sentence, as it was in this particular case. Arthur was a strong willed man, not prone to cowardice, but even a brave man is still merely a man, and was easily rent asunder into bloody bits by inhuman clawed hands. The police, whom were Kyle's fathers friends found a scene of carnage which couldn't be squared in a sane world view free of monsters, and though the two officers, the blood splatter expert, and the medical examiner were convince of the truth, they dared not even hint of it in the reports they wrote for fear of losing all credibility. Arthur was cremated with no view of the body possible due to how he had been killed. Kyle was started to spiral out of control after his father's death and ran afoul with his father's officer friends whom directly investigated the scene. By that time that happened the officers had already formed a hunter cell and was piecing together what could about those who were responsible, and out of compassion told Kyle to the truth, which at first he didn't accept. It wasn't until they sat him down and forced him to see all the evidence they'd collected, including photographs of his father looked like when he was found, which gave Kyle's life meaning and direction once again.<br /> The officers didn't mean to harm Kyle, they believed he needed to know the truth and be able to face the things that took his father in order to cope. It broke him though it seemed at the time to save him. It crystallized his suicidal death wish after his father's death into a martyr complex. He became willing to die to destroy the monster and all their ilk which took his father from him. It was this death wish dressed up in honorable noble gallantry that attracted the attention of a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1269755#post1269755\">predator, a being which preys on the aspirations of mortal to make monsters</a>, and Kyle's aspiration of &quot;Give my life to defend &lt;Insert town here&gt; against werewolves&quot; was perfect to turn Kyle into one.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Martyrdom <b>Vice:</b> Vengeful<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Devour souls to ease void, Kill werewolves<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 5<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2, Computer 1, Crafts 2, Investigation 1, Medicine 1, Science 1, Politics 2, Athletics 2, FireArms 1, Stealth 1, Weaponry 1, Animal Ken 1, Empathy 4, Expression 2, Persuasion 3, Socialize 2, Street Wise 1(Urban Legends), Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Mystery Cult Initiation 4 (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1188352#post1188352\">Cult of the Yonder</a>), Mystery Cult Initiation 2 (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/799082-cofd-diy-mystery-cults?p=1173136#post1173136\">The Union</a>), Iron Will 3, Allies 1 (Network 0), Allies 1 (The local Police)<br /> <b>Merits from Mystery Cult Initiations:</b> Astral Adept 3, Familiar (Kyle's ) 2, Dream 1, Allies 1 (The Union)<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 5<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Integrity</b> 5<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Takes an Aggravated wound each day there are no werewolves within &lt;Insert Town Here&gt;, which he can't heal until a werewolf comes within the city limits of &lt;insert aforementioned town&gt;.<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Leaving &lt;aforementioned town&gt; causes Kyle to immediately die, but in a way that allows his Immortally to immediately reform him in &lt;aforementioned town&gt;<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> <b>Crossbow</b> with bolts covered in his blood<br /> [+2L Ranged 40/80/160; 4 dice Moderate Poisoned which acts as Silver] (With him when uses Surprise Entrance or Immortal to enter a Scene)<br /> <b>Very big silver-plated bowie knife</b> also coated in his blood<br /> [+2L Melee; 3 dice Moderate Poisoned which acts as Silver, and counts as silver itself] (With him when uses Surprise Entrance or Immortal to enter a Scene)<br /> <br /> <b>VENOMOUS ICHOR</b><br /> Kyle\u2019s blood and flesh is poisonous. Specifically his blood appears to be a metallic silver ichor. Anyone biting Kyle suffers the moderate Poisoned Tilt. Kyle\u2019s blood can be used to taint, food, drink or surfaces, making consuming the tainted substance inflict the grave Poisoned Tilt; surfaces smeared with the blood inflict the moderate Tilt if touched within an hour. Also the damage inflicted by these tilts are Silver based for purposes of Banes.<br /> <br /> <b>IMMORTAL</b><br /> Kyle isn\u2019t bound by mortal laws of life and death. He\u2019s not indestructible, per se, but if he\u2019s killed by anything other than his Bane, he just comes back in a later scene like nothing happened, having reformed elsewhere in the town. When killed he, his clothing, and his equipment dissolve into the Venomous Ichor which make up his blood. Even if he\u2019s destroyed with his Bane, he\u2019s never really gone \u2014 Uratha within the city limits of &lt;insert aforementioned town&gt; while the full moon is visible in the sky above the town will always resurrect the Kyle and bring him back for a sequel story.<br /> <br /> <b>SURPRISE ENTRANCE</b><br /> No matter how secure Kyle's victims think they are, by spending 1 Willpower Kyle may suddenly appear in the scene which contains Uratha and is inside the city limits of &lt;insert aforementioned town&gt;, even the Hisil. He does this by manifesting out of the nothingness beyond reality. Any character witnessing this entrance must succeed on a reflexive Resolve + Composure roll or gain the Shaken Condition.<br /> If the characters have actively taken appropriate measures to keep the Kyle out (powerful magic warding against such things, Spiritual Influence creating Wards or supernatural Barriers) it will take Kyle one full turn to break through, giving the characters time to react. If not, Kyle\u2019s just there as a reflexive action and can take one more action before anyone can react.<br /> <br /> <b>SOUL THIEF</b><br /> Kyle is capable of stealing souls from werewolves, and he does so for sustenance, the soul being immediate obliterated upon its theft. The restriction or condition that must fulfill to steal a soul is that the werewolf must be responsible for killing Kyle, whether it is with its own tooth or claw, a bullet from a rifle, a trap the werewolf set, or even as indirect as the werewolf convincing a group of people to convince another group of people to kill Kyle. Once the restriction is met, Kyle may spend 3 Willpower and roll Resolve + Empathy, contested by the victim\u2019s Resolve + Primal Urge. Kyle may only make this check once per day per werewolf. Note Kyle can feel each werewolf whose responsible for his death because of this power, and dying in order to inflict harm on werewolves fulfills Kyle's Virtue of Martyrdom, so he'll try to steal their souls until successful. If Kyle succeeds, it steals the victim\u2019s soul and inflicts the Soulless Condition, and that clears the victim of one particular incident of killing Kyle. The victim's soul is gone forever making clinging to the Flesh impossible, but can be remedied by acquiring a human soul from a spirit or different Horror with the ability to steal souls. If the werewolf does acquire a soul in this way then they subject to this power again if their murders of Kyle out number the times they have had their Soul removed.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Kyle's Martyrdom</b> (Rank 1 Acamoth)<br /> A floating bloodless version of Kyle with bullet holes, knifewounds, its limbs and bite sized chunks dangling free of gravity's influence and attached by veins and arteries.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Power:</b> 3<br /> <b>Finesse:</b> 1<br /> <b>Resistance:</b> 4<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Twilight Form, Familiar<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Martyrdom 1<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Echoing Intent, Implant Mission, Dement<br /> <b>Ban:</b> All missions it implants must be that of self-sacrifice.<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 11<br /> [B]Defense: 4<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 5<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 5<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 10/<br /> <br /> <b>Echoing Intent</b> by <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime\">Teatime</a><br /> Under the right circumstances, like in the event of its destruction, the Entity may instead spend a dot of Resistance for the following effect to occur: All present witnesses become unable to perceive or directly affect it. All mundane rolls fail outright and it becomes immune to all of their Spells. The entity likewise becomes unable to affect them or even alter the environment in their presence, with the exception of communicating with others. It also can't acknowledge their existence outside of their presence, but otherwise has full access to its powers. Each use of this effect is permanent. On the bright side, you can trap the entity in a room by locking the door and guarding it. Of course, you would need someone else to confirm if you succeeded.\u200b<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 12-17-2018, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T00:12:31-08:00","id":1275244,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:24px\">Elf on a Shelf</span><br /> Some of these trendy little holiday toys were not mass produced from cheap materials in soulless factories to slate the avarice of a consumer culture. Some of these toys come from a magical place which borders both Aether and Arcadia, with the Northern lights of the aurora dance across the sky, while heavenly choirs of angels triumphantly sing carols about the glorious birth of the son of God, while icy cold winds blow snowflakes by windows to workshops where diligent elves labor away to create the Fated rewards for good little boys and girls whom believe. Christmas and Christianity are full of Supernal symbolism, those symbols carry Power and more Truth than anything in the Fallen World. Were these things always True? Was Jesus and Saint Nicolas Archmages whose ascensions created more cosmic Truth? <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/NoSuchThingAsWizardJesus\" target=\"_blank\">Might Jesus be the Hieromage, who'll come again as foretold</a>*? That's all highly debatable and quite controversial topics as faith and religion can be, but Christmas symbols and other elements of Christianity carry Supernal Truth and Power. While the core of Elf on a Shelf is a Lie and a middle aged Southern woman's clever cash grab by contriving a counterfeit Holiday Tradition spun from the oppressive strands of the selfish parental desire for compliant obedience woven with fearful docility squeezed from children subjected to panoptic paranoia of constant surveillance, a kernel of Supernal Truth was able to take root. The sweet desire of children to be seen as good and worthy of praise was the real Christmas magic this cynical merchandising scheme sparked in some cases. Those Elf on a Shelf which were not given as gifts, ordered online, or bought at a store, the ones that came down from the Supernal Realms into this Fallen World to make it just a bit better are not Ephemeral Entities and not quite Artifacts, but instead follow these mechanics:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Horror Type:</b> Minion<br /> <b>Best Dice Pool:</b> 5 (Judging which Christmas Miracle is worthy of fulfilling; Insight in cultivating the essence of Christmas; Being in unexpected places)<br /> <b>Worst Dice Pool:</b> Chance Die (Avoiding invoking paranoia, holding any precarious pose without tipping over)<br /> <b>All Other Pools:</b> 2<br /> <b>Tags:</b> Supernal, Construct<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Making the world a more moral and compassionate place, Judge the naughty from the nice<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Surprise Entrance, Know if Naughty or Nice, Christmas Miracle<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Unable to use their magic to harm humans; May only Exist in the Fallen World from American Thanksgiving to sunset on Christmas Eve day (Uses Surprise Entrance to go back to Santa's Workshop<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Being in a location with a Paradox Environmental Tilt inflict 1 Aggravated Wound per Turn; Being Touched by a Entity or Being with a Paradox Condition or has the Abyssal Tag inflict 1 Aggravated Wound Per Turn<br /> <b>Size:</b> 1<br /> <b>Health:</b> 3<br /> <b>Willpower/Scene:</b> 2<br /> <br /> <b>SURPRISE ENTRANCE</b><br /> Each Elf-on-a-Shelf is an inanimate doll which doesn't move, yet no matter how secure its victims think they are, by spending 1 Willpower an Elf-on-a-Shelf may suddenly appear in the scene in whatever pose suits the Elf. It simply blinks out of existence at one location and appears at another when &quot;unobserved&quot;. Any character attempting to witness this egress or entrance must succeed on a reflexive Resolve + Composure roll or gain the Shaken Condition when the Elf-on-a-Shelf appears in a split momentary break in observation enforced by Fate.<br /> If the characters have actively taken appropriate measures to keep the Horror out (such as actively observing the Elf at its point of egress or entrance) it will take the creature one full turn to have a contrivance of Fate to enforce the momentary break of observation, giving the characters time to react. If not, it\u2019s just there as a reflexive action and can take one more action before anyone can react.<br /> <br /> <b>KNOW IF YOU'RE NAUGHTY OR NICE</b><br /> The creature can see into the depths of its victim\u2019s soul. By spending 1 Willpower, it automatically learns the victim\u2019s Virtue, Vice, Aspirations, and current Integrity. By spending an additional Willpower point, it learns the circumstances of the character\u2019s most severe breaking point check. This power also lets the Elf on a Shelf know if the victim has written a letter to Santa Claus and if so what any such letter would have. If the creature uses its knowledge against the victim, it earns an exceptional success on a roll of three successes or more.<br /> <br /> <b>CHRISTMAS MIRACLE</b><br /> An Elf-on-a-Shelf is capable of performing miraculous feats at the request of humans. Miracles include, but aren\u2019t necessarily<br /> limited to:<br /> \u2022 Removing (or applying) any Condition or Tilt (or similar affliction not modeled by these mechanics).<br /> \u2022 Granting any Merit, Skill, or Attribute at 5 dots.<br /> \u2022 Fulfilling an Aspiration of the victim.<br /> The Elf-on-a-Shelf cannot do any of these things unless explicitly a living human being with Integrity 8 or higher writes a letter to Santa Claus, and that letter must also reflect the Aspiration which will be fulfilled by the Christmas Miracle. The activation of this Dread Power can take place at any time between Thanksgiving and sunset on Christmas Eve day, but the fulfillment always takes place on December 25th in the future. A particular person may only receive a Christmas Miracle from an Elf-on-a-Shelf once in their existence, even if they encounter different Elf-on-a-Shelf later.<br /> Finally, all magic of this sort comes with a price. When the Elf-on-a-Shelf grants a victim\u2019s wish, the victim\u2019s Aspiration which was fulfilled is Permanently Replaced. The Aspiration which permanently replaces the one that was fulfilled is &quot;Honor Christmas in my heart, and try to keep compassionate Christian goodness all the year round.&quot; The character will never be able to replace that Aspiration, but it can be lost to Dread Power or Environments which consume Aspirations. The victim is also considered to have the Open condition for Christmas Cheer Geotia (but not Spirits) each December until the Aspiration is lost.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> *Subversion of Linked Trope <div align=\"center\"><b><i>\u200b<span style=\"font-size:28px\">Merry Christmas All<br /> and<br /> God Bless Us,<br /> Everyone!</span></i></b></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 12-19-2018, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T04:50:39-08:00","id":1275264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1275244#post1275244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\">Elf on a Shelf</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think the intersection of Christianity, Christmas, and the Supernal is odd here. Supernal Aether and Angels aren't explicitly Christian (though they aren't explicitly <i>not</i> either). Christmas also has older roots that aren't quite being addressed, yet seem to be referenced, leaving the whole thing confusing.<br /> <br /> As to the Dread Powers, they seem highly specific for new ones - could similar be achieved by just adding flavor and restrictions to Know Soul and Miracle? (Also, Integrity isn't Morality, so the 8+ restriction on Miracle seems off).<br /> <br /> I do wonder how these could be recast in other game lines, or as a more mysterious-origin generic Horror. I can see a Changeling, Mummy, Werewolf, and maybe Demon instances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"